WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.204
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.872
we wanted to find out
the biggest differences

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.974
between the UK and US McDonald's.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.682
This is what a small drink
looks like in the UK.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.351
Joe Avella: This is a US small.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.020
Harry: This is what a
medium drink looks like.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.622
Joe: This is a US medium.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.391
Harry: And this is a large.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:28.261
Joe: [grunts] And this is a US large.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.200
Harry: So, with our McNuggets in the UK,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.870
the default adult sizes on the menu

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.005
are a box of six,

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.140
a box of nine,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.008
or a share box of 20.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:46.312
Joe: Nuggets. You can get a box of four,

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.248
or you can get a six piece,

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.984
or 10.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:53.253
20, for "sharing."

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:57.057
Or...ahh.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.392
40.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.327
And according to the three
McDonald's in the area,

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.363
they don't have 20 or 40 boxes,

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.632
they just do them in increments of 10,

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.801
but this is on the menu.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:12.305
Harry: In the UK, we got
three sizes of fries.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.873
These are our small
fries in the paper bag.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.775
Joe: Here is the small fry.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.445
Harry: These are our medium
fries in the iconic carton.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.846
Joe: Here is the medium fry.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.047
Harry: And then these are our large fries.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.850
Joe: And here is the large fry.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.753
Harry: So, we couldn't find
the exact weight measurement

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.887
for these fries online,

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.723
so what we're gonna do
is weigh them ourselves.

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:43.169
Just out of curiosity,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.338
gonna bring our trusty
friend, the scales, back,

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.372
and we're gonna weigh the Big Mac

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.174
and see if there is
any difference in size.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.276
I'm not sure there will
be, but let's find out.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.655
Joe: Hang on, hang on, hang on.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.137
Harry: So, while McDonald's
fries might look and taste

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.938
pretty similar in the UK and the US,

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.940
in the UK we only have three ingredients,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.042
which is oil, salt, and potatoes.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.046
Joe: The McDonald's
french fries in America

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.314
have way more ingredients.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.983
These fries are made
from potatoes, obviously;

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.019
a vegetable oil, which
has canola oil, corn oil,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:36.556
soybean oil, hydrogeni...

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:39.025
hydrogenitated...genitated?

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.326
Producer: Hydrogenated.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.694
Joe: Ha! Thank you.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:45.365
Hydrogenated soybean
oil, natural beef flavor,

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:48.001
dextrose, sodium aspid...phosphitate?

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:51.938
Phosphifi...phos...phiupp...pyrophosphate,

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:55.608
pyrophosphate, sodium acid pyrophosphate,

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.844
which is used to maintain the color.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.078
Are they that much of a different

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.380
color than the ones in the UK?

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.281
Is it worth it?

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:02.482
Can we get a side-by-side comparison?

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:03.716
Are they that much more bright yellow

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.686
we need to put sodium acid pyrophosphate

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.321
or whatever it's called in it?

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:11.724
Salt, and I should mention
that a natural beef flavor

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:14.827
contains hydrolyzed
wheat and hydrolyzed milk

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:17.630
as a starting ingredient, and of course

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.399
I have no idea what that means.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:21.167
Harry: So, the biggest calorie
difference in a Big Mac

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.368
actually comes from the sauce.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.536
In the US they've got about

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.772
40 more calories than we do in the UK.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:28.174
We're not sure if this is
because there's more sauce

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.176
or because the ingredients list in the UK

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.378
is just a little bit more simple.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:37.083
Joe: Our sauce is made of soybean oil,

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.686
sweet relish, which is
made of diced pickles,

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.487
sugar, high-fructose corn syrup,

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.590
distilled vinegar, salt, corn syrup,

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.491
all right, two types of corn syrup,

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.260
xanthan gum,

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.361
hang on.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:54.167
Calcium chloride, spice extractives?

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.735
Water. All right, I've heard of that.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.604
Egg yolks, distilled vinegar,

00:03:57.604 --> 00:04:00.273
spices, onion powder, salt,

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.976
propylene glycol alginate?

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.744
Garlic powder; vegetable protein,

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.780
which has hydrolyzed corn, soy, and wheat;

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.483
sugar; caramel color; turmeric;

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.386
extractives of paprika; and, of course,

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:16.389
soy...lechithen.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.824
Leechithen.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:19.626
Lecithin.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.261
I don't know which one it is.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.395
Harry: So, if you are
trying to eat healthily

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.997
at McDonald's, it might actually be

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.965
the drinks that you have to look out for.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.404
Joe: That's nothing, guys.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:35.942
Our chocolate shake? 840 calories.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.710
That's as many calories as

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:41.047
two cheeseburgers and one hamburger.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.248
Harry: So, what does that all mean?

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.950
If you were to walk into a UK McDonald's

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.919
and order yourself a large
Big Mac meal with a milkshake,

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.555
it would be around 1,400 calories.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.658
Joe: And if you were to
get the large Big Mac meal

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.426
with a chocolate shake in America,

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:57.630
the total here is 1,870 calories.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:00.199
So that's 1,870 calories,

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:04.170
the daily calorie allowance
for an American dude

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.239
is 2,500, OK.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:09.242
So you have 630 left.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:12.078
One McNugget is 55 calories, right?

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:14.914
So you could also have 11 more nuggets,

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.784
and there you go, that's
all you need for the day.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.023
Harry: Here's everything you can only get

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.725
at a UK McDonald's.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.794
So, here we've got the
Veggie Deluxe burger,

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:29.762
which is a veggie burger that's served

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.397
with some mayo and some lettuce.

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:34.500
Here we've got a Chicken Legend,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.269
which is a chicken burger,

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:38.271
again served with mayo and lettuce.

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:40.073
Joe: Chicken Legend, I don't
even know what that is.

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:42.575
Not gonna catch on.
That can stay in the UK.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.444
Harry: We have a range of wraps
that you can get in the UK.

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:45.611
We have a wrap of the day.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:48.581
Here we've got the fajita
crisp, which is some chicken,

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:51.617
along with some veg and
some spicy fajita sauce.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.186
Here we've got some Veggie Dippers.

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:55.254
These were actually introduced
at part of Veganuary

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.523
in 2020 in the UK, but
they're stuck on the menu.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.625
So, these are Vegan Society-approved,

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:02.929
and they're sort of like a
fried-bean-patty sort of thing.

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.897
Joe: [sighs] Like, pick a more

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:08.034
unappetizing thing to get at McDonald's.

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:09.469
Veggie Dippers.

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:11.738
Harry: And then finally we've
got some Mozzarella Dippers,

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:14.207
which are just kind of
mozzarella sticks, really.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:18.177
Joe: Well, sucks to be in the UK,

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:22.815
'cause everything you see
right here is USA only, baby.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:25.485
Haha, USA only!

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:30.022
So, I'm gonna talk about
the coffee drinks real fast.

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.658
Here in the US, we have
all the same coffee drinks

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.627
they do in the UK, but every coffee drink

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:38.364
has an iced version and also a caramel

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:40.633
and/or French vanilla
and/or mocha version,

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.567
depending on what you're getting.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:45.471
So, we in the US, of
course, have more variety.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.573
Shamrock Shake.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.908
The Shamrock Shake is, like,

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.644
it's like vanilla and mint shake.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:53.246
Strawberry Sundae.

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:56.182
This has recently been
discontinued in the UK.

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:57.116
Sorry, guys.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.684
Still got it in the US.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:02.121
My favorite as a kid, the Caramel Sundae.

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.390
Fruit and Yogurt Parfait,
maybe it's healthy,

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.392
I have no idea, probably not.

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:08.928
Those were the cold items I
wanted to get out of the way

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.230
as they slowly melt under these lights.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.900
Got a lot more to go through.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.736
Harry, bear with me here, buddy.

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:19.138
Buttermilk Crispy Chicken Sandwich.

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.940
Yo, I think this was introduced

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.642
when the chicken-sandwich
wars were really heating up

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:24.243
when Chick-fil-A started taking over.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.845
Let's see what's under the hood.

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:29.482
Look at that. Look at this.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:33.186
Quarter Pounder with Cheese Deluxe.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:35.488
This is your fancy Quarter
Pounder with Cheese.

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:39.592
This is for Sunday dinner.
When you have company over.

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:41.127
Ah, there's so much.

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:43.029
Sausage Breakfast Burrito.

00:07:43.029 --> 00:07:44.530
Even after it's, for a while, it's, like,

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:48.301
still, like, glowing yellow. [laughs]

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:53.940
Now, these are the Buttermilk
Crispy Chicken Tenders.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:57.643
These smell amazing. I wanna
just bite into these so bad.

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:59.846
I wanna just take a big bite.

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:01.614
Wanna talk about sauces real quick.

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:04.750
OK, I'm at McDonald's, and I
go get me one of everything.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.220
I've heard from Harry and
the team over in the UK

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.554
that some of these they don't have,

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:11.090
including sweet 'n sour, honey mustard,

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.291
what else don't you guys have?

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:14.994
I don't think you guys have
ranch either, or buffalo.

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:17.563
I gotta say, though, the
sauces are everything.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:19.499
Harry: We've got a couple of sauces that

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:20.900
are kind of unique to the UK as well.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.569
We've got a sweet curry dipping sauce,

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:25.571
and then we've also got
a salsa dip as well,

00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:27.740
which I didn't know existed until today.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.243
Joe: Oh, yes, Donut Sticks.

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:34.747
These Donut Sticks also come
with a chocolate dipping sauce.

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:37.216
Another thing I'm certain
they don't have in the UK.

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:39.719
Yo ho ho ho ho ho ho!

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:42.355
Breakfast is served!

00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:44.490
Look at this. Oh, yeah.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.792
Who's ready to start the day?

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:48.494
[claps] It's McGriddle talk.

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:51.497
[audience applause]
[jazzy music]

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:00.940
So, for those of you in the UK

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.942
who don't know what a McGriddle is,

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:06.045
the United States McDonald's
had this genius idea:

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:07.880
What if we took breakfast sandwiches,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.315
replaced the buns,

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:12.618
and made them pancakes
and somehow injected

00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:14.820
some sort of syrup
flavor into the pancakes?

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.022
And the McGriddle was born.

00:09:16.022 --> 00:09:18.391
And, I have to say, they're fantastic.

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:21.928
This one right here, the bacon,
egg, and cheese McGriddle.

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:26.666
This is the sausage.

00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:31.837
Yeah? Hi!

00:09:31.837 --> 00:09:34.473
Hey, hey.

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:38.778
This is the sausage, egg,
and cheese McGriddle.

00:09:38.778 --> 00:09:41.614
American food engineering at its finest.

00:09:41.614 --> 00:09:42.481
Look at that.

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:46.719
In the UK, you guys call
biscuits cookies. Here...no.

00:09:46.719 --> 00:09:50.556
So, in the UK, biscuits are cookies,

00:09:50.556 --> 00:09:51.924
what we call cookies.

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:55.494
In the US, biscuits are what we call...

00:09:55.494 --> 00:09:56.796
uh...

00:09:56.796 --> 00:09:58.598
I don't know what else you can call them.

00:09:58.598 --> 00:10:01.767
Like, you bake them, and
they're from the South,

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.736
and they're dry, and I
don't know what they are.

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:05.438
Much like the McGriddles,

00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:07.673
we have a version of
every breakfast sandwich

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:11.444
that instead of the regular
bun bread, it's biscuits.

00:10:11.444 --> 00:10:14.747
Not the cookie biscuits
like you guys have.

00:10:14.747 --> 00:10:16.449
These biscuits.

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:17.984
Harry: Joe, you were so close on the whole

00:10:17.984 --> 00:10:19.518
cookie-biscuit thing.

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:20.753
What you guys call biscuits,

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.455
we would actually kind of call scones,

00:10:22.455 --> 00:10:24.123
or scones, depending on where you're from,

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:25.491
and the thought of putting breakfast food

00:10:25.491 --> 00:10:26.993
in between them is kinda weird.

00:10:26.993 --> 00:10:27.927
They're usually reserved for

00:10:27.927 --> 00:10:29.762
cream and jam for an afternoon tea.

00:10:31.163 --> 00:10:34.266
Joe: Last, and,

00:10:34.266 --> 00:10:37.203
in my opinion, least,

00:10:37.203 --> 00:10:38.471
is this thing.

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:43.476
The Southwest Grilled Chicken Salad.

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:51.684
Producer: Yeah.

00:10:51.684 --> 00:10:53.719
Joe: Oh ho ho ho ho.

00:10:58.524 --> 00:11:00.760
Harry: Can I eat now?

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.428
Yeah? Yeah? K, cool.

00:11:03.396 --> 00:11:05.898
I don't care how many calories,
it's just really good.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.571
Mm-hmm.

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:14.774
Joe Avella From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:11:14.774 --> 00:11:16.942
we wanted to find out
all the differences

00:11:16.942 --> 00:11:19.679
between McDonald's in India
and the US .

00:11:19.679 --> 00:11:21.013
This is "Food Wars."

00:11:25.418 --> 00:11:28.087
Drinks in McDonald's
India come in three sizes:

00:11:28.087 --> 00:11:30.623
regular, medium, and large.

00:11:30.623 --> 00:11:33.559
Drinks in the McDonald's
in the US, four sizes:

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:36.996
extra small, small, medium, and large.

00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:41.467
Time to keep 'em honest.

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:46.605
Lost a couple drops. 26, 27 fluid ounces.

00:11:46.605 --> 00:11:48.307
Whoo!

00:11:48.307 --> 00:11:50.810
Hm.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.778
Fries in India come in three sizes:

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:55.014
regular, medium, and large.

00:11:55.014 --> 00:11:59.151
In America, our fries come
in four sizes, I think.

00:11:59.151 --> 00:12:02.121
We have a small, kids,

00:12:02.121 --> 00:12:04.890
or kids, small --

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:06.992
I can't tell the difference either --

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:09.228
medium, and large.

00:12:09.228 --> 00:12:11.464
The medium and large
come in these really cool

00:12:11.464 --> 00:12:14.366
new packaging where you can
just open it up like that

00:12:14.366 --> 00:12:15.735
and it's nice and easy to share.

00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:16.869
It's a little plate.

00:12:16.869 --> 00:12:18.704
Good job, McDonald's. Very innovative.

00:12:18.704 --> 00:12:20.306
But now it's time to measure

00:12:20.306 --> 00:12:22.174
and see how much we're really getting.

00:12:22.174 --> 00:12:24.076
Joe: First things first, the large.

00:12:26.645 --> 00:12:27.980
175 grams.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:30.182
Obviously it's different
per scoops or whatever.

00:12:30.182 --> 00:12:31.217
Yeah, let's go here.

00:12:31.217 --> 00:12:34.854
This one, almost exactly 100 grams.

00:12:34.854 --> 00:12:36.789
This one,

00:12:36.789 --> 00:12:37.890
80 grams.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.091
Fry math, hang on.

00:12:41.193 --> 00:12:42.795
This is, like ...

00:12:42.795 --> 00:12:43.796
yep, there you go.

00:12:43.796 --> 00:12:45.231
That's a 20-gram difference right there.

00:12:45.231 --> 00:12:46.732
So, you tell me, internet.

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:48.634
Is the kids and the small different sizes?

00:12:48.634 --> 00:12:49.702
I don't think they are.

00:12:49.702 --> 00:12:52.772
"Food Wars" is on it! We're on it, baby!

00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:53.739
What about McNuggets?

00:12:53.739 --> 00:12:56.876
Here in India, you can
order them in three sizes:

00:12:56.876 --> 00:13:00.613
six pieces, nine pieces, and 20 pieces.

00:13:00.613 --> 00:13:03.482
They gave it to us in
two boxes of 10 each.

00:13:03.482 --> 00:13:05.451
Oh, is that it, India? Cute.

00:13:05.451 --> 00:13:08.053
Our McNuggets start at four,

00:13:08.053 --> 00:13:09.488
then you got six,

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:10.823
10,

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:12.057
20,

00:13:12.057 --> 00:13:13.425
and not to be outdone,

00:13:13.425 --> 00:13:15.861
booyah, 40 McNuggets.

00:13:15.861 --> 00:13:18.397
All the mathheads watching
will be quick to point out

00:13:18.397 --> 00:13:22.401
that that is double India's
largest nugget option.

00:13:22.401 --> 00:13:24.703
The only burger that
India shares with the US

00:13:24.703 --> 00:13:27.339
is the McChicken, the humble McChicken.

00:13:27.339 --> 00:13:30.376
Not even gonna bother
with the analog scale now.

00:13:30.376 --> 00:13:31.544
Boop!

00:13:31.544 --> 00:13:33.646
149 grams.

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:35.915
Ah, just so frustrating.

00:13:35.915 --> 00:13:38.484
Just one more gram and
it would be perfect.

00:13:38.484 --> 00:13:41.220
With the paper? I mean, we'll do this and

00:13:42.454 --> 00:13:45.558
shave off an eighth of an ounce.

00:13:45.558 --> 00:13:49.728
Our McChicken weighs 140 grams.

00:13:52.097 --> 00:13:53.465
Here is everything you'll find on the menu

00:13:53.465 --> 00:13:56.635
at McDonald's India that you
will not find in the USA.

00:13:56.635 --> 00:13:58.237
And here's all the McDonald's menu items

00:13:58.237 --> 00:14:01.407
from the US you won't find in India.

00:14:01.407 --> 00:14:03.108
Here in India, we can't really recreate

00:14:03.108 --> 00:14:04.877
the iconic McDonald's Big Mac

00:14:04.877 --> 00:14:06.779
because it's made from a beef patty,

00:14:06.779 --> 00:14:08.881
and to keep to the religious sentiments

00:14:08.881 --> 00:14:10.549
of Hindus and even Muslims,

00:14:10.549 --> 00:14:11.817
we don't serve beef or pork

00:14:11.817 --> 00:14:13.319
in a lot of fast-food restaurants.

00:14:13.319 --> 00:14:17.289
We have something called
the chicken Maharaja Mac.

00:14:17.289 --> 00:14:21.393
As you can see, it's got
three buns, two patties,

00:14:21.393 --> 00:14:23.963
a lot of cheese and mayonnaise,

00:14:23.963 --> 00:14:26.699
some tomatoes, onions, lettuce.

00:14:26.699 --> 00:14:29.635
Lettuce try it now.
[ba-dum tish]

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.838
Oh, my God.

00:14:32.838 --> 00:14:35.207
That is truly a Maharaja Mac.

00:14:35.207 --> 00:14:37.543
If you're wondering, a raja is a king,

00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:39.812
and a maharaja is like an emperor.

00:14:39.812 --> 00:14:42.381
So this is clearly our
answer to the Big Mac.

00:14:42.381 --> 00:14:44.416
Now let's taste the veg Maharaja Mac.

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:46.185
I think it's actually
a very cool challenge

00:14:46.185 --> 00:14:47.586
that a lot of fast-food restaurants here

00:14:47.586 --> 00:14:49.288
have had to adapt to the Indian palate,

00:14:49.288 --> 00:14:52.091
as well as sensibilities of food.

00:14:52.091 --> 00:14:54.760
We have come up with such
cool, iconic fast food

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.762
that you won't get
anywhere else in the world.

00:14:56.762 --> 00:14:58.998
Like, look at this! This is outrageous!

00:14:58.998 --> 00:15:01.467
There's no way to eat
this without being messy.

00:15:01.467 --> 00:15:02.801
There's literally no way.

00:15:05.804 --> 00:15:06.805
Mm!

00:15:06.805 --> 00:15:08.941
Oh, my God. That's really good.

00:15:08.941 --> 00:15:11.277
Yes to all that, looks really good.

00:15:11.277 --> 00:15:13.812
Because of India's lack of beef,

00:15:13.812 --> 00:15:16.782
all the American beef options
are technically exclusives.

00:15:20.886 --> 00:15:22.121
All right.

00:15:22.121 --> 00:15:23.188
Big Mac.

00:15:23.188 --> 00:15:27.159
There it is, just brimming with stuff.

00:15:27.159 --> 00:15:29.061
My go-to for, like, 20 years.

00:15:29.061 --> 00:15:30.629
I still get it occasionally.

00:15:30.629 --> 00:15:33.565
The classic McDonald's hamburger.

00:15:33.565 --> 00:15:35.668
Beef patty, ketchup, and mustard.

00:15:35.668 --> 00:15:39.471
Of course, you can get it with cheese. Hi.

00:15:39.471 --> 00:15:42.875
You can upgrade to a double
cheeseburger or a McDouble.

00:15:42.875 --> 00:15:44.643
What's the difference, you ask?

00:15:44.643 --> 00:15:45.844
I'm not sure either.

00:15:45.844 --> 00:15:48.547
So let's start with the
double cheeseburger.

00:15:48.547 --> 00:15:50.282
Look at that. Look how yellow that is.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:53.152
Beef, cheese, beef, cheese, toppos.

00:15:53.152 --> 00:15:57.957
The McDouble is beef, cheese, beef.

00:15:57.957 --> 00:15:59.591
So it's just one slice of cheese

00:15:59.591 --> 00:16:00.893
in the middle, but not on top.

00:16:00.893 --> 00:16:03.729
What's the price difference?
Can we get that on-screen?

00:16:03.729 --> 00:16:05.531
And how much is a slice of cheese?

00:16:06.398 --> 00:16:07.967
Joe's hack, get yourself a McDouble

00:16:07.967 --> 00:16:09.835
and bring your own slice
of American cheese.

00:16:09.835 --> 00:16:12.705
Booyah. Save yourself
this amount of money.

00:16:12.705 --> 00:16:14.807
The problem with millennials today,

00:16:14.807 --> 00:16:16.875
the reason you guys can't buy houses is

00:16:16.875 --> 00:16:19.211
you're spending all
your money at Starbucks,

00:16:19.211 --> 00:16:21.680
you're getting your double cheeseburgers

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:25.017
instead of a McDouble and
bringing your own cheese slice.

00:16:25.017 --> 00:16:27.086
I mean, you guys are terrible with money!

00:16:27.086 --> 00:16:28.520
You're eating, what, seven,

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.122
eight McDoubles a day like me, right?

00:16:30.122 --> 00:16:33.826
And that adds up to, like,
at the end of the year, $18?

00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:37.029
10,000 years later, that's
a down payment on a house.

00:16:38.364 --> 00:16:39.565
What are you guys doing?

00:16:39.565 --> 00:16:43.702
All right, next up is the
iconic McAloo tikki burger.

00:16:43.702 --> 00:16:46.572
You take mashed potato, and
you fry it in breadcrumbs,

00:16:46.572 --> 00:16:48.640
and you get this really delicious cutlet.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:51.810
Here in India, they
adapted it into this burger

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:53.679
with a very special sauce,

00:16:53.679 --> 00:16:56.015
some tomato, and chopped onions.

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.619
Mm. It's just so classic.

00:17:00.619 --> 00:17:02.154
They nailed this burger.

00:17:02.154 --> 00:17:04.857
Next up, there is a Mexican McAloo tikki,

00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:08.660
which I assume has some
stereotypical Mexican ingredients

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.363
and flavors like jalapeño.

00:17:11.363 --> 00:17:13.399
Yes! Jalapeño.

00:17:13.399 --> 00:17:14.600
Mm, nice.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:17.169
It's way more spicy. Good twist.

00:17:17.169 --> 00:17:20.139
Next up, they have a McEgg burger.

00:17:20.139 --> 00:17:22.374
McEgg. McEgg, McEgg.

00:17:22.374 --> 00:17:23.776
I don't know why I did that.

00:17:23.776 --> 00:17:25.310
Let's see what that looks like.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.712
Ugh!

00:17:26.712 --> 00:17:27.813
Sorry.

00:17:27.813 --> 00:17:29.915
I did not expect ... pesto?

00:17:29.915 --> 00:17:32.284
Next up is a chicken kebab burger.

00:17:32.284 --> 00:17:34.887
Every time an Indian
fast-food chain tries to adapt

00:17:34.887 --> 00:17:38.457
an Indian special food into a burger,

00:17:38.457 --> 00:17:39.925
I take it with a pinch of salt

00:17:39.925 --> 00:17:41.994
because this is not what
we're used to seeing

00:17:41.994 --> 00:17:42.995
when we think of kebabs,

00:17:42.995 --> 00:17:46.131
but I'm going to try it,
and let's see what happens.

00:17:46.131 --> 00:17:47.433
Mm.

00:17:47.433 --> 00:17:49.068
It's very, very dry.

00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:52.037
Patty has almost a
cardboard-y taste to it.

00:17:52.037 --> 00:17:54.039
I wouldn't put those flavors together

00:17:54.039 --> 00:17:56.275
if I was thinking kebab.

00:17:56.275 --> 00:17:59.178
McCardboard tikki, maybe? No? OK.

00:17:59.178 --> 00:18:00.512
That's a bit harsh. I'm sorry.

00:18:00.512 --> 00:18:02.414
Next up is the McVeggie,

00:18:02.414 --> 00:18:06.385
which is the vegetarian
counterpart to our McChicken.

00:18:06.385 --> 00:18:09.254
If I had to eat this
versus the chicken one,

00:18:09.254 --> 00:18:11.323
I would not be upset at all.

00:18:11.323 --> 00:18:12.257
Really good.

00:18:12.257 --> 00:18:14.460
Next up, we have two "American" burgers:

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:17.529
the American Cheese Supreme veg

00:18:17.529 --> 00:18:20.999
and the American Cheese Supreme chicken.

00:18:20.999 --> 00:18:22.801
My hunch for what makes them American

00:18:22.801 --> 00:18:26.305
is that they will have a
nice big square of cheese

00:18:26.305 --> 00:18:29.374
and they will not be spicy at all.

00:18:29.374 --> 00:18:32.544
Except they have a lot
of jalapeños on them.

00:18:32.544 --> 00:18:37.082
Joe, let me know if this
constitutes "American."

00:18:37.082 --> 00:18:38.684
That's American cheese, my man.

00:18:38.684 --> 00:18:40.085
That's what makes it American.

00:18:40.085 --> 00:18:41.620
I don't know about those
other toppings, but,

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:42.488
yeah, it sounds about right.

00:18:42.488 --> 00:18:44.189
All right, so this is what
the McDonald's website

00:18:44.189 --> 00:18:46.225
says is in this burger.

00:18:46.225 --> 00:18:48.994
"Whole-wheat buns
sourced from Maharashtra,

00:18:48.994 --> 00:18:51.530
tangy jalapeños from Karnataka,

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.933
shredded onions grown
in local Indian farms,

00:18:54.933 --> 00:18:59.304
and cheese from Amaravati, also in India."

00:18:59.304 --> 00:19:02.174
Quite close to home, this burger.

00:19:02.174 --> 00:19:04.776
Currently, this would
probably be my favorite order,

00:19:04.776 --> 00:19:07.713
a McSpicy chicken, and
there's the vegetarian option,

00:19:07.713 --> 00:19:11.483
which is a McSpicy paneer,
which is just leaking lettuce.

00:19:11.483 --> 00:19:13.085
For those of you who
don't know what paneer is,

00:19:13.085 --> 00:19:15.087
it's basically cottage cheese.

00:19:15.087 --> 00:19:16.321
We love our paneer.

00:19:16.321 --> 00:19:19.324
We put it in curries, we eat
it plain, we put it in kebabs.

00:19:19.324 --> 00:19:21.860
It is so delicious. Let's try this.

00:19:24.062 --> 00:19:26.532
Mm. It has just the right kick,

00:19:26.532 --> 00:19:28.167
and it goes really well with the paneer.

00:19:28.167 --> 00:19:30.369
Fair warning, while this
may have a light kick

00:19:30.369 --> 00:19:33.305
of spice for us, it might
be a hard kick for you.

00:19:33.305 --> 00:19:37.109
So, take everything with
a pinch of chili powder.

00:19:37.109 --> 00:19:39.678
Gonna move up to something
called the Quarter Pounder,

00:19:39.678 --> 00:19:41.313
and that's, like, their big burger.

00:19:41.313 --> 00:19:42.948
So you can get a Quarter
Pounder with cheese.

00:19:42.948 --> 00:19:43.782
Here it is.

00:19:43.782 --> 00:19:45.784
I mean, it looks fake, right?

00:19:45.784 --> 00:19:47.586
Like, "Just kidding, it's cake!"

00:19:47.586 --> 00:19:50.956
Or the new one is, "It's
actually a candle!"

00:19:50.956 --> 00:19:54.293
And then you can get a Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:19:54.293 --> 00:19:56.929
More veggies on it, all
the junk that I brush off.

00:19:56.929 --> 00:20:00.899
You can upgrade to a double
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:20:00.899 --> 00:20:04.469
Let's take a look. Oh, man.
Look how thick this is!

00:20:04.469 --> 00:20:08.207
And then you can get that
same double with bacon.

00:20:08.207 --> 00:20:09.374
Yeah!

00:20:09.374 --> 00:20:12.244
Oh, man. Skimping on the bacon. Guys!

00:20:12.244 --> 00:20:14.646
What we lack in beef
burgers we make up for

00:20:14.646 --> 00:20:16.748
in gourmet burgers.

00:20:16.748 --> 00:20:18.750
That's right. Here at McDonald's India,

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.052
we have our own collection of

00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:23.255
chef's special gourmet burgers.

00:20:23.255 --> 00:20:24.223
Delicious.

00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:25.757
And I think this is a rolling menu.

00:20:25.757 --> 00:20:27.626
I think they introduce new
things from time to time.

00:20:27.626 --> 00:20:31.330
The buns themselves
look a lot more gourmet.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.365
You know, there's a nice
rift down the middle.

00:20:33.365 --> 00:20:35.334
Kind of looks like a butt, but that's OK.

00:20:35.334 --> 00:20:36.868
We're not gonna concentrate on that.

00:20:37.903 --> 00:20:40.539
First up, we have triple
cheese American veg burger

00:20:40.539 --> 00:20:43.575
and triple cheese American chicken burger.

00:20:43.575 --> 00:20:47.412
Same thing. Cheese, jalapeño,
some sauce, lettuce,

00:20:47.412 --> 00:20:50.315
simple chicken patty, gourmet bun.

00:20:50.315 --> 00:20:51.850
Does this scream "American" to you?

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:54.686
Next up, Cheese Lava American veg burger

00:20:54.686 --> 00:20:57.589
and Cheese Lava American chicken burger,

00:20:57.589 --> 00:20:58.857
again with American

00:20:58.857 --> 00:21:01.860
and again with the strange relation

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:05.297
of food to volcanoes and lava.

00:21:06.798 --> 00:21:07.966
OK.

00:21:07.966 --> 00:21:10.068
This burger is very spicy.

00:21:10.068 --> 00:21:13.305
This qualifies as a
volcano product, for sure.

00:21:13.305 --> 00:21:15.173
Congratulations, McDonald's.

00:21:15.173 --> 00:21:18.744
The lava in the title
of this burger works.

00:21:18.744 --> 00:21:21.013
The McSpicy chicken premium, though,

00:21:21.013 --> 00:21:24.082
has an egg patty inside of it.

00:21:24.082 --> 00:21:26.418
Mm-mm.

00:21:26.418 --> 00:21:29.087
Mm, that's pretty good.

00:21:29.087 --> 00:21:31.223
I just feel so existential right now.

00:21:32.157 --> 00:21:33.759
Imagine sitting here at this table

00:21:33.759 --> 00:21:37.462
and just tasting every single
burger on a McDonald's menu.

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:40.265
Amazing.

00:21:40.265 --> 00:21:42.200
But also, s---.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:44.403
We also have some exclusive wrap options.

00:21:44.403 --> 00:21:47.773
We have Big Spicy paneer
and Big Spicy chicken.

00:21:47.773 --> 00:21:51.376
I think this is the same
McSpicy chicken patty,

00:21:51.376 --> 00:21:53.945
and it's wrapped around a tortilla,

00:21:53.945 --> 00:21:56.214
which is actually way
closer to an Indian chapati

00:21:56.214 --> 00:21:57.783
than most other fast-food restaurants.

00:21:57.783 --> 00:22:00.152
It doesn't feel as synthetic.

00:22:00.152 --> 00:22:02.287
Our McDonald's in the US

00:22:02.287 --> 00:22:04.923
had wraps for a brief period of time.

00:22:04.923 --> 00:22:07.893
One day they were gone. Nobody noticed.

00:22:07.893 --> 00:22:09.928
Yeah, you guys got some chicken
stuff that we don't have,

00:22:09.928 --> 00:22:11.263
but we got a few of our own.

00:22:11.263 --> 00:22:12.998
More recently than you think,

00:22:12.998 --> 00:22:15.667
they finally introduced
their chicken sandwich

00:22:15.667 --> 00:22:19.538
to an already-crowded
chicken-sandwich market,

00:22:19.538 --> 00:22:21.873
and that is of course their
crispy chicken sandwich,

00:22:21.873 --> 00:22:24.810
and this thing is fantastic.

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:26.211
It's one of the best ones.

00:22:26.211 --> 00:22:27.446
They were late to the game,

00:22:27.446 --> 00:22:29.081
and they kind of took
it over, in my opinion.

00:22:29.081 --> 00:22:31.516
And what I like about it,
it's simple. Look at this.

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:34.686
You just got crispy
chicken, pickles that suck.

00:22:34.686 --> 00:22:36.121
It's baller. It tastes great.

00:22:36.121 --> 00:22:37.956
Like it a little spicy, India?

00:22:37.956 --> 00:22:39.091
It probably doesn't
compare to what you guys

00:22:39.091 --> 00:22:40.826
are rocking in India but, you know,

00:22:40.826 --> 00:22:43.061
this one has a little nice heat to it.

00:22:43.061 --> 00:22:44.363
Pickles, sauce.

00:22:44.363 --> 00:22:46.031
Want to take it up a notch?

00:22:46.031 --> 00:22:47.399
Gotta go deluxe.

00:22:47.399 --> 00:22:49.901
The cool crispness of the vegetables

00:22:49.901 --> 00:22:53.205
just clash so well with the spicy sauce.

00:22:53.205 --> 00:22:54.873
It's good. It's good.

00:22:54.873 --> 00:22:56.475
Nikhil, say the word,

00:22:56.475 --> 00:22:58.577
and I'm putting one in
the post for you tomorrow.

00:22:58.577 --> 00:23:00.011
So when it arrives in three weeks,

00:23:00.011 --> 00:23:01.813
you can throw it out.

00:23:01.813 --> 00:23:04.316
Now we're getting into
exclusive side dishes.

00:23:04.316 --> 00:23:07.085
Here in India, we have these add-ons.

00:23:07.085 --> 00:23:10.489
No. 1, the veg pizza McPuff.

00:23:10.489 --> 00:23:13.325
This is one of the most
delicious things we have here.

00:23:13.325 --> 00:23:15.494
It's basically a pizza Hot Pocket.

00:23:15.494 --> 00:23:17.829
Masala wedges. These are potato wedges

00:23:17.829 --> 00:23:21.633
with classic Indian masala flavor to them.

00:23:21.633 --> 00:23:22.801
Ooh, boy.

00:23:22.801 --> 00:23:24.669
Masalas are basically what we use

00:23:24.669 --> 00:23:26.738
to spice and flavor dishes,

00:23:26.738 --> 00:23:29.107
and they consist primarily
of ground-up spices

00:23:29.107 --> 00:23:31.243
like cardamom, cloves,

00:23:31.243 --> 00:23:33.111
red chilies, Kashmiri chilies.

00:23:33.111 --> 00:23:35.514
You go to every Indian home, the mums,

00:23:35.514 --> 00:23:38.183
the grandmums will have
their own random, you know,

00:23:38.183 --> 00:23:41.987
masala mix that they
use and that's guarded

00:23:41.987 --> 00:23:44.790
and treasured in their family, forever.

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:47.058
Next up, we have cheesy masala wedges.

00:23:47.058 --> 00:23:51.196
They're also serving a
classic cup of boiled corn,

00:23:51.196 --> 00:23:55.634
which is so unique, and they
give you a side of Amul butter.

00:23:55.634 --> 00:23:58.570
Guys, Amul butter is part of our culture.

00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:01.506
Makhan. Makhan!

00:24:01.506 --> 00:24:02.407
This is probably going to be

00:24:02.407 --> 00:24:04.176
the most delicious bite of the day.

00:24:07.646 --> 00:24:08.847
I love corn.

00:24:08.847 --> 00:24:10.215
Next up, chicken strips.

00:24:10.215 --> 00:24:14.219
They come in packs of two, three, or five.

00:24:14.219 --> 00:24:17.189
Cheesy nugget veg bites.

00:24:17.189 --> 00:24:18.723
Yeah, this is just a vegetarian version

00:24:18.723 --> 00:24:19.624
of the chicken nuggets,

00:24:19.624 --> 00:24:21.993
and it's got some corn, some tomato.

00:24:23.195 --> 00:24:24.663
Mm, it's OK.

00:24:24.663 --> 00:24:28.500
Next, we have the double cheese McMuffin.

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:32.404
And lastly, we have Mexican cheesy fries.

00:24:32.404 --> 00:24:34.072
On the McDonald's India website,

00:24:34.072 --> 00:24:36.208
one British customer said

00:24:36.208 --> 00:24:39.644
that these Mexican cheesy
fries are "the real deal."

00:24:39.644 --> 00:24:42.581
I have no idea how a
British person can say

00:24:42.581 --> 00:24:44.416
that Mexican cheesy
fries are the real deal,

00:24:44.416 --> 00:24:46.551
but anytime a British person says

00:24:46.551 --> 00:24:49.354
that another culture's
food is "the real deal,"

00:24:49.354 --> 00:24:53.325
it puts a little fear in
our small Indian hearts.

00:24:53.325 --> 00:24:54.793
Yeah those fries look like ass.

00:24:54.793 --> 00:24:59.231
And the next exclusive side
that we have is apple slices.

00:25:00.866 --> 00:25:03.468
Cut 'em up, put 'em in a plastic bag.

00:25:03.468 --> 00:25:06.438
'Bout to get saucy. That's
right, ladies and gentlemen.

00:25:09.641 --> 00:25:11.910
Sauce talk.

00:25:11.910 --> 00:25:12.978
Thank you.

00:25:14.079 --> 00:25:15.046
Spicy Buffalo.

00:25:16.581 --> 00:25:17.616
Not that good.

00:25:17.616 --> 00:25:19.584
We got a tangy barbecue.

00:25:20.519 --> 00:25:21.353
Ooh.

00:25:22.821 --> 00:25:23.722
Much better.

00:25:23.722 --> 00:25:25.657
Mm. Honey mustard.

00:25:28.159 --> 00:25:29.361
Tastes like salad dressing.

00:25:29.361 --> 00:25:30.462
Sweet and sour.

00:25:32.264 --> 00:25:33.565
I would tie it with the tangy barbecue

00:25:33.565 --> 00:25:35.934
because it's so different,
so we'll keep these guys

00:25:35.934 --> 00:25:37.035
same tier.

00:25:37.035 --> 00:25:40.105
Ranch, I don't know.
America, we love our ranch.

00:25:40.105 --> 00:25:41.072
Ranch is just OK.

00:25:41.072 --> 00:25:43.441
That's right, I said it. Ranch is just OK.

00:25:43.441 --> 00:25:47.045
Oh, and all ranch tastes the same. Yeah.

00:25:47.045 --> 00:25:48.647
And finally, honey.

00:25:50.815 --> 00:25:52.117
How do you like that?

00:25:52.117 --> 00:25:53.552
Honey's the best one.

00:25:53.552 --> 00:25:55.854
And all that money, all that energy,

00:25:55.854 --> 00:25:58.356
all that time creating all these recipes,

00:25:58.356 --> 00:26:01.626
trying to sway the American mind,

00:26:01.626 --> 00:26:05.463
and you got beat by a bunch of bees.

00:26:05.463 --> 00:26:07.599
Power to the bees!

00:26:07.599 --> 00:26:09.801
We have one exclusive spice mix

00:26:09.801 --> 00:26:11.970
as well as one exclusive
sauce here in India.

00:26:11.970 --> 00:26:14.072
We have chili sauce, which
is pretty straightforward.

00:26:14.072 --> 00:26:15.173
It's chili sauce.

00:26:15.173 --> 00:26:17.208
But let me tell you about

00:26:17.208 --> 00:26:20.378
peri-peri spice mix.

00:26:20.378 --> 00:26:24.549
So, McDonald's launched
this in 2013 here in India,

00:26:24.549 --> 00:26:27.252
and it was so popular, there were riots

00:26:27.252 --> 00:26:28.653
when they said they were
going to discontinue it.

00:26:28.653 --> 00:26:32.357
And so now, it's a permanent
addition to the menu.

00:26:32.357 --> 00:26:34.593
First, you get this shake bag,

00:26:34.593 --> 00:26:36.628
then you grab your fries,

00:26:36.628 --> 00:26:38.830
and then you just pour that in there.

00:26:38.830 --> 00:26:39.698
Ah.

00:26:46.538 --> 00:26:48.707
Boom! Oh, boy.

00:26:48.707 --> 00:26:50.809
Can we cut to a before of the fries?

00:26:50.809 --> 00:26:54.412
You saw how they were. Now look at these.

00:26:54.412 --> 00:26:56.915
You can see the little flecks of spice

00:26:56.915 --> 00:26:58.950
just adorning each fry.

00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:07.659
Hello, it's Crystelle.

00:27:07.659 --> 00:27:10.662
And I know Nikhil has
peri-peri McDonald's chips,

00:27:10.662 --> 00:27:13.298
but in the UK, it is all about Nando's.

00:27:13.298 --> 00:27:14.599
Cheeky Nando's.

00:27:14.599 --> 00:27:16.301
Let's talk about peri-peri.

00:27:16.301 --> 00:27:18.970
Peri means pepper. And
it's a blend of spices,

00:27:18.970 --> 00:27:22.273
so it's got things like paprika,
ground bird's eye chili,

00:27:22.273 --> 00:27:24.709
a bit of oregano, a pinch
of ginger and cardamom,

00:27:24.709 --> 00:27:26.378
but it's a Portuguese spice blend.

00:27:26.378 --> 00:27:28.446
It's funny because
obviously Nikhil mentioned

00:27:28.446 --> 00:27:30.882
that the peri-peri fries
just blew off in India,

00:27:30.882 --> 00:27:33.151
and it makes sense, because I'm from Goa,

00:27:33.151 --> 00:27:34.653
which is in the south of India.

00:27:34.653 --> 00:27:36.921
Goa was colonized by the Portuguese.

00:27:36.921 --> 00:27:38.790
And so I really think that Indians

00:27:38.790 --> 00:27:40.725
are accustomed to that
Portuguese taste palate,

00:27:40.725 --> 00:27:44.562
which is why peri-peri fries
are doing so well in India.

00:27:44.562 --> 00:27:45.830
But enough of the talking.

00:27:45.830 --> 00:27:48.366
I want to dig into these
fries, because they look great.

00:27:48.366 --> 00:27:50.402
Mm. Oh, this is so good.

00:27:50.402 --> 00:27:51.903
Harry, get involved.

00:27:51.903 --> 00:27:52.937
You're not eating chips
without me, are you?

00:27:52.937 --> 00:27:54.906
Oh, sorry, I've already had a head start.

00:27:54.906 --> 00:27:56.207
Harry: Cheers.
Crystelle: Cheers.

00:27:57.208 --> 00:28:01.112
God damn, if that isn't like crack.

00:28:01.112 --> 00:28:02.080
For the early risers,

00:28:02.080 --> 00:28:04.382
there's plenty of
exclusive breakfast items

00:28:04.382 --> 00:28:05.717
at the US McDonald's.

00:28:05.717 --> 00:28:07.786
Sausage biscuit with egg.

00:28:07.786 --> 00:28:09.287
Next one,

00:28:09.287 --> 00:28:10.488
sausage biscuit.

00:28:10.488 --> 00:28:13.124
I mean, they take the
egg out, so it's just ...

00:28:13.124 --> 00:28:16.528
This, of course, is
bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:28:16.528 --> 00:28:17.529
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:28:17.529 --> 00:28:19.097
we've reached the point of the breakfast

00:28:19.097 --> 00:28:20.699
where we get into the McGriddles.

00:28:20.699 --> 00:28:21.766
I love McGriddles.

00:28:21.766 --> 00:28:24.369
What's a McGriddle, you ask,
India? Fantastic question.

00:28:24.369 --> 00:28:27.138
McDonald's had this genius idea

00:28:27.138 --> 00:28:29.908
to replace the breakfast
sandwiches they already had

00:28:29.908 --> 00:28:31.543
with pancakes.

00:28:31.543 --> 00:28:35.613
And they also, like, inject
syrup into it somehow?

00:28:35.613 --> 00:28:39.584
But it is a breakfast sandwich
with pancakes for buns,

00:28:39.584 --> 00:28:43.955
and it's the best idea anyone's
ever had, anywhere, ever.

00:28:43.955 --> 00:28:47.492
[Joe laughing]

00:28:47.492 --> 00:28:49.094
Look at this! Look at this, look at this.

00:28:49.094 --> 00:28:51.029
They've even got a little M on there.

00:28:51.029 --> 00:28:52.197
This mini pancake.

00:28:52.197 --> 00:28:54.199
I know I'm wearing the
gloves, but this one's mine.

00:28:55.667 --> 00:28:56.534
Mm.

00:28:56.534 --> 00:29:00.505
We have a veg McMuffin
and a sausage McMuffin.

00:29:02.006 --> 00:29:02.841
Mm.

00:29:02.841 --> 00:29:05.477
The sausage here in India
is not made out of pork,

00:29:05.477 --> 00:29:06.811
like it is in the US.

00:29:06.811 --> 00:29:09.314
Instead, it's made out of simple chicken.

00:29:09.314 --> 00:29:12.817
Speaking of sausage, you
can get a breakfast burrito.

00:29:14.319 --> 00:29:17.088
Bro, I could put five of
these away, easy. Easy.

00:29:17.088 --> 00:29:19.157
If you're, like, a total drag

00:29:19.157 --> 00:29:21.860
and you want oatmeal in
the morning, we have it.

00:29:21.860 --> 00:29:24.229
It's about as inspiring
as you would think.

00:29:24.229 --> 00:29:25.797
Hotcakes and sausage.

00:29:25.797 --> 00:29:28.032
Of course, it comes with hot syrup.

00:29:28.032 --> 00:29:29.067
This here,

00:29:30.301 --> 00:29:32.403
the big breakfast with hotcakes.

00:29:32.403 --> 00:29:33.438
And it's big.

00:29:33.438 --> 00:29:36.274
A lot of eggs, kind of
wimpy-looking bacon,

00:29:36.274 --> 00:29:39.077
got yourself two English muffins here.

00:29:39.077 --> 00:29:42.080
And, of course, comes with a hash brown.

00:29:42.080 --> 00:29:44.048
Potatoes. Who doesn't love 'em?

00:29:44.048 --> 00:29:46.184
McDonald's hash brown, undefeated.

00:29:46.184 --> 00:29:47.152
These things are so good.

00:29:47.152 --> 00:29:48.953
India exclusive desserts.

00:29:48.953 --> 00:29:51.956
We have a Black Forest McFlurry,

00:29:51.956 --> 00:29:53.825
a vanilla chocolate muffin,

00:29:53.825 --> 00:29:56.261
and a chocolate chip muffin.

00:29:56.261 --> 00:29:59.264
It's kind of like a
McFlurry soup right now.

00:30:01.065 --> 00:30:04.602
This would be really good when
it was actually a McFlurry.

00:30:04.602 --> 00:30:07.005
Desserts! USA, we got 'em.

00:30:07.005 --> 00:30:08.640
So, starting down here, very simple,

00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:10.475
chocolate chip cookies.

00:30:10.475 --> 00:30:12.343
This next thing, apple fritter, right?

00:30:13.545 --> 00:30:14.646
Mm.

00:30:14.646 --> 00:30:17.849
This right here is called a
glazed pull-apart doughnut.

00:30:17.849 --> 00:30:18.983
Blueberry muffin.

00:30:18.983 --> 00:30:20.218
If you've had one, you've had them all.

00:30:20.218 --> 00:30:21.486
This is a what type of pie?

00:30:23.121 --> 00:30:24.522
Let's see what's inside.

00:30:24.522 --> 00:30:27.759
OK. I'm suddenly more interested. Yeah!

00:30:27.759 --> 00:30:29.761
Guava and cream.

00:30:29.761 --> 00:30:32.363
How about we'll call it
the cream and guava pie?

00:30:32.363 --> 00:30:33.498
Nah, this sucks.

00:30:33.498 --> 00:30:34.966
[Anders laughing]

00:30:35.800 --> 00:30:36.801
I don't f--- with it.

00:30:36.801 --> 00:30:39.504
Standard menu item, the
McDonald's apple pie.

00:30:39.504 --> 00:30:40.338
Everyone knows about this.

00:30:40.338 --> 00:30:42.674
I don't want a pizza version of this.

00:30:42.674 --> 00:30:45.710
Eh! And last but not least, cinnamon roll.

00:30:45.710 --> 00:30:46.978
Too sticky. I don't feel like eating it.

00:30:51.049 --> 00:30:52.684
Update: It's not sticky.

00:30:52.684 --> 00:30:55.086
It's actually [knocks on cinnamon roll].

00:30:55.086 --> 00:30:57.388
Exclusive drinks, starting with,

00:30:57.388 --> 00:30:59.023
we have something called

00:30:59.023 --> 00:31:02.527
B Natural's mixed fruit juice.

00:31:02.527 --> 00:31:03.695
Next up, we have something

00:31:03.695 --> 00:31:07.732
that they call raw mango fruit splash.

00:31:07.732 --> 00:31:08.900
Oh!

00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:10.401
It's a bit too sweet.

00:31:10.401 --> 00:31:12.503
Berry lemonade splash.

00:31:12.503 --> 00:31:16.174
All of these come in these very unique

00:31:16.174 --> 00:31:18.543
reusable bottles, apparently.

00:31:18.543 --> 00:31:22.714
Next up, strawberry chiller,
green apple chiller,

00:31:22.714 --> 00:31:25.683
and lemon chiller.

00:31:26.851 --> 00:31:29.254
It's just flavored water.
That's exactly what it is.

00:31:29.254 --> 00:31:31.789
It's flavored water,
and I kind of like it.

00:31:31.789 --> 00:31:34.325
This is a mixed berry smoothie.

00:31:36.361 --> 00:31:38.263
It's still quite sweet, but quite good.

00:31:38.263 --> 00:31:40.865
Next up, American mud pie shake.

00:31:42.333 --> 00:31:45.036
Mm. That's pretty yum.

00:31:45.036 --> 00:31:46.504
Drink roulette.

00:31:46.504 --> 00:31:48.773
Ooh, and the ice melted. Fantastic.

00:31:48.773 --> 00:31:51.476
Dr. Pepper. Let's go!

00:31:51.476 --> 00:31:54.245
Coke, nonexclusive. Let's go.

00:31:54.245 --> 00:31:55.747
Sweet tea, too sweet.

00:31:57.215 --> 00:31:59.450
Ugh, yeah. Unsweetened
tea, not sweet enough.

00:31:59.450 --> 00:32:00.518
You guys combine.

00:32:00.518 --> 00:32:02.987
For the kids watching,
why are you watching?

00:32:02.987 --> 00:32:04.822
Where are your parents or supervisors?

00:32:04.822 --> 00:32:07.525
You can get yourself apple juice, milk.

00:32:07.525 --> 00:32:08.993
Come on, you're drinking milk?

00:32:08.993 --> 00:32:10.261
The thought of drinking straight milk,

00:32:10.261 --> 00:32:11.462
like, hurts my stomach.

00:32:11.462 --> 00:32:12.964
There's also chocolate milk on the menu.

00:32:12.964 --> 00:32:13.932
Once upon a time,

00:32:13.932 --> 00:32:16.901
this was an iced French vanilla latte.

00:32:16.901 --> 00:32:19.971
Now it's more of a room-temperature
French vanilla latte.

00:32:21.806 --> 00:32:23.942
That's just OK. It's, like, really sweet.

00:32:23.942 --> 00:32:25.543
Strawberry banana smoothie.

00:32:26.611 --> 00:32:28.079
Yeah, I always loved getting these.

00:32:28.079 --> 00:32:29.180
These are good.

00:32:29.180 --> 00:32:31.282
So I'm going to assume
they're not good for me.

00:32:31.282 --> 00:32:32.717
Exclusive hot drinks.

00:32:32.717 --> 00:32:35.286
First off, we have strawberry green tea.

00:32:35.286 --> 00:32:38.022
Next up, English breakfast tea

00:32:38.022 --> 00:32:40.325
and Moroccan tea.

00:32:40.325 --> 00:32:42.760
Next up, a flat white coffee.

00:32:42.760 --> 00:32:46.197
India, a land where we run on chai,

00:32:46.197 --> 00:32:49.100
and McDonald's does
not have a chai option.

00:32:49.100 --> 00:32:50.802
Caramel macchiato,

00:32:50.802 --> 00:32:52.737
cappuccino,

00:32:52.737 --> 00:32:53.938
caramel latte,

00:32:53.938 --> 00:32:55.006
a vanilla cappuccino.

00:32:55.006 --> 00:32:57.041
The V does look like a U.

00:32:57.041 --> 00:33:00.244
McDonald's premium roast coffee.

00:33:02.180 --> 00:33:03.381
I'm going to hang on to this one.

00:33:05.717 --> 00:33:09.287
In India, a chicken Maharaja
Mac will cost you 231 rupees

00:33:09.287 --> 00:33:10.455
for just the sandwich.

00:33:10.455 --> 00:33:13.124
That's around $3.03.

00:33:13.124 --> 00:33:15.193
We do not have the chicken Maharaja Mac,

00:33:15.193 --> 00:33:16.861
but we do have the Big Mac,

00:33:16.861 --> 00:33:20.164
and a Big Mac in the US costs $4.89.

00:33:20.164 --> 00:33:23.167
That is a 61% price increase.

00:33:23.167 --> 00:33:25.236
Now, what if you turn this into a meal?

00:33:25.236 --> 00:33:28.339
A McSaver Maharaja Mac combo
comes with regular fries

00:33:28.339 --> 00:33:32.377
and a regular drink and
will cost you 356 rupees.

00:33:32.377 --> 00:33:35.747
That is $4.67, still less than the price

00:33:35.747 --> 00:33:37.749
of the American sandwich on its own.

00:33:37.749 --> 00:33:40.151
But does the combo meal
make a difference in the US?

00:33:40.151 --> 00:33:41.419
A medium Big Mac combo,

00:33:41.419 --> 00:33:44.389
so Big Mac, medium fries, medium drink,

00:33:44.389 --> 00:33:46.624
is $8.99.

00:33:46.624 --> 00:33:49.927
That's a 92% cost increase,

00:33:49.927 --> 00:33:52.563
even worse than if you just
bought the sandwich on its own.

00:33:52.563 --> 00:33:54.198
On the Indian McDonald's menu,

00:33:54.198 --> 00:33:55.600
you'll find a two-person meal,

00:33:55.600 --> 00:33:58.836
which contains a chicken
Maharaja Mac, a veg Maharaja Mac,

00:33:58.836 --> 00:34:02.807
large fries, two pizza
McPuffs, and a drink.

00:34:02.807 --> 00:34:07.445
All of this will cost
you 681 rupees, or $8.93.

00:34:07.445 --> 00:34:09.514
So, basically, you're
getting food for two people

00:34:09.514 --> 00:34:12.350
for the price of one
person's meal in the US.

00:34:12.350 --> 00:34:14.152
However, while it seems a lot cheaper

00:34:14.152 --> 00:34:16.020
than the food in the US,

00:34:16.020 --> 00:34:17.588
it's still very expensive

00:34:17.588 --> 00:34:19.957
and aspirational to people over here.

00:34:19.957 --> 00:34:22.026
Your minimum wage per hour

00:34:22.026 --> 00:34:24.362
is equal to our daily minimum wage.

00:34:24.362 --> 00:34:25.463
And so, yeah,

00:34:25.463 --> 00:34:27.632
a lot of people can't really
afford this kind of food.

00:34:27.632 --> 00:34:29.267
The English-speaking Indians that you see

00:34:29.267 --> 00:34:32.003
in a lot of YouTube videos on the internet

00:34:32.003 --> 00:34:33.438
aren't really a proper reflection

00:34:33.438 --> 00:34:35.473
of the majority of people
that live in this country,

00:34:35.473 --> 00:34:37.575
who still can't afford food like this.

00:34:37.575 --> 00:34:39.844
So, I'm checking my privilege,

00:34:39.844 --> 00:34:41.712
and we should all make sure we check ours.

00:34:41.712 --> 00:34:43.314
But let's play devil's advocate.

00:34:43.314 --> 00:34:45.616
McDonald's India has definitely included

00:34:45.616 --> 00:34:48.119
a lot more affordable
options on their menu.

00:34:48.119 --> 00:34:50.421
And so they are more approachable

00:34:50.421 --> 00:34:53.624
to the average urban Indian
than other fast-food chains.

00:34:57.095 --> 00:34:58.129
Let's compare some items

00:34:58.129 --> 00:35:01.499
to see who has the least
healthy McDonald's food.

00:35:01.499 --> 00:35:05.103
In the US, a McChicken
contains 400 calories,

00:35:05.103 --> 00:35:08.439
21 grams of fat, 39 grams of carbs.

00:35:08.439 --> 00:35:09.974
5 of those are sugar,

00:35:09.974 --> 00:35:12.343
and 560 milligrams of sodium.

00:35:12.343 --> 00:35:13.878
How about the Indian McChicken?

00:35:13.878 --> 00:35:16.781
One of these contains 398 calories,

00:35:16.781 --> 00:35:19.317
15 grams of total fat, 48 grams of carbs,

00:35:19.317 --> 00:35:21.452
5 grams of which are sugars,

00:35:21.452 --> 00:35:24.455
787 milligrams of sodium.

00:35:24.455 --> 00:35:28.092
So the Indian version has
slightly fewer calories,

00:35:28.092 --> 00:35:32.163
way lesser fats, but much
more carbs and sodium.

00:35:32.163 --> 00:35:33.464
What if we made that a combo meal?

00:35:33.464 --> 00:35:36.334
Well, a medium fry in the
US contains the following:

00:35:36.334 --> 00:35:39.237
320 calories, 15 grams of total fat,

00:35:39.237 --> 00:35:41.639
43 grams of carbs, no sugar,

00:35:41.639 --> 00:35:43.808
and 260 milligrams of sodium.

00:35:43.808 --> 00:35:47.512
While a medium fries in
India contains 340 calories,

00:35:47.512 --> 00:35:50.715
17 grams of total fat, 41 grams of carbs,

00:35:50.715 --> 00:35:52.216
0 grams of sugars,

00:35:52.216 --> 00:35:55.520
and 256 milligrams of sodium.

00:35:55.520 --> 00:35:58.089
And if we add the medium Coke,

00:35:58.089 --> 00:36:01.559
that is adding 210 calories, no fat,

00:36:01.559 --> 00:36:04.462
56 grams of carbs, 56 of those are sugar,

00:36:04.462 --> 00:36:06.731
and 55 milligrams of sodium.

00:36:06.731 --> 00:36:08.533
Ooh, a nice salty Coke.

00:36:08.533 --> 00:36:10.001
We'll do the same. Here in India,

00:36:10.001 --> 00:36:13.504
one medium Coke will
cost you 151 calories,

00:36:13.504 --> 00:36:16.174
0 grams of fat, 38 grams of carbs,

00:36:16.174 --> 00:36:18.643
38 grams of which are sugars,

00:36:18.643 --> 00:36:21.512
and there are 0 grams
of sodium, but my God,

00:36:21.512 --> 00:36:24.549
that is a lot of sugar packed in this cup.

00:36:24.549 --> 00:36:26.651
That leaves the Indian
meal at a grand total

00:36:26.651 --> 00:36:30.087
of 889 calories, 32 grams of fat,

00:36:30.087 --> 00:36:31.923
127 grams of carbs,

00:36:31.923 --> 00:36:33.758
out of which 43 grams are sugars,

00:36:33.758 --> 00:36:38.396
and 1,043 milligrams of sodium.

00:36:38.396 --> 00:36:39.297
Sheesh.

00:36:39.297 --> 00:36:42.133
Which means this whole bad boy altogether

00:36:42.133 --> 00:36:44.168
is 930 calories,

00:36:44.168 --> 00:36:45.703
36 grams of total fat,

00:36:45.703 --> 00:36:47.171
138 grams of carbs,

00:36:47.171 --> 00:36:49.373
61 of those grams are sugar,

00:36:49.373 --> 00:36:52.176
875 milligrams of sodium.

00:36:52.176 --> 00:36:54.979
Little bit lower sodium than India,

00:36:54.979 --> 00:36:59.283
but we got you guys beat in
calorie, fats, carbs, and sugar.

00:36:59.283 --> 00:37:03.421
Mm, mm, mm, mm! We win. We win.

00:37:03.421 --> 00:37:04.522
Ah!

00:37:04.522 --> 00:37:05.489
Unfortunately for India,

00:37:05.489 --> 00:37:07.225
the combo stats are a little misleading,

00:37:07.225 --> 00:37:09.293
and the difference maker is the Coke,

00:37:09.293 --> 00:37:12.129
because the American meal
has a larger portion.

00:37:12.129 --> 00:37:14.932
If you order the Coke
Zero in both countries,

00:37:14.932 --> 00:37:17.835
the Indian meal will actually
have a higher calorie count.

00:37:20.371 --> 00:37:22.406
McDonald's India does
not share a full list

00:37:22.406 --> 00:37:23.608
of their ingredients,

00:37:23.608 --> 00:37:26.544
but there are some things
we do know about their food.

00:37:26.544 --> 00:37:27.778
Like, did you know that McDonald's India

00:37:27.778 --> 00:37:29.947
actually changed Indian farming practices

00:37:29.947 --> 00:37:32.650
just so they could grow the
kind of potato that they wanted?

00:37:32.650 --> 00:37:34.986
When they first launched in India in 1996,

00:37:34.986 --> 00:37:36.420
McDonald's promised the government

00:37:36.420 --> 00:37:38.089
that they would use products grown

00:37:38.089 --> 00:37:40.024
and sourced right here in India.

00:37:40.024 --> 00:37:42.059
But people who had eaten McDonald's abroad

00:37:42.059 --> 00:37:45.096
realized that the fries
didn't taste quite the same.

00:37:45.096 --> 00:37:46.764
The reason for this is
that Indian potatoes

00:37:46.764 --> 00:37:48.132
were too small, round,

00:37:48.132 --> 00:37:50.701
had way too much moisture
and sugar content.

00:37:50.701 --> 00:37:53.871
And so the fries made out of
them were not long enough,

00:37:53.871 --> 00:37:56.207
they didn't get crispy
enough, and they didn't have

00:37:56.207 --> 00:37:59.176
that distinctive McDonald's oomph to them.

00:37:59.176 --> 00:38:01.679
So, McDonald's partnered
with McCain Foods,

00:38:01.679 --> 00:38:05.383
and they spent nine years
trying to perfect their potato.

00:38:05.383 --> 00:38:08.185
They imported saplings
which had the perfect shape

00:38:08.185 --> 00:38:09.954
and starch content that they needed.

00:38:09.954 --> 00:38:12.156
They also chose Gujarat
as their farming location

00:38:12.156 --> 00:38:13.624
for its climate, and they switched

00:38:13.624 --> 00:38:16.527
from a flood irrigation
to a sprinkler system

00:38:16.527 --> 00:38:19.163
to reduce moisture content and save water.

00:38:19.163 --> 00:38:22.300
The result: bigger and
more starchy potatoes

00:38:22.300 --> 00:38:24.268
that can be used to make
the McDonald's fries

00:38:24.268 --> 00:38:26.037
that you know and love.

00:38:26.037 --> 00:38:29.273
McDonald's in the US
mostly uses russet Burbank

00:38:29.273 --> 00:38:32.810
or Shepody, "shep-a-tee," potatoes.

00:38:32.810 --> 00:38:34.445
Potato me.

00:38:34.445 --> 00:38:38.983
So, these are big enough that
the distinctive long fry,

00:38:38.983 --> 00:38:41.652
yeah, look how long this is. Wow!

00:38:41.652 --> 00:38:44.722
Known to be low moisture
and low sugar content.

00:38:44.722 --> 00:38:47.091
This means they can
remain crispy when fried

00:38:47.091 --> 00:38:48.659
and don't caramelize too fast,

00:38:48.659 --> 00:38:51.295
so you can get a nice, even browning.

00:38:51.295 --> 00:38:53.531
McDonald's in the US actually discloses

00:38:53.531 --> 00:38:54.565
all of its ingredients,

00:38:54.565 --> 00:38:56.834
so we can figure out a
few other differences.

00:38:56.834 --> 00:38:58.102
In the US, for instance,

00:38:58.102 --> 00:39:00.404
our mayonnaise contains egg yolk,

00:39:00.404 --> 00:39:02.340
as does most American mayo.

00:39:02.340 --> 00:39:05.142
Thanks to the FAQ page on
the McDonald's India website,

00:39:05.142 --> 00:39:07.511
we found out that the
mayonnaise is eggless,

00:39:07.511 --> 00:39:08.879
along with all of the other sauces

00:39:08.879 --> 00:39:10.548
except for the tartar sauce.

00:39:10.548 --> 00:39:13.250
When people describe things
as vegetarian here in India,

00:39:13.250 --> 00:39:15.753
they typically mean it
doesn't contain egg.

