Not to be confused with,
what, Canadian salsa?

00:47:49.766 --> 00:47:50.767
This is actually the same burrito

00:47:50.767 --> 00:47:53.370
from the US-UK thing we
shot over a year ago. So.

00:47:53.370 --> 00:47:55.739
Let's go on to these
breakfast sandwiches here.

00:47:55.739 --> 00:47:57.708
Japan does have the McGriddles,

00:47:57.708 --> 00:47:59.109
which are a favorite of mine,

00:47:59.109 --> 00:48:01.678
so unfortunately we will not
be talking about those today.

00:48:01.678 --> 00:48:02.813
Sad face.

00:48:02.813 --> 00:48:04.381
I love you, McGriddles.

00:48:04.381 --> 00:48:05.816
So, what they don't have,

00:48:05.816 --> 00:48:07.584
and also the UK did not have,

00:48:07.584 --> 00:48:10.153
were our breakfast biscuit sandwiches.

00:48:10.153 --> 00:48:11.989
I don't know how to describe a biscuit,

00:48:11.989 --> 00:48:14.992
other than it's dry,

00:48:14.992 --> 00:48:16.260
it's baked.

00:48:16.260 --> 00:48:17.895
Maybe they're made with cornmeal?

00:48:17.895 --> 00:48:18.762
According to the internet,

00:48:18.762 --> 00:48:21.031
this is not a scone, so there you go.

00:48:21.031 --> 00:48:22.966
Sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:48:22.966 --> 00:48:24.468
Our egg is like

00:48:24.468 --> 00:48:28.505
this fluffy, folded scrambled-egg egg.

00:48:28.505 --> 00:48:30.007
So theirs are, like, sunny-side up?

00:48:30.007 --> 00:48:31.041
Ours are scrambled.

00:48:31.041 --> 00:48:32.709
I can tell this was folded over.

00:48:32.709 --> 00:48:34.311
You can see the fold lines there.

00:48:34.311 --> 00:48:35.913
This is how we do it in the US.

00:48:35.913 --> 00:48:37.080
Bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:48:37.080 --> 00:48:39.116
Is there a better breakfast
combination in the world?

00:48:39.116 --> 00:48:40.117
I don't think there is.

00:48:40.117 --> 00:48:41.985
Then they just have a sausage,

00:48:41.985 --> 00:48:42.886
no egg, no cheese,

00:48:42.886 --> 00:48:44.888
just sausage and biscuit.

00:48:44.888 --> 00:48:46.456
We have regular-sized hotcakes,

00:48:46.456 --> 00:48:49.359
and we have a hotcake-and-sausage combo.

00:48:49.359 --> 00:48:52.529
And, of course, comes with syrup

00:48:52.529 --> 00:48:54.831
and butter.

00:48:57.034 --> 00:48:59.036
Very natural pose.

00:48:59.036 --> 00:49:01.038
Very natural feeling right now.

00:49:01.038 --> 00:49:05.142
♪ Always up for a pour, yes! ♪

00:49:06.276 --> 00:49:08.645
Breakfast is served.

00:49:08.645 --> 00:49:09.546
Oatmeal.

00:49:09.546 --> 00:49:11.248
On the side, to be mixed in,

00:49:11.248 --> 00:49:12.549
cranberries and raisins

00:49:12.549 --> 00:49:13.884
and

00:49:13.884 --> 00:49:14.718
diced --

00:49:14.718 --> 00:49:15.552
oh!

00:49:17.321 --> 00:49:18.588
Diced apples.

00:49:18.588 --> 00:49:19.790
[slurps]

00:49:19.790 --> 00:49:23.327
And here we've got Mega Muffin.

00:49:23.327 --> 00:49:24.728
Pork patties.

00:49:24.728 --> 00:49:26.797
That's huge one.

00:49:26.797 --> 00:49:28.632
Mini pancakes.

00:49:28.632 --> 00:49:29.900
Oh, cute.

00:49:29.900 --> 00:49:32.636
It comes with apple cream sauce.

00:49:33.904 --> 00:49:36.273
Ooh.

00:49:37.674 --> 00:49:40.377
Ooh, this is perfect for breakfast.

00:49:40.377 --> 00:49:41.712
I would get it.

00:49:41.712 --> 00:49:44.581
Bacon egg McSandwich.

00:49:44.581 --> 00:49:47.150
So, it's got bacon

00:49:47.150 --> 00:49:48.618
and round egg

00:49:48.618 --> 00:49:50.287
and cheddar cheese.

00:49:50.287 --> 00:49:51.355
That's it.

00:49:51.355 --> 00:49:53.724
And you might be surprised,

00:49:53.724 --> 00:49:55.826
we've got Filet-O-Fish.

00:49:55.826 --> 00:49:57.928
Ta-da!

00:49:57.928 --> 00:50:00.564
So, Filet-O-Fish is on the breakfast menu.

00:50:00.564 --> 00:50:02.599
I guess Japanese people tend to

00:50:02.599 --> 00:50:04.801
eat fish for breakfast.

00:50:04.801 --> 00:50:06.336
Three exclusive burgers here in the US

00:50:06.336 --> 00:50:09.639
are variations on the
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:50:09.639 --> 00:50:11.441
Yes, we've all seen "Pulp Fiction,"

00:50:11.441 --> 00:50:13.343
we know about the whole
Quarter Pounder thing.

00:50:13.343 --> 00:50:14.845
Does not exist outside of the US,

00:50:14.845 --> 00:50:15.712
I don't think.

00:50:15.712 --> 00:50:17.180
So, probably why they don't have

00:50:17.180 --> 00:50:18.982
Quarter Pounders in Japan.

00:50:18.982 --> 00:50:20.984
The classic Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:50:20.984 --> 00:50:21.985
Look at this guy.

00:50:21.985 --> 00:50:25.389
I mean, this was maybe my
go-to one for a decade.

00:50:25.389 --> 00:50:28.158
The Quarter Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:50:28.158 --> 00:50:29.426
I don't know.

00:50:29.426 --> 00:50:31.194
I feel like this is
pretty close to a Whopper.

00:50:31.194 --> 00:50:32.462
I'm not a big Whopper guy,

00:50:32.462 --> 00:50:33.663
but there you go,

00:50:33.663 --> 00:50:36.099
a deluxe Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:50:36.099 --> 00:50:37.868
The double Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:50:37.868 --> 00:50:39.970
Look at the size of this thing!

00:50:39.970 --> 00:50:42.439
Yes, sir.

00:50:42.439 --> 00:50:45.008
Japan's exclusive burgers.

00:50:45.008 --> 00:50:46.777
Teriyaki McBurger,

00:50:46.777 --> 00:50:50.080
which is my most favorite one.

00:50:50.080 --> 00:50:53.450
My body is made of McTeriyaki burger.

00:50:55.919 --> 00:50:58.755
[angelic singing]

00:51:01.224 --> 00:51:03.427
So, it's got mayo right there,

00:51:03.427 --> 00:51:05.228
and lettuce, pork patties,

00:51:05.228 --> 00:51:07.464
dip it into delicious teriyaki sauce,

00:51:07.464 --> 00:51:10.667
and it's covering whole
pork patties perfectly.

00:51:10.667 --> 00:51:14.604
Joe, when you come to
Japan, please try this.

00:51:14.604 --> 00:51:17.274
You will thank me later.

00:51:17.274 --> 00:51:19.009
Everything that they have

00:51:19.009 --> 00:51:21.745
looks so good and sounds so good.

00:51:21.745 --> 00:51:23.880
Man, when I go to Tokyo,

00:51:23.880 --> 00:51:25.882
first stop, I'm going to McDonald's.

00:51:25.882 --> 00:51:28.752
Sushi, ramen, get it out of my face.

00:51:28.752 --> 00:51:30.320
I want the teriyaki burger.

00:51:30.320 --> 00:51:32.189
That's the first thing I'm
getting when I get there.

00:51:33.190 --> 00:51:34.424
Mm!

00:51:34.424 --> 00:51:36.493
I'm getting full, actually.

00:51:36.493 --> 00:51:37.461
[laughs]

00:51:39.262 --> 00:51:41.198
Slow down, George. We got
a lot of food to cover.

00:51:45.068 --> 00:51:48.638
[dance music]

00:51:48.638 --> 00:51:50.474
All right, so we've got

00:51:50.474 --> 00:51:53.276
bacon lettuce burger right here.

00:51:53.276 --> 00:51:54.744
It looks sad.

00:51:56.246 --> 00:51:58.181
Egg cheeseburger,

00:51:58.181 --> 00:52:01.084
but we also call it Eguchi.

00:52:01.084 --> 00:52:04.554
Eguchi is an abbreviation
for egg cheeseburger.

00:52:04.554 --> 00:52:07.290
Japanese people love abbreviation.

00:52:07.290 --> 00:52:11.094
It's got ketchup and pickle, round egg,

00:52:11.094 --> 00:52:13.864
and cheddar cheese and beef patties.

00:52:13.864 --> 00:52:14.731
Next one.

00:52:14.731 --> 00:52:16.867
Spicy beef burger.

00:52:16.867 --> 00:52:18.368
Ooh, look at this!

00:52:18.368 --> 00:52:19.769
Oh, it looks so spicy!

00:52:19.769 --> 00:52:21.938
It has spicy mayo or something like that.

00:52:21.938 --> 00:52:26.409
So, here we've got Samurai Mac.

00:52:26.409 --> 00:52:28.011
Samurai!

00:52:28.011 --> 00:52:29.846
Samurai Mac?

00:52:29.846 --> 00:52:32.649
Yo, that sounds awesome.

00:52:32.649 --> 00:52:33.917
And this blue one

00:52:33.917 --> 00:52:37.821
is called roasted soy
sauce double thick beef.

00:52:37.821 --> 00:52:40.524
We've got roasted soy sauce

00:52:40.524 --> 00:52:42.592
bacon tomato thick beef.

00:52:42.592 --> 00:52:44.361
So if you want a little bit more, like,

00:52:44.361 --> 00:52:46.763
healthy veggies,

00:52:46.763 --> 00:52:47.898
go for it.

00:52:47.898 --> 00:52:49.232
Uh, yeah, George, I don't know if that

00:52:49.232 --> 00:52:50.433
makes that much healthier there

00:52:50.433 --> 00:52:53.136
'cause it also has twice
as much meat and cheese.

00:52:53.136 --> 00:52:54.938
If you're looking to be healthy
at a McDonald's in Japan,

00:52:54.938 --> 00:52:56.640
I'd stick with the vegetable juice.

00:52:56.640 --> 00:52:59.543
And this one right here is called

00:52:59.543 --> 00:53:01.545
Teriyaki chicken Filet-O.

00:53:01.545 --> 00:53:04.147
Wow. So much sauce.

00:53:04.147 --> 00:53:07.184
So, next one, we've got ebi Filet-O.

00:53:07.184 --> 00:53:08.251
Ebi means shrimp,

00:53:08.251 --> 00:53:10.453
so it's a shrimp Filet-O.

00:53:10.453 --> 00:53:12.822
Oh, yeah. It's got aurora sauce.

00:53:12.822 --> 00:53:16.760
Aurora sauce is like
ketchup and mayonnaise.

00:53:16.760 --> 00:53:18.695
So, it's got a lot of shrimp in there.

00:53:21.064 --> 00:53:22.265
Mm!

00:53:22.265 --> 00:53:24.367
So good. So good.

00:53:24.367 --> 00:53:25.602
In the US, we have about

00:53:25.602 --> 00:53:29.406
four exclusive chicken
sandwiches specifically.

00:53:29.406 --> 00:53:30.574
I didn't see this on the menu,

00:53:30.574 --> 00:53:33.476
but apparently you guys
don't have a McChicken,

00:53:33.476 --> 00:53:36.780
which is just chicken sandwich.

00:53:36.780 --> 00:53:39.416
Regular bun, mayo,

00:53:39.416 --> 00:53:40.217
chicken.

00:53:41.384 --> 00:53:42.352
Yeah.

00:53:42.352 --> 00:53:43.620
We also have,

00:53:43.620 --> 00:53:46.356
check this out, spicy McChicken.

00:53:47.224 --> 00:53:48.225
So pretty much the same McChicken,

00:53:48.225 --> 00:53:49.426
but they put spicy coating

00:53:49.426 --> 00:53:51.494
on the breading on the chicken.

00:53:51.494 --> 00:53:54.397
Every fast-food chain in America right now

00:53:54.397 --> 00:53:55.265
is having what we're calling

00:53:55.265 --> 00:53:57.000
the fried-chicken-sandwich wars.

00:53:57.000 --> 00:54:00.470
Popeyes, Burger King,
of course McDonald's,

00:54:00.470 --> 00:54:02.606
all of them are at this arms race

00:54:02.606 --> 00:54:03.873
to have the best chicken sandwich.

00:54:03.873 --> 00:54:05.909
I think 'cause Chick-fil-A
has edged everyone out.

00:54:05.909 --> 00:54:09.145
These are the three that
are currently available.

00:54:09.145 --> 00:54:10.780
I don't know for how long.

00:54:10.780 --> 00:54:12.215
You have the crispy chicken sandwich.

00:54:12.215 --> 00:54:14.417
I think it's a brioche bun,

00:54:14.417 --> 00:54:17.787
pickles, and no sauce,
which I think is strange.

00:54:17.787 --> 00:54:18.955
So, like, the whole flavor

00:54:18.955 --> 00:54:20.690
is just the chicken.

00:54:20.690 --> 00:54:23.593
Spicy chicken sandwich.

00:54:23.593 --> 00:54:24.694
Same deal,

00:54:24.694 --> 00:54:28.965
but, of course, spicy sauce.

00:54:28.965 --> 00:54:32.135
And the spicy chicken deluxe,

00:54:32.135 --> 00:54:33.803
which, to George's point,

00:54:33.803 --> 00:54:35.238
has more vegetables on it.

00:54:35.238 --> 00:54:38.074
You know, to be healthier.

00:54:38.074 --> 00:54:40.443
OK, so when it comes to side menus,

00:54:40.443 --> 00:54:44.180
we've got Shaka Shaka Chicken,

00:54:44.180 --> 00:54:45.548
and we have

00:54:45.548 --> 00:54:46.683
two fla --
[thunder rumbles]

00:54:46.683 --> 00:54:47.517
oh!

00:54:47.517 --> 00:54:48.885
Two flavors.

00:54:48.885 --> 00:54:52.522
Can you hear that?
Thunder, thunder, thunder!

00:54:52.522 --> 00:54:54.824
'Cause it's rainy season in Japan.

00:54:54.824 --> 00:54:57.794
It's the sunny season here
in Southern California.

00:54:57.794 --> 00:55:00.397
And here is red pepper.

00:55:00.397 --> 00:55:02.632
And this one is cheddar cheese.

00:55:02.632 --> 00:55:05.802
[thundering]

00:55:05.802 --> 00:55:07.637
Thunder, stop!

00:55:07.637 --> 00:55:08.938
So, all you have to do is just

00:55:08.938 --> 00:55:11.141
put the powder into the bag

00:55:11.141 --> 00:55:12.942
and shake it.

00:55:12.942 --> 00:55:15.712
[paper rattling]

00:55:17.213 --> 00:55:19.783
And the powder should be covering

00:55:19.783 --> 00:55:21.785
the whole Shaka Chicken.
[thundering]

00:55:21.785 --> 00:55:23.887
Ooh, big one!

00:55:23.887 --> 00:55:25.188
Like this.

00:55:29.693 --> 00:55:32.062
This I've seen before. This I want.

00:55:32.062 --> 00:55:34.264
That's the thing I want the
most at a Japanese McDonald's.

00:55:34.264 --> 00:55:36.499
US McDonald's, we have the bags,

00:55:36.499 --> 00:55:38.101
we have the chicken.

00:55:38.101 --> 00:55:41.304
Just get the spice packets. Throw it in.

00:55:41.304 --> 00:55:43.940
George: We've got side salad,

00:55:43.940 --> 00:55:48.078
and it comes with this
roasted sesame dressing.

00:55:48.078 --> 00:55:49.412
Let's go!

00:55:49.412 --> 00:55:51.881
Ooh.

00:55:51.881 --> 00:55:53.083
That was cool.

00:55:53.083 --> 00:55:54.517
Now put it all in the garbage.

00:55:54.517 --> 00:55:57.420
We've got edamame and corn.

00:55:58.288 --> 00:55:59.723
Yogurt,

00:55:59.723 --> 00:56:02.325
and there's cow,

00:56:02.325 --> 00:56:03.426
cow.

00:56:03.426 --> 00:56:04.794
Exclusive sauces.

00:56:04.794 --> 00:56:06.429
It's sauce talk time.

00:56:06.429 --> 00:56:07.964
Sauce Talk.

00:56:07.964 --> 00:56:10.567
We have sweet 'n sour sauce.

00:56:10.567 --> 00:56:12.068
They gave me

00:56:12.068 --> 00:56:13.670
hot mustard.

00:56:13.670 --> 00:56:15.372
This was supposed to be honey mustard.

00:56:15.372 --> 00:56:16.539
You guys have hot mustard?

00:56:16.539 --> 00:56:17.941
I know you don't have honey mustard.

00:56:17.941 --> 00:56:19.709
Of course, ranch.

00:56:20.810 --> 00:56:23.947
Ooh, spicy Buffalo.

00:56:23.947 --> 00:56:25.048
Now, these might be promotions

00:56:25.048 --> 00:56:28.752
'cause of that singing group BTS,

00:56:28.752 --> 00:56:30.887
but we have right now a

00:56:30.887 --> 00:56:33.590
Cajun sauce and a sweet chili sauce.

00:56:33.590 --> 00:56:37.060
This sauce is fantastic.

00:56:37.060 --> 00:56:39.129
This is the sauce. This
has to stay on the menu.

00:56:39.129 --> 00:56:41.631
So, these two are new ones.

00:56:41.631 --> 00:56:44.134
This one right here is

00:56:44.134 --> 00:56:46.236
soy sauce, best sauce.

00:56:49.038 --> 00:56:51.174
Man. This is fantastic!

00:56:51.174 --> 00:56:52.175
Good job!

00:56:52.175 --> 00:56:54.110
Very good taste.

00:56:54.110 --> 00:56:56.613
So, this one right here is called

00:56:56.613 --> 00:56:58.248
Louisiana hot sauce.

00:56:58.248 --> 00:57:01.818
Ooh, it does look like very spicy one.

00:57:05.755 --> 00:57:07.690
This is not spicy at all.

00:57:07.690 --> 00:57:11.528
Actually, we were supposed
to have bai burger options,

00:57:11.528 --> 00:57:14.731
but unfortunately you can
only get them from 5:30 p.m.

00:57:14.731 --> 00:57:17.167
But let me explain what bai burger is.

00:57:17.167 --> 00:57:20.136
Bai simply means double in Japanese.

00:57:20.136 --> 00:57:22.172
So if you order a normal Big Mac,

00:57:22.172 --> 00:57:23.973
it has two beef patties, right?

00:57:23.973 --> 00:57:26.276
But if you order bai Big Mac,

00:57:26.276 --> 00:57:27.777
it has four beef patties.

00:57:27.777 --> 00:57:30.713
But not only Big Mac, but all burgers

00:57:30.713 --> 00:57:32.982
adopts the bai burger options.

00:57:32.982 --> 00:57:33.817
That's funny.

00:57:33.817 --> 00:57:35.752
You can only get double
the meat after 5:30,

00:57:35.752 --> 00:57:36.719
that's really funny.

00:57:36.719 --> 00:57:39.456
That would not stand
in this country at all.

00:57:39.456 --> 00:57:41.624
People would lose their minds.

00:57:41.624 --> 00:57:43.827
Four patties?

00:57:43.827 --> 00:57:45.361
On a Big Mac?

00:57:45.361 --> 00:57:46.696
So after shooting this video,

00:57:46.696 --> 00:57:49.065
I'm going to order bai Big Mac.

00:57:49.065 --> 00:57:51.634
And then bye-bye, health.

00:57:51.634 --> 00:57:53.403
You ain't gotta tell me, George!

00:57:53.403 --> 00:57:54.537
Bye, health!

00:57:57.607 --> 00:57:58.842
All right, here are all the ingredients

00:57:58.842 --> 00:58:00.477
for a US Big Mac.

00:58:00.477 --> 00:58:01.311
Oh, God.

00:58:01.311 --> 00:58:02.545
The bun. It has:

00:58:02.545 --> 00:58:04.047
enriched flour, which is wheat flour,

00:58:04.047 --> 00:58:06.516
[fast-forwarding]

00:58:06.516 --> 00:58:08.885
vinegar, and contains wheat.

00:58:08.885 --> 00:58:09.953
On to the beef patty.

00:58:09.953 --> 00:58:13.056
100% pure USDA inspected beef,

00:58:13.056 --> 00:58:14.958
no fillers, no extenders!

00:58:14.958 --> 00:58:16.526
Prepared on the grill with seasoning,

00:58:16.526 --> 00:58:17.894
salt and black pepper.

00:58:17.894 --> 00:58:19.596
There you go. There you go.

00:58:19.596 --> 00:58:21.064
Try the lettuce ingredients,

00:58:21.064 --> 00:58:22.098
lettuce.

00:58:22.098 --> 00:58:23.099
Nice.

00:58:23.099 --> 00:58:24.868
The Big Mac sauce ingredients.

00:58:24.868 --> 00:58:26.269
Soybean oil,

00:58:26.269 --> 00:58:29.005
[fast-forwarding]

00:58:29.005 --> 00:58:32.542
extractives of paprika, soy lecithin.

00:58:32.542 --> 00:58:33.409
[burps]

00:58:33.409 --> 00:58:35.044
The pickle slice ingredients.

00:58:35.044 --> 00:58:36.913
Cucumbers, water, distilled vinegar,

00:58:36.913 --> 00:58:39.549
salt, calcium chloride, alum,

00:58:39.549 --> 00:58:41.584
potassium sorbate as a preservative,

00:58:41.584 --> 00:58:43.586
natural flavors, polysorbate 80,

00:58:43.586 --> 00:58:45.722
extractives of turmeric for color.

00:58:45.722 --> 00:58:46.823
Onion ingredients.

00:58:46.823 --> 00:58:47.657
Onions.

00:58:47.657 --> 00:58:48.691
There you go.

00:58:48.691 --> 00:58:50.260
A few things I want to note.

00:58:50.260 --> 00:58:53.096
Alum is used to dissolve steel.

00:58:53.096 --> 00:58:57.166
Polysorbate 80 has been linked
to colon cancer in mice.

00:58:57.166 --> 00:58:58.535
Cue the dancing mice.

00:58:58.535 --> 00:59:02.305
[dance music]

00:59:02.305 --> 00:59:05.174
And caramel color is on
California's list of chemicals

00:59:05.174 --> 00:59:08.411
that may cause cancer and
reproductive toxicity,

00:59:08.411 --> 00:59:09.579
good God.

00:59:09.579 --> 00:59:10.580
Counterpoint.

00:59:10.580 --> 00:59:12.282
They all taste fantastic.

00:59:12.282 --> 00:59:14.584
So, McDonald's Japan doesn't disclose

00:59:14.584 --> 00:59:16.619
their ingredients in the Big Mac.

00:59:16.619 --> 00:59:20.924
However, they do tell us where
the ingredients come from.

00:59:20.924 --> 00:59:22.825
If you order a Big Mac in Japan,

00:59:22.825 --> 00:59:26.696
you'll eat beef from
Australia or New Zealand;

00:59:26.696 --> 00:59:30.199
buns made from wheat
imported from the USA,

00:59:30.199 --> 00:59:32.402
Canada, and Australia;

00:59:32.402 --> 00:59:35.805
and pickles made from
cucumbers grown in Turkey,

00:59:35.805 --> 00:59:38.041
Sri Lanka, or India;

00:59:38.041 --> 00:59:41.611
onions grown in the USA or India;

00:59:41.611 --> 00:59:44.213
sliced cheddar cheese made in New Zealand,

00:59:44.213 --> 00:59:47.517
Australia, the USA, or Japan;

00:59:47.517 --> 00:59:49.586
and lettuce grown in Japan,

00:59:49.586 --> 00:59:53.289
Taiwan, the USA, or Malaysia.

00:59:53.289 --> 00:59:56.326
The only ingredients that come from Japan

00:59:56.326 --> 00:59:58.628
are the cheese and the lettuce.

00:59:58.628 --> 01:00:01.831
And even then, McDonald's
still imports some lettuce

01:00:01.831 --> 01:00:04.067
and cheese from other countries.

01:00:04.067 --> 01:00:07.003
So this is a very international burger.

01:00:07.904 --> 01:00:09.205
Thank you, world!

01:00:12.342 --> 01:00:15.912
In Japan, our Big Mac is 525 calories

01:00:15.912 --> 01:00:18.481
and 28.3 grams of fat

01:00:18.481 --> 01:00:22.018
and 1,007 milligrams of sodium

01:00:22.018 --> 01:00:25.154
and 41.8 grams of carbs

01:00:25.154 --> 01:00:27.757
and 26 grams of protein.

01:00:27.757 --> 01:00:31.194
In the US, our Big Mac is 550 calories,

01:00:31.194 --> 01:00:32.228
30 grams of fat,

01:00:32.228 --> 01:00:34.464
1,010 milligrams of sodium,

01:00:34.464 --> 01:00:35.798
45 grams of carbs,

01:00:35.798 --> 01:00:38.368
and 25 grams of protein.

01:00:38.368 --> 01:00:39.902
So the US has a slight increase

01:00:39.902 --> 01:00:42.171
on everything except protein.

01:00:42.171 --> 01:00:44.540
So, in Japan, our five-piece nuggets

01:00:44.540 --> 01:00:46.709
is 270 calories

01:00:46.709 --> 01:00:49.379
and 17.2 grams of fat

01:00:49.379 --> 01:00:52.281
and 506 milligrams of sodium

01:00:52.281 --> 01:00:55.184
and 13.1 grams of carbs

01:00:55.184 --> 01:00:58.221
and 15.8 grams of protein.

01:00:58.221 --> 01:01:01.224
Broken down, each nugget is 54 calories.

01:01:01.224 --> 01:01:02.759
We don't have a five-piece here in the US,

01:01:02.759 --> 01:01:04.160
but we do have this, a 10-piece.

01:01:04.160 --> 01:01:05.795
Let's get those stats on the screen.

01:01:05.795 --> 01:01:07.330
Go ahead and divide everything by two,

01:01:07.330 --> 01:01:10.166
and, yes, now we have the
stats for a five-piece.

01:01:10.166 --> 01:01:11.200
Pretty smart, eh?

01:01:11.200 --> 01:01:13.770
If we want to divide all
that by, I think, five,

01:01:13.770 --> 01:01:16.439
you'll get the stats for one nugget.

01:01:16.439 --> 01:01:18.675
[sighs] This is so exhausting.

01:01:18.675 --> 01:01:20.810
In Japan, if you order a Big Mac meal

01:01:20.810 --> 01:01:24.247
with large fries and a
medium chocolate shake,

01:01:24.247 --> 01:01:27.950
the grand total will be 1,405 calories.

01:01:27.950 --> 01:01:29.952
And in the US, adding medium fries

01:01:29.952 --> 01:01:31.921
and a medium chocolate shake to a Big Mac,

01:01:31.921 --> 01:01:35.291
the grand total is 1,660 calories.

01:01:35.291 --> 01:01:39.796
And that is a calorie increase of 18.14%.

01:01:39.796 --> 01:01:41.564
If you're wondering why
we're using a large fry

01:01:41.564 --> 01:01:43.166
but a medium chocolate shake,

01:01:43.166 --> 01:01:44.534
it turns out that in Japan,

01:01:44.534 --> 01:01:47.103
you can't get a large chocolate shake.

01:01:47.103 --> 01:01:48.805
They'll only sell it to you in medium.

01:01:48.805 --> 01:01:49.839
I'm assuming because they don't want you

01:01:49.839 --> 01:01:51.674
eating that much ice cream.

01:01:52.241 --> 01:01:53.876
Tianran: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:01:53.876 --> 01:01:55.445
we wanted to find all the differences

01:01:55.445 --> 01:01:58.247
between McDonald's in the US and China.

01:01:58.247 --> 01:02:00.216
This is "Food Wars."

01:02:01.584 --> 01:02:04.420
New season, USA versus China.

01:02:04.420 --> 01:02:06.222
I'm so excited for you guys to see this

01:02:06.222 --> 01:02:09.292
and to meet our new cohost, Tianran.

01:02:09.292 --> 01:02:11.728
USA versus China, let's go.

01:02:13.830 --> 01:02:16.999
Drinks from McDonald's in
China come in three sizes,

01:02:16.999 --> 01:02:19.902
small, medium, and big.

01:02:19.902 --> 01:02:24.073
But for some reason the
medium is 444 milliliters,

01:02:24.073 --> 01:02:28.411
which in Chinese basically
just means die, die, die,

01:02:28.411 --> 01:02:29.579
which is just super unlucky,

01:02:29.579 --> 01:02:31.414
so I guess they really
want you to either get

01:02:31.414 --> 01:02:33.182
the large or the small.

01:02:33.182 --> 01:02:35.785
The drinks at a US
McDonald's come four sizes,

01:02:35.785 --> 01:02:37.687
the extra small, where'd it go?

01:02:37.687 --> 01:02:38.855
Sorry, they forgot it.

01:02:38.855 --> 01:02:42.091
The small, the medium, and the large.

01:02:42.091 --> 01:02:45.595
Our large is 80.9% bigger

01:02:45.595 --> 01:02:47.630
than China's largest soda.

01:02:47.630 --> 01:02:49.232
Let's see if that's true.

01:02:49.232 --> 01:02:51.067
Bound to be a little bit in the lid.

01:02:54.570 --> 01:02:56.472
That is blasphemous!

01:02:56.472 --> 01:02:59.275
Shame these people. Shame this clown.

01:02:59.275 --> 01:03:01.811
Some of you over the past several years

01:03:01.811 --> 01:03:03.513
have said something to the tune of,

01:03:03.513 --> 01:03:04.947
it doesn't count or it's wrong

01:03:04.947 --> 01:03:07.216
because we add the ice, or
we keep the ice in there,

01:03:07.216 --> 01:03:08.384
and that isn't a true measurement,

01:03:08.384 --> 01:03:10.486
which I don't believe, but fine.

01:03:10.486 --> 01:03:11.954
For the first time ever,

01:03:11.954 --> 01:03:13.956
I want to measure this without the ice.

01:03:13.956 --> 01:03:16.659
I'm solving this once and for all.

01:03:16.659 --> 01:03:19.028
So, right away you get even less soda.

01:03:19.028 --> 01:03:23.566
Let's get this up to
exactly 32 fluid ounces.

01:03:23.566 --> 01:03:25.268
32 ounces of Coca-Cola

01:03:25.268 --> 01:03:29.639
in the supposed 32-ounce McDonald's cup.

01:03:29.639 --> 01:03:31.440
I'm so sick of this.

01:03:31.440 --> 01:03:35.278
Why are they saying 32 fluid ounces?

01:03:35.278 --> 01:03:39.248
Look! Just say 30 or 31. It's fine.

01:03:39.248 --> 01:03:40.483
Your move, McDonald's.

01:03:40.483 --> 01:03:42.518
Our fries come in three sizes:

01:03:42.518 --> 01:03:44.654
small, medium, and large.

01:03:44.654 --> 01:03:46.589
American fries come in three sizes:

01:03:46.589 --> 01:03:49.025
small, medium, and large.

01:03:49.025 --> 01:03:51.494
We will now weigh our largest fry.

01:03:52.528 --> 01:03:53.763
So, what about McNuggets?

01:03:53.763 --> 01:03:55.598
Here in China, you can only get them

01:03:55.598 --> 01:03:58.067
as an order of five or 10,

01:03:58.067 --> 01:04:00.770
which is really just two portions of five.

01:04:00.770 --> 01:04:02.505
That's cute, China. Real cute.

01:04:02.505 --> 01:04:06.175
Here in the US, we have way
many more nugget options.

01:04:06.175 --> 01:04:08.177
Four-piece, for your infant,

01:04:08.177 --> 01:04:10.813
six-piece, 10-piece, 20-piece,

01:04:10.813 --> 01:04:13.816
and our largest, the 40-piece.

01:04:13.816 --> 01:04:16.219
All the mathheads watching
will be quick to point out

01:04:16.219 --> 01:04:21.224
that this is 300% of
China's largest portion.

01:04:23.426 --> 01:04:26.395
So, here are all the McDonald's
menu items from China

01:04:26.395 --> 01:04:28.197
that you won't find in the US.

01:04:28.197 --> 01:04:30.633
Here are all the
McDonald's items in the US

01:04:30.633 --> 01:04:31.934
you won't find in China.

01:04:31.934 --> 01:04:33.803
Oh, my God, I've been
staring at this for so long.

01:04:33.803 --> 01:04:35.972
This is incredible. Check out the back!

01:04:35.972 --> 01:04:38.975
It's an origami apple! This is the best.

01:04:38.975 --> 01:04:40.276
Let's see what we got.

01:04:40.276 --> 01:04:42.712
A hamburger, mini fries,

01:04:42.712 --> 01:04:45.848
a drink, a corn cup.

01:04:45.848 --> 01:04:48.784
[gasps] Dun-dun-dun!

01:04:48.784 --> 01:04:50.253
Po!

01:04:50.253 --> 01:04:53.990
Oh, my God, this is way
better than the Hamburglar.

01:04:53.990 --> 01:04:56.792
What? do I have to build Po as well?

01:04:56.792 --> 01:05:00.129
This is -- [laughs] I'm too old for this.

01:05:00.129 --> 01:05:01.864
Anyway, if you don't want a hamburger,

01:05:01.864 --> 01:05:04.800
you can also change this
out for a fish fillet

01:05:04.800 --> 01:05:07.103
or for four pieces of nuggets.

01:05:07.103 --> 01:05:11.908
You can also get the corn cup
changed out for apple slices,

01:05:11.908 --> 01:05:14.610
but they will cost you 1 kuai extra.

01:05:15.745 --> 01:05:19.715
And with the juice, you can
have either apple juice,

01:05:19.715 --> 01:05:21.684
milk, or water.

01:05:21.684 --> 01:05:25.254
So only healthy options
here in China's McDonald's.

01:05:25.254 --> 01:05:26.689
OK, now on to the toy.

01:05:26.689 --> 01:05:28.357
So, this is going to take
a while. Give me a second.

01:05:28.357 --> 01:05:29.191
Ugh.

01:05:29.191 --> 01:05:32.695
And then something flips
out from behind his groin.

01:05:32.695 --> 01:05:35.965
In here! It's coming together!

01:05:35.965 --> 01:05:38.267
Oh!

01:05:38.267 --> 01:05:40.569
It's a basketball hoop.

01:05:40.569 --> 01:05:43.606
Oh, my God, this is ingenuity at its best.

01:05:43.606 --> 01:05:45.408
Look, we can play hoops with this.

01:05:45.408 --> 01:05:47.410
Three, two, one!

01:05:47.410 --> 01:05:49.345
Whoa!

01:05:49.345 --> 01:05:52.949
I noticed that his Happy
Meal, even the box was a toy.

01:05:52.949 --> 01:05:55.651
In America, our Happy Meal box

01:05:55.651 --> 01:05:58.087
is another opportunity
for an advertisement.

01:05:58.087 --> 01:06:01.290
All-new season of "The Masked
Singer" on Fox. Check it out.

01:06:01.290 --> 01:06:04.193
Jesus, they're shameless. These kids.

01:06:04.193 --> 01:06:06.963
Remember before, the
extra-small fry? Found it.

01:06:06.963 --> 01:06:08.931
More nuggets, a four-piece.

01:06:08.931 --> 01:06:10.533
Apple slices.

01:06:10.533 --> 01:06:13.336
Our toy is decidedly not a puzzle.

01:06:13.336 --> 01:06:15.905
Remember when Kermit
the Frog was in there?

01:06:15.905 --> 01:06:17.173
That was weird.

01:06:17.173 --> 01:06:18.274
OK, what is this?

01:06:18.274 --> 01:06:20.443
Who? What celebrity was the fox?

01:06:20.443 --> 01:06:21.978
Oh, it was Wayne Brady.
OK, I've heard of him.

01:06:21.978 --> 01:06:24.046
What, is his head in here?

01:06:24.046 --> 01:06:25.514
Oddly enough, shows the stark difference

01:06:25.514 --> 01:06:26.782
between China and the US.

01:06:26.782 --> 01:06:28.517
Theirs has this puzzle to put together,

01:06:28.517 --> 01:06:30.386
ours is an ad for a TV show.

01:06:30.386 --> 01:06:33.656
[laughs and cries]

01:06:35.191 --> 01:06:38.661
OK, so these are our
exclusive beef burgers.

01:06:38.661 --> 01:06:42.131
Here in China, people mostly eat pork,

01:06:42.131 --> 01:06:43.566
so I think with the beef

01:06:43.566 --> 01:06:46.235
they've really had to
go the premium route,

01:06:46.235 --> 01:06:48.070
so you've got some
interesting combinations.

01:06:48.070 --> 01:06:51.874
This is the German sausage
double beef burger,

01:06:51.874 --> 01:06:54.677
but in Chinese the name is kind of like

01:06:54.677 --> 01:06:57.646
the "anti-vegetarian tyrant."

01:06:57.646 --> 01:07:00.950
So they've got some pretty
aggressive marketing for this.

01:07:00.950 --> 01:07:05.254
Imagine Terry Crews just
pulsing his pecks while he --

01:07:05.254 --> 01:07:06.655
what is that?

01:07:06.655 --> 01:07:07.790
Ugh.

01:07:07.790 --> 01:07:10.693
If this is what they
call a German sausage,

01:07:10.693 --> 01:07:13.062
then I think the Germans
will be very angry.

01:07:13.062 --> 01:07:16.399
Here we've got a BLT double beef burger.

01:07:18.234 --> 01:07:20.436
I'm so sad. What is this?

01:07:20.436 --> 01:07:21.971
This is like a BLT sandwich

01:07:21.971 --> 01:07:24.974
that's been sat at the bottom
of your bag for a week.

01:07:24.974 --> 01:07:26.542
I'm excited about these, though.

01:07:26.542 --> 01:07:31.013
These are the Angus
max thick beef burgers.

01:07:31.013 --> 01:07:33.916
Now, McDonald's have done
premium collaborations

01:07:33.916 --> 01:07:36.385
with Michelin-starred chefs in the past,

01:07:36.385 --> 01:07:39.922
and they even have these
really super-fancy packaging.

01:07:39.922 --> 01:07:43.059
Look at that. Double cheeseburger.

01:07:43.059 --> 01:07:47.430
Oh, wow! Look at that.

01:07:47.430 --> 01:07:50.066
The meat patty is thicker than my thumb.

01:07:50.066 --> 01:07:51.767
That's a proper burger.

01:07:51.767 --> 01:07:53.035
Mm.

01:07:53.035 --> 01:07:55.871
Well, it's very meaty. Incredibly cheesy.

01:07:55.871 --> 01:07:58.441
This is the double cheeseburger,
so I can understand that.

01:07:58.441 --> 01:08:00.176
For the vast majority of Chinese people,

01:08:00.176 --> 01:08:03.746
their understanding or
access to Western food

01:08:03.746 --> 01:08:05.714
may really come from
fast-food restaurants.

01:08:05.714 --> 01:08:09.218
So this is probably the
gourmet burger experience

01:08:09.218 --> 01:08:11.620
for the vast majority of
the Chinese population.

01:08:11.620 --> 01:08:15.357
In the US, you can get a
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

01:08:15.357 --> 01:08:17.726
What the heck? They gave us two tops?

01:08:17.726 --> 01:08:19.095
This is the special two-top

01:08:19.095 --> 01:08:20.629
Quarter Pounder with cheese, apparently.

01:08:20.629 --> 01:08:23.332
And we also have a double Quarter Pounder,

01:08:23.332 --> 01:08:24.934
if you want to increase the meat.

01:08:24.934 --> 01:08:26.702
If someone wants to get
their daily vegetables,

01:08:26.702 --> 01:08:29.105
here is the Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe.

01:08:29.105 --> 01:08:30.473
Swimming in mayonnaise.

01:08:30.473 --> 01:08:32.374
We have something in the United
States called the McDouble.

01:08:32.374 --> 01:08:35.077
If you want slightly less
cheese on a double cheeseburger,

01:08:35.077 --> 01:08:35.911
we got you covered.

01:08:35.911 --> 01:08:37.146
Quarter Pounder with bacon.

01:08:37.146 --> 01:08:38.547
Every once in a while, they
just take a Quarter Pounder

01:08:38.547 --> 01:08:39.515
and put bacon on it,

01:08:39.515 --> 01:08:41.717
and they repackage it for a celebrity.

01:08:41.717 --> 01:08:45.654
And these are our exclusive
chicken and fish options.

01:08:45.654 --> 01:08:46.989
So, I want to start you off with this,

01:08:46.989 --> 01:08:51.327
which has since become
McDonald's best spicy burger.

01:08:51.327 --> 01:08:54.296
This is the McSpicy chicken fillet.

01:08:54.296 --> 01:08:58.634
Apparently it's 1,000 SHU,

01:08:58.634 --> 01:09:00.536
which is a Scoville unit,

01:09:00.536 --> 01:09:03.906
and it's roughly equivalent
to the spiciness you get

01:09:03.906 --> 01:09:05.674
from a spicy and numbing hot pot,

01:09:05.674 --> 01:09:07.943
and those guys are pretty spicy.

01:09:07.943 --> 01:09:09.745
Mm. Oh, that's delicious.

01:09:09.745 --> 01:09:11.247
You don't feel the burn at first,

01:09:11.247 --> 01:09:13.482
and then it's like your tongue
slowly starts to wake up,

01:09:13.482 --> 01:09:15.417
and it's like a frog in a pot.

01:09:15.417 --> 01:09:17.887
It slowly starts to realize
it's being boiled alive,

01:09:17.887 --> 01:09:19.588
and by the end of this burger,

01:09:19.588 --> 01:09:20.756
you're going to want that Coke.

01:09:20.756 --> 01:09:25.361
Now, this is McDonald's
best-selling non-spicy burger,

01:09:25.361 --> 01:09:27.229
the grilled chicken sandwich,

01:09:27.229 --> 01:09:29.532
which supposedly has no growth hormones

01:09:29.532 --> 01:09:30.633
in their chicken feed.

01:09:32.101 --> 01:09:34.937
Very heavy on the black
pepper. Oh. Ooh, wow.

01:09:34.937 --> 01:09:36.005
I'm very excited about this.

01:09:36.005 --> 01:09:38.707
This is the McCrunch
chicken fillet burger,

01:09:38.707 --> 01:09:41.544
and in Chinese the name is "katsusui."

01:09:41.544 --> 01:09:43.846
It sounds like how it's supposed to taste.

01:09:43.846 --> 01:09:45.814
"Ka" is kind of like "crunchy,"

01:09:45.814 --> 01:09:47.750
and "tsu" is kind of like

01:09:47.750 --> 01:09:49.785
the juice kind of squirting out.

01:09:49.785 --> 01:09:54.290
So this should be both crunchy and juicy.

01:09:54.290 --> 01:09:58.060
Ooh, that looks like a much
better piece of chicken.

01:09:59.862 --> 01:10:01.797
Yes, yes.

01:10:01.797 --> 01:10:03.966
I didn't get the "ka,"

01:10:03.966 --> 01:10:06.001
probably because this has gone a bit cold,

01:10:06.001 --> 01:10:08.704
but look at that. It is juicy in there.

01:10:08.704 --> 01:10:11.974
OK, this is the
super-spicy chicken fillet.

01:10:11.974 --> 01:10:13.008
Look at this guy!

01:10:13.008 --> 01:10:15.511
You know this is going to
be super spicy. It's orange!

01:10:19.515 --> 01:10:21.850
It's not that spicy.

01:10:21.850 --> 01:10:24.019
[coughs] Ooh!

01:10:24.019 --> 01:10:26.388
It's not as -- oh!

01:10:26.388 --> 01:10:28.591
Oh, my God.

01:10:28.591 --> 01:10:29.625
Very tasty.

01:10:29.625 --> 01:10:32.695
Finish that, and it's

01:10:32.695 --> 01:10:34.330
to the hospital you go. Whew.

01:10:34.330 --> 01:10:38.901
And last but, in my opinion,
least, the double fish burger.

01:10:38.901 --> 01:10:41.337
Chicken sandwiches.

01:10:41.337 --> 01:10:43.505
There's something that is new-ish,

01:10:43.505 --> 01:10:45.307
the bacon ranch McCrispy.

01:10:46.542 --> 01:10:48.043
Hm.

01:10:48.043 --> 01:10:49.044
It's just OK.

01:10:49.044 --> 01:10:51.680
There's also a bacon
ranch deluxe McCrispy,

01:10:51.680 --> 01:10:53.215
where deluxe equals more vegetables.

01:10:53.215 --> 01:10:57.019
The McCrispy is something that
we ordered and they forgot.

01:10:57.019 --> 01:10:59.221
And then now, piling on the vegetables,

01:10:59.221 --> 01:11:01.156
you got the McCrispy deluxe.

01:11:01.156 --> 01:11:02.758
Spicy McCrispy.

01:11:02.758 --> 01:11:04.727
So they just rebranded the
crispy chicken sandwich

01:11:04.727 --> 01:11:06.195
to be the McCrispy?

01:11:07.129 --> 01:11:09.798
How spicy can this be?
This is not spicy at all.

01:11:13.969 --> 01:11:17.406
So, McDonald's China has one roll option,

01:11:17.406 --> 01:11:20.843
which is this crispy pork and

01:11:20.843 --> 01:11:23.379
pickled bamboo shoot wrap.

01:11:25.381 --> 01:11:26.915
Mm.

01:11:26.915 --> 01:11:28.150
That's tasty. It's nice and crunchy.

01:11:28.150 --> 01:11:31.420
Very spicy! [laughs] Wow.

01:11:32.855 --> 01:11:33.756
Mm.

01:11:33.756 --> 01:11:35.291
It's spicy. It's sour.

01:11:35.291 --> 01:11:38.193
Anything that has Sichuan peppercorn in it

01:11:38.193 --> 01:11:39.328
is just incredible.

01:11:39.328 --> 01:11:41.563
Here we've got the McSpicy wings,

01:11:41.563 --> 01:11:45.834
which come in portions of two, four,

01:11:45.834 --> 01:11:47.603
or nine.

01:11:47.603 --> 01:11:49.171
Straight up, I wish we had those wings.

01:11:49.171 --> 01:11:50.406
Those wings look really good.

01:11:50.406 --> 01:11:52.041
Also, I don't know if you've noticed,

01:11:52.041 --> 01:11:55.277
but the decoration here on the packet,

01:11:55.277 --> 01:11:56.278
this is a collaboration

01:11:56.278 --> 01:12:00.516
with a streetwear brand
called Clot, or C-L-O-T,

01:12:00.516 --> 01:12:03.752
and it uses traditional
Chinese aesthetics.

01:12:03.752 --> 01:12:05.988
So here you've got the lucky knot,

01:12:05.988 --> 01:12:09.625
which is sort of like a symbol
for good luck and longevity.

01:12:09.625 --> 01:12:10.793
As Chinese as it gets.

01:12:10.793 --> 01:12:14.463
And this is also the same
flavor as the McSpicy burger.

01:12:14.463 --> 01:12:17.333
I don't know if there's an
accurate translation for this.

01:12:17.333 --> 01:12:19.668
This is literally called

01:12:19.668 --> 01:12:23.072
"such a big chicken chop."

01:12:23.072 --> 01:12:27.176
It's about the same size as
my palm, a little bit bigger.

01:12:27.176 --> 01:12:28.877
The McCrispy chicken.

01:12:29.945 --> 01:12:32.181
Mm. Crispy, wow.

01:12:32.181 --> 01:12:33.716
Mm, yes!

01:12:33.716 --> 01:12:37.419
This is very special.

01:12:37.419 --> 01:12:39.455
We didn't think we'd be
able to get this today.

01:12:39.455 --> 01:12:41.123
This is the

01:12:41.123 --> 01:12:44.660
spicy lobster-flavored chicken tenders.

01:12:44.660 --> 01:12:46.762
The Chinese says "yao yao,"

01:12:46.762 --> 01:12:48.564
which means you have to shake it.

01:12:50.699 --> 01:12:52.735
Oh, let's try these babies.

01:12:52.735 --> 01:12:53.936
There was no need to shake it at all.

01:12:53.936 --> 01:12:55.738
There's no seasoning there at all.

01:12:55.738 --> 01:12:59.007
It's just literally chicken tenders.

01:13:00.376 --> 01:13:05.047
It's more of an aspiration
towards lobster, though.

01:13:05.047 --> 01:13:07.449
And we've got crinkle-cut fries.

01:13:07.449 --> 01:13:09.118
Oh, how I've missed you.

01:13:09.118 --> 01:13:11.720
Mm. Nothing beats a crinkle-cut fry.

01:13:11.720 --> 01:13:14.890
In China, we have a bunch
of different barrel options.

01:13:14.890 --> 01:13:19.228
For example, this one is
the Golden Arches bucket,

01:13:19.228 --> 01:13:21.196
which actually didn't come in a bucket,

01:13:21.196 --> 01:13:23.298
they just put everything into a box.

01:13:23.298 --> 01:13:26.168
The name actually is the
reason why we got this,

01:13:26.168 --> 01:13:28.771
because McDonald's in China

01:13:28.771 --> 01:13:31.840
has officially renamed to Jingongmen,

01:13:31.840 --> 01:13:33.876
which literally translates
as Golden Arches,

01:13:33.876 --> 01:13:36.845
and when they did that
they caught a lot of flak.

01:13:36.845 --> 01:13:38.380
Everybody started laughing at them.

01:13:38.380 --> 01:13:41.216
Nobody calls them the
Golden Arches in Chinese.

01:13:41.216 --> 01:13:42.751
It's just McDonald's.

01:13:42.751 --> 01:13:46.188
But legally they are now
known as the Golden Arches.

01:13:46.188 --> 01:13:49.725
Featuring sauces, you know
what that means, Yuelei.

01:13:49.725 --> 01:13:51.293
Sauce talk.

01:13:51.293 --> 01:13:54.062
Here are all of our exclusive sauces.

01:13:54.062 --> 01:13:55.964
Garlic chili.

01:13:55.964 --> 01:13:57.032
That's pretty much it.

01:13:57.032 --> 01:13:58.700
Oh, and no Sichuan sauce, either.

01:13:58.700 --> 01:13:59.868
That's an American invention,

01:13:59.868 --> 01:14:01.403
just like General Tso's chicken.

01:14:01.403 --> 01:14:04.373
But here in China, you
don't really get sauces

01:14:04.373 --> 01:14:07.209
unless you ask for them.
They come with the nuggets.

01:14:07.209 --> 01:14:09.845
Chinese people expect food to be complete

01:14:09.845 --> 01:14:11.146
when it arrives at your table.

01:14:11.146 --> 01:14:13.749
You don't go and add more sauce to it.

01:14:13.749 --> 01:14:16.618
Sauces. In the United
States, optimal for dipping.

01:14:16.618 --> 01:14:18.954
Tangy barbecue. Spicy Buffalo.

01:14:18.954 --> 01:14:21.223
It's the USA, so you
know we got that ranch.

01:14:21.223 --> 01:14:22.257
Honey mustard.

01:14:22.257 --> 01:14:25.027
Honey, which is not here.
I don't know where it is.

01:14:25.027 --> 01:14:27.529
Mayonnaise, which also
they did not include.

01:14:27.529 --> 01:14:29.765
Mexican-style salsa.

01:14:29.765 --> 01:14:32.468
These are our exclusive desserts.

01:14:32.468 --> 01:14:34.603
I am going to try every
single one of them.

01:14:34.603 --> 01:14:38.140
We can start with the taro pie.

01:14:38.140 --> 01:14:41.009
Taro is kind of like a cross

01:14:41.009 --> 01:14:43.045
between sweet potato and potato.

01:14:43.045 --> 01:14:45.848
It's often used in desserts in Asia.

01:14:45.848 --> 01:14:49.718
You'll find them in everything
from pies to bubble tea.

01:14:50.986 --> 01:14:53.789
It's a bit like yam with a bit of jam,

01:14:53.789 --> 01:14:55.224
but it's subtly sweet.

01:14:55.224 --> 01:14:57.759
For Chinese people, if you say
a dessert is not very sweet,

01:14:57.759 --> 01:14:58.927
that's actually a compliment.

01:14:58.927 --> 01:15:02.264
Pineapple pie, also one of my favorites.

01:15:03.532 --> 01:15:07.102
Mm. That is heavenly.

01:15:07.102 --> 01:15:08.337
I think I'm going to finish this.

01:15:08.337 --> 01:15:10.672
Now I need to chew for a very long time.

01:15:12.074 --> 01:15:14.209
So, here we've got the strawberry sundae,

01:15:14.209 --> 01:15:15.677
which is kind of melted already,

01:15:15.677 --> 01:15:18.514
but I'm sure it would've been
amazing when it first arrived.

01:15:18.514 --> 01:15:21.817
An affogato and a
matcha-flavored affogato,

01:15:21.817 --> 01:15:24.920
and then here we've got the McFlurrys.

01:15:24.920 --> 01:15:28.290
This is the strawberry McFlurry

01:15:28.290 --> 01:15:30.626
with Oreo cookies.

01:15:30.626 --> 01:15:35.197
Oh, my gosh, that is perhaps
the most sinful thing

01:15:35.197 --> 01:15:36.431
that you could have.

01:15:36.431 --> 01:15:38.867
Oh, but it's so good.

01:15:38.867 --> 01:15:41.103
This is just the regular McFlurry,

01:15:41.103 --> 01:15:43.605
and here is my all-time favorite,

01:15:43.605 --> 01:15:47.509
mango-pomelo-sago-flavored McFlurry.

01:15:47.509 --> 01:15:50.078
Hm. It's very different
with the ice cream.

01:15:50.078 --> 01:15:52.548
You still got the mango in there,

01:15:52.548 --> 01:15:55.884
and the pomelo, it's
very juicy, it's tender,

01:15:55.884 --> 01:15:57.686
like little tiny pips in there

01:15:57.686 --> 01:15:59.354
that kind of pop when you eat them.

01:15:59.354 --> 01:16:00.622
Oh! Just perfect.

01:16:01.823 --> 01:16:04.293
Mm. Brain freeze. Oh!

01:16:04.293 --> 01:16:05.527
In the US, you can get yourself

01:16:05.527 --> 01:16:08.263
a McFlurry with mini M&amp;M's.

01:16:08.263 --> 01:16:12.935
For some reason, mini M&amp;M's
taste better than regular M&amp;M's.

01:16:12.935 --> 01:16:15.804
I love mini M&amp;M's. Mm.

01:16:15.804 --> 01:16:17.406
Hot caramel sundae.

01:16:17.406 --> 01:16:19.641
It's classic. They don't
have this in China?

01:16:19.641 --> 01:16:23.278
God, I mean, what's more
American than an apple pie?

01:16:23.278 --> 01:16:25.447
Look at this thing. Let's
crack that bad boy open.

01:16:25.447 --> 01:16:27.249
We got chocolate chip cookies.

01:16:27.249 --> 01:16:29.217
Shakes. You can get three
different types of shakes

01:16:29.217 --> 01:16:31.353
here at a US McDonald's. Chocolate.

01:16:32.621 --> 01:16:33.589
Classic chocolate.

01:16:33.589 --> 01:16:35.157
Strawberry, personal favorite.

01:16:36.024 --> 01:16:37.192
That's so good.

01:16:37.192 --> 01:16:39.127
Vanilla, the classic.

01:16:39.127 --> 01:16:43.298
Our exclusive drinks
include the Fuze iced tea.

01:16:43.298 --> 01:16:46.835
We've got the Minute Maid orange McFloat,

01:16:46.835 --> 01:16:49.171
bubble tea, soy milk,

01:16:49.171 --> 01:16:51.707
pure milk, Ceylon black tea,

01:16:51.707 --> 01:16:54.142
which in China we would call red tea,

01:16:54.142 --> 01:16:56.578
which just confuses you for fun.

01:16:56.578 --> 01:16:58.847
I'm going to go back to here

01:16:58.847 --> 01:17:00.882
because this is the
only thing I want to try

01:17:00.882 --> 01:17:01.883
out of all of them.

01:17:03.785 --> 01:17:05.187
That tastes like orange juice.

01:17:05.187 --> 01:17:06.989
It's just plain old orange juice.

01:17:06.989 --> 01:17:08.991
In the US, you can get
yourself a Dr Pepper,

01:17:08.991 --> 01:17:12.694
a Fanta orange and an
Orange Lavaburst, lemonade.

01:17:12.694 --> 01:17:14.963
You can also get frozen drinks.

01:17:14.963 --> 01:17:18.166
You can get a frozen Fanta
blue raspberry or frozen Coke.

01:17:18.166 --> 01:17:19.835
McDonald's also has smoothies.

01:17:19.835 --> 01:17:23.905
A mango pineapple smoothie
and a strawberry smoothie.

01:17:23.905 --> 01:17:25.807
Yeah, they make a decent
smoothie at McDonald's.

01:17:25.807 --> 01:17:26.608
As you can see,

01:17:26.608 --> 01:17:29.811
we have an absolute ton of
breakfast options here in China.

01:17:29.811 --> 01:17:32.681
I think McDonald's has done
fantastic in this regard

01:17:32.681 --> 01:17:36.818
because the Chinese treat
breakfast as a very special meal.

01:17:36.818 --> 01:17:38.286
We have a very similar saying to,

01:17:38.286 --> 01:17:40.222
"Eat breakfast like a king,

01:17:40.222 --> 01:17:42.758
lunch like a prince,
dinner like a pauper."

01:17:42.758 --> 01:17:46.862
So, starting with the
sausage McMuffin with egg.

01:17:46.862 --> 01:17:48.096
Always a good way to start the day.

01:17:48.096 --> 01:17:51.466
You can get this as a double as well.

01:17:51.466 --> 01:17:53.669
Next we have the ham muffin.

01:17:53.669 --> 01:17:56.371
It's just literally a piece of ham,

01:17:56.371 --> 01:17:58.140
some lettuce, and two muffins,

01:17:58.140 --> 01:18:01.076
so I guess this would
actually be a hamburger.

01:18:01.076 --> 01:18:02.811
You can get this as a double as well.

01:18:02.811 --> 01:18:05.681
Next we have the grilled chicken muffin.

01:18:08.917 --> 01:18:11.186
This chicken's been
sitting around for a while.

01:18:11.186 --> 01:18:15.524
Next we've got the
crispy chicken McMuffin.

01:18:15.524 --> 01:18:20.529
So this is the breakfast version of the

01:18:20.529 --> 01:18:22.597
"such a big chicken chop."

01:18:22.597 --> 01:18:26.601
Breakfast in the US. We have
so many breakfast options,

01:18:26.601 --> 01:18:28.603
starting down here, the sandwiches.

01:18:28.603 --> 01:18:30.839
Egg McMuffin. Maybe the first

01:18:30.839 --> 01:18:32.974
fast breakfast sandwich
to ever hit the market.

01:18:32.974 --> 01:18:34.976
Sausage McMuffin. Sausage and cheese.

01:18:34.976 --> 01:18:35.944
If you hadn't noticed,

01:18:35.944 --> 01:18:38.480
this is all on what we
call an English muffin,

01:18:38.480 --> 01:18:39.881
'cause they're from England.

01:18:39.881 --> 01:18:42.117
There's also a bacon,
egg, and cheese McMuffin.

01:18:42.117 --> 01:18:44.786
But the option that we have most for

01:18:44.786 --> 01:18:47.322
are the scrambled-egg burgers.

01:18:47.322 --> 01:18:49.257
Scrambled-egg grilled chicken burger.

01:18:49.257 --> 01:18:53.995
The scrambled egg is
very luminously yellow.

01:18:53.995 --> 01:18:55.197
Wow, look at that.

01:18:56.665 --> 01:18:58.233
Very peppery.

01:18:58.233 --> 01:18:59.901
They love their pepper here, don't they?

01:18:59.901 --> 01:19:02.170
So, the scrambled-egg sausage burger.

01:19:02.170 --> 01:19:03.705
You'll notice the buns are different now.

01:19:03.705 --> 01:19:06.007
We're no longer on the muffins.
We're back to regular buns.

01:19:06.007 --> 01:19:08.076
Oh, it's squeezing out, isn't it?

01:19:08.076 --> 01:19:10.612
Scrambled-egg cheeseburger.

01:19:10.612 --> 01:19:13.982
This is the brightest burger
I've ever seen in my life.

01:19:13.982 --> 01:19:15.584
It's definitely very portable.

01:19:15.584 --> 01:19:17.686
I think that's one thing that
McDonald's has done very well,

01:19:17.686 --> 01:19:21.323
because Chinese breakfast
traditionally is not too portable

01:19:21.323 --> 01:19:23.792
in the sense that you need to
sit down to a lot of meals,

01:19:23.792 --> 01:19:26.661
like if you want to eat
wonton in the morning

01:19:26.661 --> 01:19:28.497
or if you want to eat
some soups in the morning.

01:19:28.497 --> 01:19:29.998
This you can just take and go.

01:19:29.998 --> 01:19:33.101
And, of course, you can
get the scrambled-egg

01:19:33.101 --> 01:19:36.138
German-flavor-sausage burger.

01:19:36.138 --> 01:19:37.205
Oh, at least they give you two,

01:19:37.205 --> 01:19:40.108
as opposed to just one tiny sausage.

01:19:40.108 --> 01:19:42.344
Biscuits, biscuits, biscuits.

01:19:42.344 --> 01:19:43.645
Sausage and egg biscuit.

01:19:43.645 --> 01:19:46.014
So, the biscuits are the
same breakfast sandwiches

01:19:46.014 --> 01:19:47.916
you get in English-muffin form,

01:19:47.916 --> 01:19:50.585
but in this biscuit form,
the American biscuit,

01:19:50.585 --> 01:19:53.588
this dry, crumbly, buttery biscuit,

01:19:53.588 --> 01:19:56.091
there is a bacon, egg, and cheese one.

01:19:56.091 --> 01:19:58.393
For some reason people in this country

01:19:58.393 --> 01:20:02.831
seem to want just a biscuit and sausage

01:20:02.831 --> 01:20:04.566
with no sauce, no nothing.

01:20:04.566 --> 01:20:07.969
This is as dry as if
you'd go into a barbershop

01:20:07.969 --> 01:20:10.005
and take a handful of hair clippings

01:20:10.005 --> 01:20:13.241
and just shove them in your
mouth. This is that dry.

01:20:13.241 --> 01:20:16.044
In the US we have something
called McGriddles,

01:20:16.044 --> 01:20:17.946
and McGriddles are breakfast sandwiches

01:20:17.946 --> 01:20:21.316
where they replace the
English muffin and/or biscuit

01:20:21.316 --> 01:20:22.851
with pancakes.

01:20:22.851 --> 01:20:24.820
So, first of all, they got the
McDonald's logo right there.

01:20:24.820 --> 01:20:26.021
Too hilarious.

01:20:26.021 --> 01:20:28.323
Somehow, through the miracle of science,

01:20:28.323 --> 01:20:31.893
was able to inject syrup
into these pancakes.

01:20:33.528 --> 01:20:34.529
Sensational.

01:20:34.529 --> 01:20:37.899
You can get your McGriddles
in sausage, egg, and cheese

01:20:37.899 --> 01:20:39.100
and then just sausage.

01:20:40.101 --> 01:20:44.005
On to what I was going to
talk about, the congee.

01:20:44.005 --> 01:20:46.808
Congee is a very traditional
breakfast item here in China.

01:20:46.808 --> 01:20:48.944
It's basically just rice porridge,

01:20:48.944 --> 01:20:51.313
and it's something that is

01:20:51.313 --> 01:20:54.416
kind of like chicken
soup for Chinese people,

01:20:54.416 --> 01:20:56.551
in the sense that if you fall ill,

01:20:56.551 --> 01:20:59.554
you're going to be given one
of these, plain, with nothing.

01:20:59.554 --> 01:21:02.624
This I think is with century egg,

01:21:02.624 --> 01:21:05.994
but the century egg,
it tastes a little bit

01:21:05.994 --> 01:21:07.996
like a blue-cheese version of egg,

01:21:07.996 --> 01:21:10.932
in that it's kind of
like egg that's gone off,

01:21:10.932 --> 01:21:12.400
but in a very nice way.

01:21:12.400 --> 01:21:15.737
And this adds a nice
savoriness to the congee.

01:21:15.737 --> 01:21:18.440
You can also get it with

01:21:18.440 --> 01:21:21.109
pickles and bamboo shoots.

01:21:21.109 --> 01:21:22.878
And if you're going to get congee,

01:21:22.878 --> 01:21:24.312
then usually you need to pair it

01:21:24.312 --> 01:21:27.616
with what they've called
an "Asian dough stick."

01:21:27.616 --> 01:21:29.651
This is what we call a youtiao,

01:21:29.651 --> 01:21:32.654
which is literally a stick of fried dough.

01:21:32.654 --> 01:21:34.789
These are absolutely amazing

01:21:34.789 --> 01:21:37.259
when paired with stuff like soy milk

01:21:37.259 --> 01:21:39.127
and, of course, with congee.

01:21:40.128 --> 01:21:41.930
You know, you need to eat these fresh.

01:21:41.930 --> 01:21:44.833
Deep-fried, they are so incredibly crispy.

01:21:44.833 --> 01:21:47.068
Oh, wow, well done, McDonald's.

01:21:47.068 --> 01:21:49.437
Like, 10 hours later,
these are still crispy.

01:21:49.437 --> 01:21:52.073
I'm very impressed but
also a little bit worried

01:21:52.073 --> 01:21:54.910
because they should never be
this crispy after that long.

01:21:54.910 --> 01:21:56.845
I wonder what they've put in here.

01:21:56.845 --> 01:21:59.414
Last but not least, our
German sausages again.

01:21:59.414 --> 01:22:00.815
It's not just sandwiches, you guys.

01:22:00.815 --> 01:22:04.352
We also have something in the US,

01:22:04.352 --> 01:22:07.222
the Big Breakfast, which
is totally in disarray.

01:22:07.222 --> 01:22:09.557
This is like the advertising
for this breakfast.

01:22:09.557 --> 01:22:11.192
I'm sorry?

01:22:11.192 --> 01:22:14.229
The Big Breakfast with pancakes.

01:22:14.229 --> 01:22:16.531
You can also get hotcakes, aka pancakes.

01:22:16.531 --> 01:22:19.467
There's no way they're back
there, like, ladling the ...

01:22:19.467 --> 01:22:21.469
right? There's no way they're doing that.

01:22:21.469 --> 01:22:23.505
These have to be premade and
they just heat them up, right?

01:22:23.505 --> 01:22:24.873
So, hotcakes and sausage.

01:22:24.873 --> 01:22:26.441
Oh, and they both come with syrup,

01:22:26.441 --> 01:22:27.809
so you know what we gotta do.

01:22:27.809 --> 01:22:31.413
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho, yeah!

01:22:31.413 --> 01:22:33.648
We also have a

01:22:33.648 --> 01:22:37.552
morning wrap with ham.

01:22:37.552 --> 01:22:40.855
The wrap itself is basically frozen solid.

01:22:40.855 --> 01:22:45.293
We can exchange that with sausage,

01:22:45.293 --> 01:22:46.695
which is also frozen.

01:22:46.695 --> 01:22:48.663
It's almost like a piece of art now,

01:22:48.663 --> 01:22:51.266
like you're supposed to look
at it instead of eating it.

01:22:51.266 --> 01:22:53.068
Wow, frozen in time.

01:22:53.068 --> 01:22:55.637
US McDonald's have

01:22:55.637 --> 01:22:58.473
sausage breakfast burritos.

01:22:58.473 --> 01:22:59.507
I mean, I can't even unfold,

01:22:59.507 --> 01:23:00.842
I'm just, like, ripping it apart.

01:23:00.842 --> 01:23:03.178
You got scrambled eggs, the sausage,

01:23:03.178 --> 01:23:05.380
it comes with Mexican-style salsa.

01:23:05.380 --> 01:23:06.681
Hey, McDonald's, it's actually pretty good

01:23:06.681 --> 01:23:08.083
considering that this is, like,

01:23:08.083 --> 01:23:11.219
probably the furthest
you can get from salsa

01:23:11.219 --> 01:23:12.954
and still legally be
able to call it salsa.

01:23:12.954 --> 01:23:15.156
If you're not trying to
completely destroy your insides

01:23:15.156 --> 01:23:16.024
first thing in the morning,

01:23:16.024 --> 01:23:18.727
you can get yourself
fruit and maple oatmeal.

01:23:18.727 --> 01:23:19.728
Seems like your breakfast

01:23:19.728 --> 01:23:22.163
is trying to escape
your body an hour later,

01:23:22.163 --> 01:23:23.765
might actually be able to hold this down.

01:23:23.765 --> 01:23:27.569
Et voilà, ze options from le bakery.

01:23:27.569 --> 01:23:29.004
So, we have macarons.

01:23:29.004 --> 01:23:30.872
Right now we have two different flavors,

01:23:30.872 --> 01:23:34.209
chocolate and berries.

01:23:34.209 --> 01:23:36.211
These actually look really legit.

01:23:37.979 --> 01:23:40.815
Pat yourself on the back.
This is really good.

01:23:40.815 --> 01:23:43.284
And these things are lamingtons.

01:23:43.284 --> 01:23:45.186
I've never actually had lamingtons.

01:23:45.186 --> 01:23:48.690
Apparently, they're basically
Australian sponge cakes

01:23:48.690 --> 01:23:50.825
which are covered in coconut flakes,

01:23:50.825 --> 01:23:52.994
and this is a lemon-flavored one.

01:23:53.962 --> 01:23:55.797
Surprisingly addictive.

01:23:55.797 --> 01:23:58.166
We have the McCafé bakery.

01:23:58.166 --> 01:24:02.070
At the McCafé bakery, you
get, you know, sweet treats,

01:24:02.070 --> 01:24:03.338
not necessarily for breakfast

01:24:03.338 --> 01:24:05.206
but probably leaning more
towards breakfast time.

01:24:05.206 --> 01:24:07.542
Ba-bam, blueberry muffin.

01:24:07.542 --> 01:24:10.745
A cinnamon roll with
cream cheese frosting.

01:24:10.745 --> 01:24:14.149
It looks like it's squishy.
It most certainly is not.

01:24:14.149 --> 01:24:16.684
I mean, come on, who doesn't
love an apple fritter?

01:24:16.684 --> 01:24:19.187
An apple fritter is a doughnut
that tastes like apple

01:24:19.187 --> 01:24:22.757
and is shaped like it was
just squoze in someone's hand

01:24:22.757 --> 01:24:23.992
for some strange reason.

01:24:23.992 --> 01:24:28.363
These are our McCafé drink options,

01:24:28.363 --> 01:24:33.001
starting with the extra-milky
latte with oat milk.

01:24:33.001 --> 01:24:34.736
A latte is two-thirds milk,

01:24:34.736 --> 01:24:35.937
and then you add oat milk in there,

01:24:35.937 --> 01:24:38.807
I don't think we're going
to have much coffee.

01:24:38.807 --> 01:24:41.676
Oh. Oh, wow, that is surprisingly good.

01:24:41.676 --> 01:24:44.045
In China, oat milk has
really, really taken off

01:24:44.045 --> 01:24:46.915
because a lot of people did
not grow up drinking milk.

01:24:46.915 --> 01:24:49.417
A lot of Chinese people
are lactose intolerant.

01:24:49.417 --> 01:24:53.388
And so oat milk is definitely
a very healthy alternative,

01:24:53.388 --> 01:24:54.956
and that's why we have the

01:24:54.956 --> 01:24:57.659
extra-strong chocolate with oat milk.

01:24:57.659 --> 01:24:59.727
You can also get this without oat milk.

01:24:59.727 --> 01:25:01.696
Extra-strong matcha milk.

01:25:01.696 --> 01:25:02.864
Extra-strong matcha --

01:25:02.864 --> 01:25:05.400
oh, we have so much matcha.

01:25:05.400 --> 01:25:08.236
Extra-strong chocolate smoothie,

01:25:08.236 --> 01:25:12.040
extra-strong milk and vanilla smoothie,

01:25:12.040 --> 01:25:16.778
and the matcha milk with matcha jelly.

01:25:16.778 --> 01:25:19.080
Matcha, matcha, oh, I'm going to --

01:25:19.080 --> 01:25:22.984
We absolutely love matcha here
in China. I don't know why.

01:25:24.252 --> 01:25:27.689
It tastes like grass and frozen grass.

01:25:27.689 --> 01:25:30.758
Coffees and coffees and
coffees and coffees.

01:25:30.758 --> 01:25:35.130
McDonald's has a assortment
of featured drinks,

01:25:35.130 --> 01:25:38.333
espresso drinks, mochas, iced lattes.

01:25:38.333 --> 01:25:39.501
Let's get all that on the screen.

01:25:39.501 --> 01:25:41.169
See? All these things.

01:25:41.169 --> 01:25:43.571
This is the cold brew. This is so strong.

01:25:44.906 --> 01:25:46.508
I think each of you should
eventually take a sip.

01:25:46.508 --> 01:25:48.643
You will not believe how
strong the cold brew is.

01:25:48.643 --> 01:25:50.612
Oh, my God.

01:25:50.612 --> 01:25:51.646
French vanilla latte.

01:25:52.547 --> 01:25:54.983
This is the exact
opposite. This is so sweet.

01:25:54.983 --> 01:25:57.085
Mocha. Who doesn't want hot chocolate

01:25:57.085 --> 01:25:58.486
first thing in the morning?

01:25:58.486 --> 01:25:59.988
Hilarious, people are buying that.

01:25:59.988 --> 01:26:02.323
Ooh, this is the premium roast coffee.

01:26:02.323 --> 01:26:03.424
I know I've been kind of dissing on it,

01:26:03.424 --> 01:26:05.827
but their actual coffee, the
actual McDonald's coffee,

01:26:05.827 --> 01:26:06.961
I think is very good.

01:26:06.961 --> 01:26:09.097
They're a good contender in
the coffee game, I think,

01:26:09.097 --> 01:26:10.198
in the fast-food coffee game.

01:26:10.198 --> 01:26:11.933
Especially the horrible
PR nightmare they had

01:26:11.933 --> 01:26:13.935
when they, like, destroyed
that lady's crotch

01:26:13.935 --> 01:26:15.236
with their superhot coffee.

01:26:15.236 --> 01:26:17.205
It is a comeback story, McDonald's.

01:26:17.205 --> 01:26:19.674
Almost killing a woman
with second-degree burns

01:26:19.674 --> 01:26:21.042
from boiling-hot coffee

01:26:21.042 --> 01:26:23.945
to these nice little fun café drinks.

01:26:23.945 --> 01:26:26.848
I would happily pour
this all over my crotch.

01:26:26.848 --> 01:26:28.816
You can get the iced-coffee drinks.

01:26:28.816 --> 01:26:30.485
Don't like this. This is the mocha.

01:26:30.485 --> 01:26:35.423
McDonald's in China also
has a late-night menu.

01:26:35.423 --> 01:26:37.892
They only have one item,
but this is worth it.

01:26:37.892 --> 01:26:42.130
I got it last night. These
are marinated chicken bones.

01:26:42.130 --> 01:26:43.231
They don't sound very appealing,

01:26:43.231 --> 01:26:46.568
but the Chinese name
is wordplay on an idiom

01:26:46.568 --> 01:26:50.738
which kind of means "the
highest level of artistry."

01:26:50.738 --> 01:26:53.508
And when I opened up this box,

01:26:53.508 --> 01:26:55.176
[gasps]

01:26:55.176 --> 01:26:58.079
I literally heard angels going, "Aah!"

01:26:58.079 --> 01:27:01.716
This is actually a street food

01:27:01.716 --> 01:27:05.787
from someplace up in Northeast
China called Shenyang.

01:27:05.787 --> 01:27:07.589
Chinese people love fiddly stuff,

01:27:07.589 --> 01:27:10.725
and meat on the bone is
just that much more tasty.

01:27:12.594 --> 01:27:15.263
Ah, still incredible, even cold.

01:27:15.263 --> 01:27:18.666
You know, the box actually
says "marinated chicken bones."

01:27:18.666 --> 01:27:21.236
"Be careful, it may contain bones."

01:27:21.236 --> 01:27:23.871
And you're actually supposed
to spit the bones out,

01:27:23.871 --> 01:27:27.275
but I'm having so much
fun eating this thing,

01:27:27.275 --> 01:27:29.244
I actually eat the bones too.

01:27:29.244 --> 01:27:32.847
It's spicy, it's sour, it's sweet.

01:27:32.847 --> 01:27:35.316
Ah, and just absolutely divine.

01:27:35.316 --> 01:27:37.819
I can see how people would be
inspired after eating this.

01:27:39.854 --> 01:27:42.857
So, McDonald's came to China in 1990,

01:27:42.857 --> 01:27:45.693
and then it opened in Beijing in '92.

01:27:45.693 --> 01:27:48.329
Back then, that was the largest
McDonald's in the world.

01:27:48.329 --> 01:27:50.031
They had 700 seats.

01:27:50.031 --> 01:27:54.068
On opening day, they served 40,000 people.

01:27:54.068 --> 01:27:55.536
And people didn't go there for the food.

01:27:55.536 --> 01:27:57.305
It was a place to be seen.

01:27:57.305 --> 01:28:00.041
Like, McDonald's was a window to the West.

01:28:00.041 --> 01:28:02.210
It was a cosmopolitan place

01:28:02.210 --> 01:28:06.481
to experience capitalism, in a way.

01:28:06.481 --> 01:28:09.817
But over time it became
a trendy hangout spot

01:28:09.817 --> 01:28:11.319
for city kids after school.

01:28:11.319 --> 01:28:12.920
They'd go there to do their homework.

01:28:12.920 --> 01:28:16.090
It still very much is middle class.

01:28:16.090 --> 01:28:19.927
I remember actually when I came
to visit China 20 years ago,

01:28:19.927 --> 01:28:24.098
my aunts greeted me at the
airport with bags of McDonald's,

01:28:24.098 --> 01:28:26.734
and I was actually kind of offended

01:28:26.734 --> 01:28:29.737
that they would bring junk food to meet me

01:28:29.737 --> 01:28:31.105
as opposed to real Chinese food,

01:28:31.105 --> 01:28:34.275
but for them McDonald's
was the best of the best.

01:28:34.275 --> 01:28:36.711
It was all the prestige.

01:28:36.711 --> 01:28:39.080
Hey, to me, McDonald's,
when it comes to fast food,

01:28:39.080 --> 01:28:42.517
is No. 1 in the US, dare I say the world.

01:28:42.517 --> 01:28:44.252
If you just want a good hot meal

01:28:44.252 --> 01:28:45.787
where you know exactly what
it's going to taste like

01:28:45.787 --> 01:28:48.589
and get it and go, McDonald's never fails.

01:28:48.589 --> 01:28:50.525
Waiting in line, getting
it at the drive-through,

01:28:50.525 --> 01:28:51.826
you get it lickety-split.

01:28:51.826 --> 01:28:54.829
Now they leaned really big
into delivery since COVID,

01:28:54.829 --> 01:28:57.665
and, man, McDonald's is
showing up right away,

01:28:57.665 --> 01:28:59.834
and I love it. It's dangerous.

01:28:59.834 --> 01:29:00.668
I can't remember the last time

01:29:00.668 --> 01:29:02.637
I've eaten inside at a McDonald's.

01:29:02.637 --> 01:29:04.772
So, I usually dine in at McDonald's,

01:29:04.772 --> 01:29:07.909
but I find that in China
they focus more on delivery,

01:29:07.909 --> 01:29:09.677
and they promise to get
everything delivered

01:29:09.677 --> 01:29:12.580
within 30 minutes, which
they actually keep to,

01:29:12.580 --> 01:29:14.248
and that's incredibly impressive.

01:29:14.248 --> 01:29:16.417
Last night I ordered the chicken carcass.

01:29:16.417 --> 01:29:18.386
It took 28 minutes.

01:29:18.386 --> 01:29:20.588
Got a Big Mac earlier.
That was 10 minutes.

01:29:20.588 --> 01:29:22.824
So they're very, very punctual.

01:29:22.824 --> 01:29:24.759
They're also open for very long,

01:29:24.759 --> 01:29:26.527
from 7 till 10 p.m.,

01:29:26.527 --> 01:29:28.196
and there are many 24-hour branches,

01:29:28.196 --> 01:29:30.198
so extremely convenient.

01:29:30.198 --> 01:29:32.166
Now, McDonald's is an American brand,

01:29:32.166 --> 01:29:34.802
so they have American
classics on the menu,

01:29:34.802 --> 01:29:37.071
hamburgers, chicken sandwiches,

01:29:37.071 --> 01:29:39.974
but they kind of
assimilated and made popular

01:29:39.974 --> 01:29:41.676
the burger culture in this country.

01:29:41.676 --> 01:29:42.910
It's hard to say, because I feel like

01:29:42.910 --> 01:29:44.679
the American taste is McDonald's.

01:29:44.679 --> 01:29:46.381
I think McDonald's has actually adapted

01:29:46.381 --> 01:29:48.282
pretty well to Chinese tastes.

01:29:48.282 --> 01:29:50.885
Besides the McSpicy burger and wings

01:29:50.885 --> 01:29:52.587
and the grilled chicken sandwich,

01:29:52.587 --> 01:29:54.622
which have all become bestsellers,

01:29:54.622 --> 01:29:57.425
McDonald's actually
uses chicken thigh meat

01:29:57.425 --> 01:30:00.261
instead of breast meat in
all of its chicken burgers,

01:30:00.261 --> 01:30:01.796
except for the McChicken.

01:30:01.796 --> 01:30:03.431
And I think that's because Chinese people

01:30:03.431 --> 01:30:05.767
think chicken breast is dry,

01:30:05.767 --> 01:30:08.736
and they've also got lots
of time-limited specials

01:30:08.736 --> 01:30:12.607
when it comes to the desserts,
like the mantou burger,

01:30:12.607 --> 01:30:14.575
which is kind of like a Chinese bun,

01:30:14.575 --> 01:30:16.744
and even cilantro sundae.

01:30:16.744 --> 01:30:18.713
McDonald's, everyone's
going after McDonald's.

01:30:18.713 --> 01:30:20.281
Burger King's been going after McDonald's

01:30:20.281 --> 01:30:21.849
since, what, the '60s?

01:30:21.849 --> 01:30:23.151
Every burger chain

01:30:23.151 --> 01:30:26.287
try to get some sort
of edge on McDonald's.

01:30:26.287 --> 01:30:30.091
We're fancier, we got
different varieties of stuff.

01:30:30.091 --> 01:30:33.428
McDonald's is No. 1,
here, now, and forever.

01:30:33.428 --> 01:30:36.464
The McDonald's logo should be
on the American flag, dammit!

01:30:36.464 --> 01:30:39.801
So, China is McDonald's
second-largest market

01:30:39.801 --> 01:30:41.769
by store count, after the US.

01:30:41.769 --> 01:30:46.407
In China, there are over
5,000 McDonald's locations,

01:30:46.407 --> 01:30:49.677
but KFC has over 9,000.

01:30:49.677 --> 01:30:50.778
They actually came here first,

01:30:50.778 --> 01:30:53.815
so it's KFC, then McDonald's,

01:30:53.815 --> 01:30:56.150
then a local brand called Dicos,

01:30:56.150 --> 01:30:59.287
which does both fried chicken and burgers,

01:30:59.287 --> 01:31:02.056
so they're really just
fighting an uphill battle.

01:31:04.325 --> 01:31:07.261
In China, a Big Mac costs 25 yuan.

01:31:07.261 --> 01:31:09.997
A Big Mac in the US costs $5.29.

01:31:09.997 --> 01:31:11.032
Make it a Big Mac meal

01:31:11.032 --> 01:31:15.937
with a medium fries and
medium Coke, and it's 36 yuan.

01:31:15.937 --> 01:31:18.606
If you want to go large,
that's 4 yuan extra

01:31:18.606 --> 01:31:21.242
for a grand total of 40 yuan.

01:31:21.242 --> 01:31:22.076
If you make it a meal

01:31:22.076 --> 01:31:23.644
with a medium fries and medium drink,

01:31:23.644 --> 01:31:26.481
price goes up to $9.29.

01:31:26.481 --> 01:31:30.418
Upgrade that to a large, and it's $10.79.

01:31:30.418 --> 01:31:34.355
Our Big Mac large meal costs 86% more.

01:31:34.355 --> 01:31:36.491
So our Big Mac meal is cheaper,

01:31:36.491 --> 01:31:39.727
but at the same time
the average daily wage

01:31:39.727 --> 01:31:43.798
of a cabby in Beijing is
about 200 yuan, give or take,

01:31:43.798 --> 01:31:47.235
and so this would be 20% of their salary.

01:31:47.235 --> 01:31:48.703
So it's still not really something

01:31:48.703 --> 01:31:51.806
that you would eat on a regular
basis, but maybe splurge on.

01:31:54.108 --> 01:31:55.176
Let's talk nutrition.

01:31:55.176 --> 01:31:57.178
This is that very Big Mac, again.

01:31:57.178 --> 01:31:59.747
In the US, it's 590 calories

01:31:59.747 --> 01:32:01.182
and all this stuff.

01:32:01.182 --> 01:32:05.586
In China, our Big Mac has 524 calories,

01:32:05.586 --> 01:32:09.190
26 grams of fat, 45 grams of carbs,

01:32:09.190 --> 01:32:11.392
27 grams of protein,

01:32:11.392 --> 01:32:14.695
and 877 milligrams of sodium.

01:32:14.695 --> 01:32:16.030
What if we did a combo?

01:32:16.030 --> 01:32:18.666
Starting with the medium fries,

01:32:18.666 --> 01:32:21.068
this adds 320 calories to the meal,

01:32:21.068 --> 01:32:22.303
and all this stuff.

01:32:22.303 --> 01:32:26.307
While a medium fries in
China contains 290 calories,

01:32:26.307 --> 01:32:28.709
13 grams of total fat,

01:32:28.709 --> 01:32:31.712
35.9 grams of carbs,

01:32:31.712 --> 01:32:34.048
we're not sure if it contains any sugars,

01:32:34.048 --> 01:32:35.349
4 grams of protein,

01:32:35.349 --> 01:32:39.387
and 252 milligrams of sodium.

01:32:39.387 --> 01:32:41.022
But you need something to drink.

01:32:41.022 --> 01:32:42.456
Add in a medium Coke to that,

01:32:42.456 --> 01:32:46.160
and this kicks your meal
up another 210 calories.

01:32:46.160 --> 01:32:47.161
We'll do the same.

01:32:47.161 --> 01:32:49.964
Here's everything in a
medium Coke in China.

01:32:49.964 --> 01:32:53.234
148 calories. That leaves the grand total

01:32:53.234 --> 01:32:57.772
for the China meal at 962 calories.

01:32:57.772 --> 01:32:59.941
While in the US, the total
ends up looking like this.

01:32:59.941 --> 01:33:03.945
1,120 calories and all this other stuff.

01:33:03.945 --> 01:33:05.846
Get a load of that sodium, though.

01:33:05.846 --> 01:33:06.847
Guh!

01:33:06.948 --> 01:33:08.916
Claudia: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:33:08.916 --> 01:33:10.885
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:33:10.885 --> 01:33:13.854
between McDonald's in the US and Italy.

01:33:13.854 --> 01:33:15.623
This is "Food Wars."

01:33:17.358 --> 01:33:20.194
Drinks at McDonald's in
Italy come in three sizes,

01:33:20.194 --> 01:33:22.163
250 milliliters,

01:33:22.163 --> 01:33:23.564
400 milliliters,

01:33:23.564 --> 01:33:25.666
and 500 milliliters.

01:33:25.666 --> 01:33:26.667
We're now going to measure

01:33:26.667 --> 01:33:30.004
a 500-ml Coke to see if that's true.

01:33:30.004 --> 01:33:31.606
Oh, oh.

01:33:31.606 --> 01:33:33.374
I think we're surpassing that.

01:33:33.374 --> 01:33:37.111
It's just right below the 600 mark,

01:33:37.111 --> 01:33:38.613
but almost there.

01:33:38.613 --> 01:33:40.181
So quite generous.

01:33:40.181 --> 01:33:42.783
Drinks in the US also come in four sizes.

01:33:42.783 --> 01:33:45.886
The extra small, which is 355 milliliters,

01:33:45.886 --> 01:33:47.622
or 12 fluid ounces.

01:33:47.622 --> 01:33:51.959
The small, 474 milliliters,
or 16 fluid ounces.

01:33:51.959 --> 01:33:56.197
And the medium, 621
milliliters, or 21 fluid ounces.

01:33:56.197 --> 01:33:59.967
And the large, 946 milliliters,

01:33:59.967 --> 01:34:01.769
or 32 fluid ounces.

01:34:01.769 --> 01:34:06.007
Since we were the ones that
filled this up at the restaurant

01:34:06.007 --> 01:34:08.843
and I don't think we got it all full up,

01:34:08.843 --> 01:34:09.977
I'm going to go ahead and fill this

01:34:09.977 --> 01:34:12.513
what I think is reasonable.

01:34:12.513 --> 01:34:15.282
I can't do to the top
because the cap is recessed.

01:34:20.955 --> 01:34:24.191
OK. 32? Surely you jest.

01:34:24.191 --> 01:34:26.961
But there's the 32 line. Not even close.

01:34:26.961 --> 01:34:30.531
It's closer to 24 than it is 32.

01:34:30.531 --> 01:34:33.668
So, fries in Italy come in three sizes.

01:34:33.668 --> 01:34:36.704
The regular, which is
technically the small,

01:34:36.704 --> 01:34:38.472
medium, and large.

01:34:38.472 --> 01:34:41.442
Here in America, our
fries come in four sizes.

01:34:41.442 --> 01:34:44.011
The kids, which comes in the Happy Meal.

01:34:44.011 --> 01:34:45.513
Look at this little guy.

01:34:45.513 --> 01:34:46.414
Little guy!

01:34:46.414 --> 01:34:49.250
The small, the medium, and the large.

01:34:49.250 --> 01:34:50.851
All the "Food Wars" heads watching

01:34:50.851 --> 01:34:52.253
know that in the China episode,

01:34:52.253 --> 01:34:55.423
our large McDonald's fry was 175 grams.

01:34:55.423 --> 01:34:56.691
In the Japan episode,

01:34:56.691 --> 01:34:59.493
our large McDonald's fry was 190 grams.

01:34:59.493 --> 01:35:01.862
So clearly there's some
difference in grammage

01:35:01.862 --> 01:35:04.198
depending on, I don't know,
the McDonald's we go to,

01:35:04.198 --> 01:35:05.366
the scooper, who knows?

01:35:05.366 --> 01:35:08.436
So we're going to weigh
our large right now.

01:35:08.436 --> 01:35:10.271
Ready? Fantastic.

01:35:13.007 --> 01:35:15.409
Eh, let's go 185.

01:35:15.409 --> 01:35:18.179
Not a bad scoop. We got
a good scooper this time.

01:35:18.179 --> 01:35:19.947
Seems pretty small, actually.

01:35:19.947 --> 01:35:21.115
What about McNuggets?

01:35:21.115 --> 01:35:24.285
In Italy you can get a bag of four,

01:35:24.285 --> 01:35:26.253
a box of six pieces,

01:35:26.253 --> 01:35:29.190
nine pieces, and 20 pieces.

01:35:29.190 --> 01:35:30.391
Claudia, in the US,

01:35:30.391 --> 01:35:32.927
our McNuggets are
available in these sizes:

01:35:32.927 --> 01:35:36.230
the four-piece, the
six-piece, 10-piece, 20-piece,

01:35:36.230 --> 01:35:39.500
which you also have, but we go
up one more here in America.

01:35:39.500 --> 01:35:41.902
Our largest size, the 40-piece.

01:35:41.902 --> 01:35:44.238
Now, if my calculations are correct,

01:35:44.238 --> 01:35:47.108
this is double your largest size.

01:35:47.108 --> 01:35:49.376
The iconic Big Mac.
Both countries have it,

01:35:49.376 --> 01:35:52.780
but we're going to compare
ours to Italy's by weighing it.

01:35:52.780 --> 01:35:56.984
226 grams for a US Big Mac.

01:35:56.984 --> 01:35:58.519
And here is an Italian Big Mac,

01:35:58.519 --> 01:36:01.122
or Il Big Mac, as is written here,

01:36:01.122 --> 01:36:03.457
and we're going to weigh it now.

01:36:03.457 --> 01:36:05.092
209 grams.

01:36:06.961 --> 01:36:09.864
Here are all the items on
the McDonald's Italy menu

01:36:09.864 --> 01:36:11.665
that you won't find in the US.

01:36:11.665 --> 01:36:14.869
And here are all the McDonald's
menu items from the US

01:36:14.869 --> 01:36:16.837
you won't find in Italy.

01:36:16.837 --> 01:36:20.040
Get a good look, Claudia.

01:36:20.040 --> 01:36:21.609
Let's start from the burgers.

01:36:21.609 --> 01:36:24.011
We have a bunch of Italian burgers

01:36:24.011 --> 01:36:26.046
that you won't get in the US.

01:36:26.046 --> 01:36:29.083
The first one we got here
is a chicken Big Mac.

01:36:29.083 --> 01:36:32.653
Oh, right. Just destroyed chicken Big Mac.

01:36:32.653 --> 01:36:35.022
Has that been inverted?

01:36:35.022 --> 01:36:37.224
Is that supposed to look like this?

01:36:40.628 --> 01:36:43.297
The cheese helps a little
bit. Sauce as well.

01:36:43.297 --> 01:36:47.368
Moving on, we have a bacon Big Mac.

01:36:47.368 --> 01:36:49.637
Yeah, there's two strips of bacon,

01:36:49.637 --> 01:36:52.740
but they're not quite
big, so it does look like

01:36:52.740 --> 01:36:54.642
maybe it's just one
that's been cut in half.

01:36:54.642 --> 01:36:59.613
We got a crispy McBacon,
which is like cheeseburger,

01:36:59.613 --> 01:37:03.517
double patty, and some bacon
again, a bit on the side.

01:37:03.517 --> 01:37:06.353
It's funny actually because growing up,

01:37:06.353 --> 01:37:08.255
I thought that the crispy McBacon

01:37:08.255 --> 01:37:12.059
was the iconic McDonald's item,

01:37:12.059 --> 01:37:15.396
and it's weird that it is
actually an Italian exclusive.

01:37:15.396 --> 01:37:17.264
Here are all the burgers in the US

01:37:17.264 --> 01:37:18.432
that you can't get in Italy.

01:37:18.432 --> 01:37:20.501
Starting down here, the
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

01:37:20.501 --> 01:37:22.303
It really is just a cheeseburger

01:37:22.303 --> 01:37:24.872
that is a quarter pound of meat.

01:37:24.872 --> 01:37:26.207
It's a great go-to burger.

01:37:26.207 --> 01:37:30.678
Meat, cheese, onions,
pickles, ketchup, and mustard.

01:37:30.678 --> 01:37:32.179
And if you want more meat,

01:37:32.179 --> 01:37:33.848
you can get the double Quarter Pounder.

01:37:33.848 --> 01:37:35.816
Correct. Not the half pounder,

01:37:35.816 --> 01:37:38.452
the double Quarter Pounder with cheese.

01:37:38.452 --> 01:37:41.455
Two patties, more meat, more cheese.

01:37:41.455 --> 01:37:42.489
Fantastic sandwich.

01:37:42.489 --> 01:37:43.958
And then we've got the first one

01:37:43.958 --> 01:37:45.593
of the My Selection range,

01:37:45.593 --> 01:37:50.130
which is a range that was
designed with Joe Bastianich.

01:37:50.130 --> 01:37:53.400
He's an American TV personality and chef.

01:37:53.400 --> 01:37:58.205
This one is speck and Asiago,
so yeah, very traditional.

01:37:58.205 --> 01:38:02.443
Speck is a type of cured
meat. It's like a smoked ham.

01:38:02.443 --> 01:38:04.478
Yeah, it's a smoked ham
from the north of Italy.

01:38:04.478 --> 01:38:06.247
It's actually very, very nice,

01:38:06.247 --> 01:38:08.148
just very salty with that smoky flavor.

01:38:08.148 --> 01:38:09.783
It's one of my favorites.

01:38:09.783 --> 01:38:11.352
And then we have Asiago,

01:38:11.352 --> 01:38:14.421
which is a cheese made
pretty much in the same area.

01:38:14.421 --> 01:38:16.891
There's also mayo and zucchini in there.

01:38:19.927 --> 01:38:21.695
A bit dry, I think.

01:38:21.695 --> 01:38:24.498
You do taste the cold cut, the speck.

01:38:24.498 --> 01:38:27.001
Just brings that saltiness, smokiness.

01:38:27.001 --> 01:38:29.036
Very nice, and the cheese
also is quite good.

01:38:29.036 --> 01:38:30.337
Yeah, actually I don't
know if you've noticed,

01:38:30.337 --> 01:38:33.707
but it is much bigger than the others.

01:38:33.707 --> 01:38:36.877
You can even take, like, bacon Big Mac.

01:38:36.877 --> 01:38:38.646
Even though it's supposed
to have two patties,

01:38:38.646 --> 01:38:40.848
it is much bigger.

01:38:40.848 --> 01:38:43.684
And then we have another
My Selection burger.

01:38:43.684 --> 01:38:45.953
This one is called My BBQ.

01:38:45.953 --> 01:38:48.322
This one has got barbecue sauce,

01:38:48.322 --> 01:38:50.257
yes, I can see it,

01:38:50.257 --> 01:38:53.727
Gouda cheese, and bacon,

01:38:53.727 --> 01:38:57.665
and it's all topped off
with some balsamic vinegar.

01:38:57.665 --> 01:39:01.835
It does still have the
same sort of fancy patty

01:39:01.835 --> 01:39:03.938
that we had before.

01:39:03.938 --> 01:39:07.341
Right, and after these very
nice and fancy burgers,

01:39:07.341 --> 01:39:10.010
we have a gluten-free burger.

01:39:11.078 --> 01:39:12.313
Oh. [record scratching]

01:39:12.313 --> 01:39:15.049
Wait, why does it come in a bag?

01:39:15.049 --> 01:39:19.086
Ooh. Yeah. Very -- ooh.

01:39:19.086 --> 01:39:20.587
Yeah, not excited about this.

01:39:20.587 --> 01:39:22.656
Just, I don't like the bread.

01:39:23.657 --> 01:39:25.960
I'm sure you can find
better gluten-free bread.

01:39:25.960 --> 01:39:27.594
There are so many around.

01:39:27.594 --> 01:39:31.265
And if you want vegetables on your burger

01:39:31.265 --> 01:39:32.633
for some strange reason,

01:39:32.633 --> 01:39:35.869
you can get the Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe,

01:39:35.869 --> 01:39:39.807
with lettuce and tomato and mayo.

01:39:39.807 --> 01:39:41.842
Oh, did you see that squirt coming out?

01:39:41.842 --> 01:39:43.277
Hit, like, a pocket of
mayonnaise on that one.

01:39:43.277 --> 01:39:44.345
That's kind of weird.

01:39:44.345 --> 01:39:45.179
It tastes great.

01:39:45.179 --> 01:39:46.613
And if you just want to
go all in on the meat,

01:39:46.613 --> 01:39:50.818
you can get a double
Quarter Pounder with bacon.

01:39:50.818 --> 01:39:52.453
Look at this.

01:39:52.453 --> 01:39:53.287
Right?

01:39:55.789 --> 01:39:57.191
It's really good. Enough said.

01:39:57.191 --> 01:39:59.793
And, surprise, another thing on our menu

01:39:59.793 --> 01:40:02.496
you guys don't have: the McDouble.

01:40:02.496 --> 01:40:04.164
McDonald's has a double cheeseburger,

01:40:04.164 --> 01:40:05.866
which is double the
meat, double the cheese,

01:40:05.866 --> 01:40:08.035
but also there's a McDouble on the menu.

01:40:08.035 --> 01:40:09.169
What's the difference, you ask?

01:40:09.169 --> 01:40:12.006
Well, McDouble only has
one slice of cheese.

01:40:12.006 --> 01:40:14.375
As you can see from here, on top,

01:40:14.375 --> 01:40:18.178
you got ketchup, mustard,
and pickles, no cheese.

01:40:18.178 --> 01:40:20.214
The cheese is in between here.

01:40:20.214 --> 01:40:22.182
I get it. Times are tough in this economy,

01:40:22.182 --> 01:40:25.419
but get the extra slice
of cheese, guys. Come on.

01:40:25.419 --> 01:40:26.620
I mean, we're not robots here.

01:40:26.620 --> 01:40:28.689
We gotta have some pleasure in our lives,

01:40:28.689 --> 01:40:31.625
and I think you should get
that extra slice of cheese.

01:40:31.625 --> 01:40:34.028
Absorb the cost of it.
It's perfectly fine.

01:40:34.028 --> 01:40:36.430
You're doing great. Come on!

01:40:36.430 --> 01:40:39.099
Next one is another one
of those My Selection.

01:40:39.099 --> 01:40:43.771
It's a chicken, avocado, and bacon burger.

01:40:43.771 --> 01:40:46.473
Hm, it's got a different bun, this one.

01:40:46.473 --> 01:40:48.175
Ooh, fancy.

01:40:48.175 --> 01:40:50.010
All right, yeah, avocado is there.

01:40:50.010 --> 01:40:51.478
There's, like, cabbage.

01:40:51.478 --> 01:40:53.180
Mm, bit less excited about that.

01:40:53.180 --> 01:40:57.317
And this one has
caciocavallo Silano cheese.

01:40:57.317 --> 01:40:58.786
I don't know. We can call this --

01:40:58.786 --> 01:41:01.355
you know sauce talk. The cheese talk.

01:41:01.355 --> 01:41:04.425
Caciocavallo comes from the
same family of mozzarella.

01:41:04.425 --> 01:41:06.393
They're called pasta filata cheeses,

01:41:06.393 --> 01:41:09.763
and it's just basically the
way that you make cheese,

01:41:09.763 --> 01:41:12.666
when you split the milk
into curds and whey.

01:41:12.666 --> 01:41:14.068
It's made in a different way.

01:41:14.068 --> 01:41:16.370
And you could say that caciocavallo

01:41:16.370 --> 01:41:18.372
is like an aged mozzarella.

01:41:18.372 --> 01:41:20.107
So it's a very versatile cheese

01:41:20.107 --> 01:41:23.010
that I think is not
very well known abroad.

01:41:23.010 --> 01:41:26.080
So, yeah, thank you, McDonald's,
for making that a thing

01:41:26.080 --> 01:41:28.215
on your menu so everybody
can know about it.

01:41:28.215 --> 01:41:32.586
So, here's the cheese that we
were talking about. [laughs]

01:41:32.586 --> 01:41:33.854
It's just always a shame.

01:41:33.854 --> 01:41:38.392
It's been put there with,
like, avocado and this cabbage.

01:41:38.392 --> 01:41:42.396
Next one, we've got
double chicken barbecue.

01:41:42.396 --> 01:41:45.065
After seeing all these big
ones, they do look quite small.

01:41:45.065 --> 01:41:47.034
And then we have a chicken burger.

01:41:47.034 --> 01:41:49.203
This one is different from a McChicken

01:41:49.203 --> 01:41:53.440
because it has Caesar
sauce and no lettuce.

01:41:53.440 --> 01:41:55.676
I think this is glue.

01:41:55.676 --> 01:41:57.111
It looks like -- there is a type of glue

01:41:57.111 --> 01:41:59.012
that looks exactly like that.

01:41:59.012 --> 01:42:02.883
We also thought it'd be
fun to compare Happy Meals.

01:42:02.883 --> 01:42:04.985
Here's the US one.

01:42:04.985 --> 01:42:06.954
Open up this box, take a look around.

01:42:06.954 --> 01:42:08.589
I'm pretty sure this is Pokémon.

01:42:08.589 --> 01:42:11.158
This one comes with kid fries,

01:42:11.158 --> 01:42:13.193
nuggets, which, we got a six-piece,

01:42:13.193 --> 01:42:15.762
and this is their Pokémon toy.

01:42:15.762 --> 01:42:16.597
So, they get the six-piece.

01:42:16.597 --> 01:42:17.831
It's funny, like, a six-piece still seems

01:42:17.831 --> 01:42:19.266
kind of like a lot for a kid.

01:42:19.266 --> 01:42:21.368
Pokémon-themed toys
coming at you these days.

01:42:21.368 --> 01:42:22.469
What is this?

01:42:23.437 --> 01:42:26.707
OK, so we got Pikachu.

01:42:26.707 --> 01:42:28.942
Does this have any value?
Because there's rare ones.

01:42:28.942 --> 01:42:30.277
There's ones that have
a lot of value to them.

01:42:30.277 --> 01:42:32.746
But not the ones at McDonald's, right?

01:42:32.746 --> 01:42:34.882
Cyclizar? Any value?

01:42:36.550 --> 01:42:39.486
We got Tandemaus.

01:42:42.289 --> 01:42:43.257
Yeah.

01:42:43.257 --> 01:42:47.794
And, of course, Sandaconda.

01:42:48.762 --> 01:42:50.664
I'll go look on eBay after this

01:42:50.664 --> 01:42:52.799
and see if these are worth anything.

01:42:52.799 --> 01:42:55.569
Culturally, I have no idea what this is.

01:42:55.569 --> 01:42:57.070
I don't know what -- this is a thing?

01:42:59.406 --> 01:43:00.841
No, I have no idea who.

01:43:03.610 --> 01:43:05.679
I don't remember any of those names.

01:43:08.248 --> 01:43:10.651
Charlizard?

01:43:10.651 --> 01:43:12.019
Cylizard?

01:43:12.019 --> 01:43:14.454
Is this Cylizard?

01:43:14.454 --> 01:43:15.956
Charmagarg.

01:43:17.591 --> 01:43:18.425
OK.

01:43:18.425 --> 01:43:21.261
In a Happy Meal in Italy,
you can find four items.

01:43:21.261 --> 01:43:24.665
Obviously there is a drink,
then there is a main course

01:43:24.665 --> 01:43:27.668
that could be either
nuggets [or] a hamburger.

01:43:27.668 --> 01:43:30.571
And exclusive to Italy is a chicken burger

01:43:30.571 --> 01:43:33.640
and a McToast, which is what we got today.

01:43:33.640 --> 01:43:35.075
We're going to see that in a moment.

01:43:35.075 --> 01:43:36.143
Then there is a side.

01:43:36.143 --> 01:43:39.213
It can either be fries or baby carrots.

01:43:39.213 --> 01:43:40.581
And a dessert.

01:43:40.581 --> 01:43:44.885
This can be either fresh fruit, Actimel,

01:43:44.885 --> 01:43:48.255
which is technically a drink
but it's a dessert here,

01:43:48.255 --> 01:43:49.957
and Parmesan.

01:43:49.957 --> 01:43:54.394
Here's our McToast. Nice.

01:43:54.394 --> 01:43:58.165
The surprise of the day.

01:43:58.165 --> 01:44:01.501
Yeah, they're just doing some
Hot Wheels collaboration.

01:44:01.501 --> 01:44:03.770
So let's have a look at what is it.

01:44:03.770 --> 01:44:06.640
I don't know, do you think
I can find a Vespa in here?

01:44:06.640 --> 01:44:11.078
Oh, cute little skateboard,

01:44:11.078 --> 01:44:11.912
pink one.

01:44:12.746 --> 01:44:14.214
Nyoom.

01:44:14.214 --> 01:44:17.718
We also have one exclusive
wrap option here in Italy.

01:44:17.718 --> 01:44:20.554
It's a McWrap with crisp chicken breast

01:44:20.554 --> 01:44:23.223
and Parmesan, or Parmigiano-Reggiano.

01:44:23.223 --> 01:44:25.792
It's made in collaboration
with Giallozafferano,

01:44:25.792 --> 01:44:29.830
which is the No. 1
recipe website in Italy.

01:44:29.830 --> 01:44:33.400
To be honest, I think
they could have come up

01:44:33.400 --> 01:44:36.637
with a better recipe, maybe, for the wrap.

01:44:36.637 --> 01:44:40.207
The wrap does look very
sad, just the actual bread.

01:44:40.207 --> 01:44:41.708
Chicken looks OK.

01:44:41.708 --> 01:44:43.644
Italy clearly has plenty of exclusive

01:44:43.644 --> 01:44:46.380
chicken-sandwich options, but
we have a few of our own here,

01:44:46.380 --> 01:44:49.516
namely the McCrispy and the spicy McCrispy

01:44:49.516 --> 01:44:52.019
and a deluxe version of each sandwich.

01:44:52.019 --> 01:44:52.853
Let's take a look.

01:44:52.853 --> 01:44:54.988
It looks closer to a chicken sandwich

01:44:54.988 --> 01:44:56.957
you would find at a Chick-fil-A,

01:44:56.957 --> 01:45:01.461
and then now Burger King has
the chicken king, I think?

01:45:01.461 --> 01:45:04.831
McDonald's did all the
research that they do

01:45:04.831 --> 01:45:08.735
to release this, the McCrispy sandwich.

01:45:08.735 --> 01:45:11.905
Now, as you can tell,
it's just pickles on here.

01:45:11.905 --> 01:45:16.276
A crispier, more natural-looking
piece of fried chicken,

01:45:16.276 --> 01:45:19.713
and no sauce. Does it
always have no sauce?

01:45:22.349 --> 01:45:24.184
I don't like that. I don't like
a place that gives you food

01:45:24.184 --> 01:45:26.920
and, like, assembly requirements.

01:45:27.754 --> 01:45:29.256
For the most part, I
should get the sandwich

01:45:29.256 --> 01:45:30.090
the way it's supposed to be.

01:45:30.090 --> 01:45:31.692
So this put your own sauce in it,

01:45:31.692 --> 01:45:32.993
it's like, no, you put it on.

01:45:32.993 --> 01:45:35.195
Here's the deluxe of it.

01:45:36.396 --> 01:45:38.365
Yay, it has mayo. Whoa.

01:45:38.365 --> 01:45:40.167
This to me is like,
yeah, do this every time.

01:45:40.167 --> 01:45:41.802
This should just be the
sandwich. I don't ...

01:45:45.072 --> 01:45:47.841
If you're like me and
you want to spice it up,

01:45:47.841 --> 01:45:49.042
ah,

01:45:50.644 --> 01:45:53.213
they have the spicy -- oh, come on.

01:45:53.213 --> 01:45:55.148
There's spicy sauce on here somewhere.

01:45:55.148 --> 01:45:58.752
Then, of course, they
got the spicy deluxe,

01:45:58.752 --> 01:46:00.354
which of course has spicy sauce

01:46:00.354 --> 01:46:01.321
and all those veggies in there.

01:46:01.321 --> 01:46:03.824
So, yeah. McDonald's, still a contender

01:46:03.824 --> 01:46:05.759
in the chicken-sandwich game, I feel.

01:46:05.759 --> 01:46:09.096
Now we're on to the exclusive
sides here in Italy.

01:46:09.096 --> 01:46:12.566
The first one that we got is cheesy fries.

01:46:12.566 --> 01:46:16.136
The same fry, just with a
bit more bacon we got here.

01:46:16.136 --> 01:46:19.139
Yeah, cheddar and bacon.

01:46:19.139 --> 01:46:20.874
This is, like, I don't know,

01:46:20.874 --> 01:46:24.111
a very sad Italian take on poutine.

01:46:24.111 --> 01:46:27.848
On the menu next for sides,
we've got panzerotti.

01:46:27.848 --> 01:46:31.485
So, actually very excited
about these because,

01:46:31.485 --> 01:46:33.954
ooh,

01:46:33.954 --> 01:46:36.256
panzerotti are from my hometown,

01:46:36.256 --> 01:46:37.824
Bari, in the south of Italy.

01:46:37.824 --> 01:46:40.193
The main difference is
that usually panzerotti,

01:46:40.193 --> 01:46:42.596
the traditional ones, they are this big.

01:46:42.596 --> 01:46:45.499
They're usually pretty wide.
It's, like, a main meal.

01:46:45.499 --> 01:46:48.335
Panzerotti normally, they
have, tomatoes and mozzarella

01:46:48.335 --> 01:46:52.539
is the most common filling,
but in Bari, again,

01:46:52.539 --> 01:46:56.443
where they are from, you can
get them with ground beef,

01:46:56.443 --> 01:46:58.412
mozzarella, and cooked ham.

01:46:58.412 --> 01:47:00.380
These are actually my favorites.

01:47:00.380 --> 01:47:03.150
I used to go and get them after school.

01:47:04.351 --> 01:47:06.253
That's just, they are the perfect snack.

01:47:10.056 --> 01:47:11.591
Quite good, actually.

01:47:11.591 --> 01:47:14.027
Filling is OK, but I
think a real panzerotto,

01:47:14.027 --> 01:47:16.129
when you bite into it,

01:47:16.129 --> 01:47:18.732
basically all the filling
should almost come out.

01:47:18.732 --> 01:47:20.333
It should, like, pop.

01:47:20.333 --> 01:47:22.102
Like, the first reaction
when you eat a panzerotti,

01:47:22.102 --> 01:47:23.637
this is like,

01:47:23.637 --> 01:47:25.839
and then you sort of put your hand here

01:47:25.839 --> 01:47:28.408
and just avoid a complete mess.

01:47:28.408 --> 01:47:30.177
This brings us to the next snack,

01:47:30.177 --> 01:47:33.847
which is Parmigiano-Reggiano, or Parmesan.

01:47:33.847 --> 01:47:35.949
This is one of the most
counterfeit cheeses

01:47:35.949 --> 01:47:37.884
in the world, so.

01:47:37.884 --> 01:47:39.920
In Italy but also in Europe,

01:47:39.920 --> 01:47:41.888
because of this whole protection thing,

01:47:41.888 --> 01:47:44.791
anything that's called even
Parmesan, not the real name,

01:47:44.791 --> 01:47:47.594
Parmigiano-Reggiano, is
in fact the real thing,

01:47:47.594 --> 01:47:50.197
so at least we are safe on that side.

01:47:50.197 --> 01:47:53.366
Having said that, I think
most of the Parmesan,

01:47:53.366 --> 01:47:58.104
Parmigiano that you will
find around in supermarkets,

01:47:58.104 --> 01:48:00.240
it's been aged for the bare minimum,

01:48:00.240 --> 01:48:01.608
which is 12 months.

01:48:01.608 --> 01:48:03.109
So it is good, it is the real thing,

01:48:03.109 --> 01:48:04.544
but if you can choose,

01:48:04.544 --> 01:48:08.148
just have something that's
been aged for a bit longer.

01:48:08.148 --> 01:48:10.083
I think in Italy we do eat a lot of cheese

01:48:10.083 --> 01:48:14.488
as a snack as it is, and I
do have definitely memories

01:48:14.488 --> 01:48:16.056
of me coming back from school

01:48:16.056 --> 01:48:18.725
and then just in the afternoon grabbing

01:48:18.725 --> 01:48:20.193
some cheese off the fridge

01:48:20.193 --> 01:48:24.064
and having a couple of slices
or even more than that.

01:48:24.064 --> 01:48:25.298
I think my mom still does that,

01:48:25.298 --> 01:48:28.068
so, sorry for exposing you, Mom.

01:48:31.538 --> 01:48:32.806
Love it.

01:48:32.806 --> 01:48:35.909
Over here we got another exclusive.

01:48:35.909 --> 01:48:39.012
There are actually three
salads on the menu.

01:48:39.012 --> 01:48:42.516
One is just a plain salad,
one is a salad with tomatoes,

01:48:42.516 --> 01:48:46.052
and then we got one with crispy
chicken breast and Parmesan.

01:48:46.052 --> 01:48:50.223
We could also select a dressing,
and we added olive oil.

01:48:50.223 --> 01:48:53.226
You could also get a tiny
bottle of balsamic vinegar

01:48:53.226 --> 01:48:54.995
or just vinegar.

01:48:54.995 --> 01:48:58.298
We actually have no
exclusive sides in the US.

01:48:58.298 --> 01:49:01.268
Every side option on our menu
can also be found in Italy.

01:49:01.268 --> 01:49:03.003
I will say, though, I love that they have

01:49:03.003 --> 01:49:06.706
a stick of cheese as a side,
kind of like a palate cleanser.

01:49:06.706 --> 01:49:07.741
I would love that.

01:49:07.741 --> 01:49:10.644
I would love to snack on cheese.
I love snacking on cheese.

01:49:10.644 --> 01:49:12.913
We should have more cheese,
is what I'm trying to say.

01:49:12.913 --> 01:49:14.748
We can bring it back with the sauces.

01:49:14.748 --> 01:49:17.651
It's time for sauce talk, Italy edition.

01:49:17.651 --> 01:49:20.153
La la la sauce talk!

01:49:21.021 --> 01:49:22.989
That had to offend somebody.

01:49:22.989 --> 01:49:24.658
Sauce talk.

01:49:24.658 --> 01:49:27.294
We have several exclusive sauces

01:49:27.294 --> 01:49:31.264
here in the United States,
including spicy Buffalo,

01:49:31.264 --> 01:49:35.835
and then we have ranch, honey
mustard, sweet 'n' sour.

01:49:35.835 --> 01:49:38.605
Now, I have two because one

01:49:38.605 --> 01:49:40.807
is from the movie "Loki," apparently.

01:49:40.807 --> 01:49:42.976
And of course you just get honey.

01:49:42.976 --> 01:49:46.012
Of all these, I'd probably
go sweet 'n' sour,

01:49:46.012 --> 01:49:48.882
but barbecue, which they
do have, is my favorite.

01:49:48.882 --> 01:49:52.185
We have one exclusive sauce in Italy,

01:49:52.185 --> 01:49:55.355
which is spicy mustard sauce.

01:49:55.355 --> 01:49:56.189
Yeah.

01:50:00.060 --> 01:50:02.462
Yeah, it is a bit spicy.

01:50:02.462 --> 01:50:05.565
Not so much, though.
Doesn't numb your tongue.

01:50:05.565 --> 01:50:08.735
I think actually it has a sweet
aftertaste for some reason.

01:50:08.735 --> 01:50:10.136
For the early risers,

01:50:10.136 --> 01:50:12.405
there are plenty of
exclusive breakfast items

01:50:12.405 --> 01:50:16.142
at the US McDonald's,
and they're all savory.

01:50:16.142 --> 01:50:18.745
Now, first thing I'm going to
talk about are the biscuits.

01:50:18.745 --> 01:50:21.247
I'm not the person to
describe American biscuits

01:50:21.247 --> 01:50:24.017
to the rest of the world.
They should have hired a poet.

01:50:24.017 --> 01:50:27.120
This is the bacon, egg,
and cheese biscuit,

01:50:27.120 --> 01:50:28.655
but you can get a biscuit version

01:50:28.655 --> 01:50:32.425
of any meat or cheese
combination that you want.

01:50:32.425 --> 01:50:34.227
In the middle here, though,

01:50:34.227 --> 01:50:37.564
Italy, Claudia, everyone,

01:50:37.564 --> 01:50:38.765
look at what I'm about to show you.

01:50:38.765 --> 01:50:41.167
You know what pancakes are.
You know what syrup is.

01:50:41.167 --> 01:50:43.236
You obviously know what
breakfast sandwiches are.

01:50:43.236 --> 01:50:45.438
This right here is a McGriddle,

01:50:45.438 --> 01:50:47.874
and they replaced the buns with this.

01:50:47.874 --> 01:50:49.442
These bun pancakes.

01:50:49.442 --> 01:50:52.078
This is a pancake, Italy. A pancake.

01:50:52.078 --> 01:50:56.416
These, here. And they somehow
injected syrup in them,

01:50:56.416 --> 01:50:58.685
so it's not like syrup like a sauce,

01:50:58.685 --> 01:51:01.788
it's just, like, already syrup somehow,

01:51:01.788 --> 01:51:04.424
and it is savory and
sweet at the same time.

01:51:04.424 --> 01:51:06.426
It is so delicious.

01:51:06.426 --> 01:51:09.029
It's a McGriddle. It's
fantastic. I love these.

01:51:09.029 --> 01:51:10.597
This is a bacon, egg,
and cheese McGriddle,

01:51:10.597 --> 01:51:13.700
but once again, you can get
it in any various sausage,

01:51:13.700 --> 01:51:16.336
egg, and/or cheese
combination that you want.

01:51:16.336 --> 01:51:17.871
McGriddles. Check 'em out.

01:51:17.871 --> 01:51:20.306
I am the McGriddle No. 1 fan over here.

01:51:20.306 --> 01:51:25.011
And the OG breakfast sandwich,
this is the egg McMuffin.

01:51:25.011 --> 01:51:27.547
They got the Big Breakfast
with or without hotcakes.

01:51:27.547 --> 01:51:28.748
I went with hotcakes.

01:51:28.748 --> 01:51:33.286
You got eggs, bacon,
pancakes, English muffin,

01:51:33.286 --> 01:51:34.554
this thing's fantastic.

01:51:34.554 --> 01:51:38.425
And if you want to just
get hotcakes and sausage,

01:51:38.425 --> 01:51:39.459
you can also do that.

01:51:39.459 --> 01:51:42.996
And each order of pancakes

01:51:42.996 --> 01:51:46.266
comes with our hotcakes syrup.

01:51:46.266 --> 01:51:50.770
I think an unsung hero of the
McDonald's breakfast menu,

01:51:50.770 --> 01:51:53.440
been a fan of this for years,

01:51:53.440 --> 01:51:56.342
it is the sausage breakfast burrito.

01:51:56.342 --> 01:51:58.545
Now, let's be honest.

01:51:58.545 --> 01:52:00.013
Italy, in case you're wondering,

01:52:00.013 --> 01:52:04.718
this in no way represents
an actual burrito.

01:52:04.718 --> 01:52:06.486
I want to make that perfectly clear.

01:52:06.486 --> 01:52:08.021
I would not put this in the same category

01:52:08.021 --> 01:52:10.824
as any sort of burrito,
breakfast or otherwise,

01:52:10.824 --> 01:52:14.894
but it's its own thing, and
I think it is fantastic.

01:52:14.894 --> 01:52:18.765
It is in a flour tortilla.

01:52:18.765 --> 01:52:21.401
Scrambled eggs, sausage, yes, I know,

01:52:21.401 --> 01:52:26.139
peppers, cheese, and the secret weapon

01:52:28.041 --> 01:52:29.909
is this, their Mexican-style salsa.

01:52:29.909 --> 01:52:34.814
Again, there is nothing
authentically Mexican about this,

01:52:34.814 --> 01:52:37.884
but it tastes great.

01:52:37.884 --> 01:52:39.786
This was a go-to for years.

01:52:39.786 --> 01:52:41.955
I could put away about four of these.

01:52:44.824 --> 01:52:47.060
McDonald's also does offer oatmeal,

01:52:47.060 --> 01:52:50.063
specifically fruit and maple oatmeal.

01:52:50.063 --> 01:52:50.930
Moving on.

01:52:50.930 --> 01:52:54.534
The Italian McDonald's
also sells breakfast items.

01:52:54.534 --> 01:52:57.170
We've got ... [laughs]

01:52:57.170 --> 01:52:58.938
That's super sad.

01:52:58.938 --> 01:53:02.575
We got scrambled eggs with
bacon and a muffin and bread,

01:53:02.575 --> 01:53:04.778
which does look more like a muffin.

01:53:04.778 --> 01:53:07.947
And then we have a McMuffin
with bacon and egg.

01:53:07.947 --> 01:53:10.450
Yeah, Italians don't really
have savory breakfast.

01:53:10.450 --> 01:53:12.986
It's definitely a habit.

01:53:12.986 --> 01:53:17.257
Like, you just associate
breakfast with sweet items.

01:53:17.257 --> 01:53:21.027
All right, US also has their
own exclusive McCafé items.

01:53:22.295 --> 01:53:24.631
Where'd they go?

01:53:24.631 --> 01:53:27.634
The McDonald'ses near our studio

01:53:27.634 --> 01:53:30.670
did not have the McCafé food items.

01:53:38.478 --> 01:53:40.747
McDonald's in Italy has
really made an effort

01:53:40.747 --> 01:53:43.449
with the McCafé menu items,

01:53:43.449 --> 01:53:47.253
and there are really a lot
of items on the menu here.

01:53:47.253 --> 01:53:49.055
So let's start from the croissants.

01:53:49.055 --> 01:53:50.824
We've got quite a few on the menu.

01:53:50.824 --> 01:53:53.726
I think this one here,

01:53:53.726 --> 01:53:55.895
because you can see a little bit of brown,

01:53:55.895 --> 01:53:59.666
this is the cocoa one with sourdough.

01:54:03.169 --> 01:54:05.071
Pretty safe to eat.

01:54:05.071 --> 01:54:06.573
This is the plain one.

01:54:06.573 --> 01:54:09.576
Does look more like a
French-style croissant.

01:54:09.576 --> 01:54:13.112
Nice layers in there as well, some air.

01:54:13.112 --> 01:54:16.349
Over here, it's quite hard to tell,

01:54:16.349 --> 01:54:19.319
but there is a subtle,
subtle layer of jam.

01:54:19.319 --> 01:54:22.989
This is berries and cereal.

01:54:22.989 --> 01:54:25.825
So, the dough, it's a little bit stiffer,

01:54:25.825 --> 01:54:30.597
and, yeah, does smell a little bit

01:54:30.597 --> 01:54:32.599
more like cereals.

01:54:32.599 --> 01:54:36.369
Same amount of jam as in the others.

01:54:36.369 --> 01:54:38.605
Not very generous, actually.

01:54:38.605 --> 01:54:40.974
I think this one is the
last one that we got,

01:54:40.974 --> 01:54:42.141
so it's the custard.

01:54:42.141 --> 01:54:46.346
This looks like we have
a bit more in there.

01:54:46.346 --> 01:54:47.347
Obviously, it's hard to tell

01:54:47.347 --> 01:54:52.151
because the custard is the
same color as the dough,

01:54:52.151 --> 01:54:54.888
has kind of turned the dough yellow.

01:54:57.457 --> 01:55:00.226
Nice. Lots of lemon in there.

01:55:00.226 --> 01:55:02.195
Another pastry option that you can get

01:55:02.195 --> 01:55:04.697
is this cream braid.

01:55:04.697 --> 01:55:08.234
This is quite a typical
thing as well in Italy.

01:55:08.234 --> 01:55:11.137
Like, you do get these kind of pastries.

01:55:11.137 --> 01:55:14.374
You can get them also savory
in different regions of Italy.

01:55:14.374 --> 01:55:16.809
Let's see if they were
generous with the cream here.

01:55:16.809 --> 01:55:19.545
Mm, yeah, I'll say so.

01:55:21.347 --> 01:55:22.649
I prefer this cream.

01:55:22.649 --> 01:55:25.785
In Italy, you can also get some cakes.

01:55:25.785 --> 01:55:30.290
We have tiramisu, which is,
yeah, traditional Italian thing,

01:55:30.290 --> 01:55:31.891
but not a breakfast item.

01:55:31.891 --> 01:55:34.727
Like, I wouldn't really have
breakfast with tiramisu.

01:55:34.727 --> 01:55:39.065
I know you guys want to hear
the opinion of an Italian,

01:55:39.065 --> 01:55:43.303
so we're going to try this
tiramisu and see if it's proper.

01:55:45.405 --> 01:55:47.006
Yes, quite good, actually.

01:55:47.006 --> 01:55:49.842
We do have other cakes as well.

01:55:49.842 --> 01:55:53.746
We have this one, which is
torta della nonna in Italian,

01:55:53.746 --> 01:55:55.615
and that literally translates to

01:55:55.615 --> 01:55:57.951
"grandma's cake" in English.

01:55:57.951 --> 01:56:01.187
This one has lemon custard and pine nuts.

01:56:02.956 --> 01:56:04.023
I think it's a bit of a joke

01:56:04.023 --> 01:56:05.992
that this is actually
called grandma's cake

01:56:05.992 --> 01:56:08.294
just because every Italian grandma

01:56:08.294 --> 01:56:10.430
that's good in the kitchen
will be able to make something,

01:56:10.430 --> 01:56:12.899
like, 100 times better than this.

01:56:12.899 --> 01:56:15.969
We've got a strawberry cheesecake.

01:56:15.969 --> 01:56:20.239
Let's move on to this
three-layer chocolate cake.

01:56:20.239 --> 01:56:22.175
It's an absolute beast.

01:56:25.812 --> 01:56:26.946
It's a bit too much.

01:56:26.946 --> 01:56:29.282
I wouldn't have this for breakfast.

01:56:29.282 --> 01:56:31.751
And then we have a few more items here

01:56:31.751 --> 01:56:33.252
at the McCafé in Italy.

01:56:33.252 --> 01:56:36.823
We have a marshmallow doughnut,

01:56:36.823 --> 01:56:39.525
which looks like the most artificial thing

01:56:39.525 --> 01:56:41.127
I've ever seen.

01:56:41.127 --> 01:56:43.596
Then we've got a Nutella muffin.

01:56:43.596 --> 01:56:45.598
It is true that Italians love Nutella,

01:56:45.598 --> 01:56:47.800
and they eat it all the time.

01:56:47.800 --> 01:56:50.503
Again, when I was a child,
my parents used to hide it.

01:56:52.238 --> 01:56:55.241
Mm, sad. [laughs]

01:56:55.241 --> 01:56:59.479
And the last item that
we've got is macarons.

01:56:59.479 --> 01:57:02.315
We have chocolate macarons,
raspberry macarons,

01:57:02.315 --> 01:57:04.317
and pistachios macarons,

01:57:04.317 --> 01:57:06.586
or pistacchio, as we do say here.

01:57:10.056 --> 01:57:13.793
Oh, the inside is, like,

01:57:13.793 --> 01:57:15.862
dangerously green.

01:57:15.862 --> 01:57:18.398
They don't taste so much
like pistachio, to be honest.

01:57:18.398 --> 01:57:20.400
Desserts, McDonald's US,

01:57:20.400 --> 01:57:22.268
we have these exclusives.

01:57:22.268 --> 01:57:24.804
Starting down here, the baked apple pie.

01:57:24.804 --> 01:57:26.072
The day they stopped frying these

01:57:26.072 --> 01:57:27.306
is the day I stopped eating them.

01:57:27.306 --> 01:57:28.908
Now they're pulling this with, like,

01:57:28.908 --> 01:57:30.843
trying to make it look like
it's a homemade pastry.

01:57:30.843 --> 01:57:33.880
It's not. This was just spit out

01:57:33.880 --> 01:57:37.517
of an AI oven machine.

01:57:37.517 --> 01:57:41.387
Blip, blip, blip. One a second. No human.

01:57:41.387 --> 01:57:43.523
I'm the first human hand to touch this.

01:57:43.523 --> 01:57:45.291
Also chocolate chip cookies.

01:57:45.291 --> 01:57:48.795
They come in orders of
one, three, the trilogy,

01:57:48.795 --> 01:57:50.696
or a tote of 13.

01:57:50.696 --> 01:57:52.532
One good thing about the
McDonald's we went to today

01:57:52.532 --> 01:57:55.268
is the McFlurry machine
was totally working,

01:57:55.268 --> 01:57:58.204
and I got this one, the M&amp;M's McFlurry.

01:57:58.204 --> 01:57:59.338
We use the mini M&amp;M's,

01:57:59.338 --> 01:58:00.606
which are better than regular M&amp;M's,

01:58:00.606 --> 01:58:01.874
I don't know why, they just are.

01:58:01.874 --> 01:58:04.977
Sundaes, sundaes, sundaes.

01:58:04.977 --> 01:58:07.313
Maybe my favorite as a
kid, the caramel sundae.

01:58:08.381 --> 01:58:11.517
Mm. Ooh, that's my childhood right there.

01:58:11.517 --> 01:58:13.686
And you can get a fudge one as well.

01:58:13.686 --> 01:58:15.354
For Italian exclusive desserts,

01:58:15.354 --> 01:58:18.658
we have a pistachios McFlurry,

01:58:18.658 --> 01:58:20.893
then a Baci Perugina McFlurry.

01:58:20.893 --> 01:58:25.164
Baci Perugina are very popular chocolates.

01:58:25.164 --> 01:58:28.000
They are made in Perugia, which
is in the center of Italy,

01:58:28.000 --> 01:58:29.435
a town in the center.

01:58:29.435 --> 01:58:32.238
And here we have a coffee sundae.

01:58:32.238 --> 01:58:35.575
It's quite nice that they
actually gave us the espresso

01:58:35.575 --> 01:58:37.276
so that we can make our own.

01:58:37.276 --> 01:58:38.845
A bit like an affogato, in a way.

01:58:38.845 --> 01:58:41.247
The other sundaes are caramel, berries,

01:58:41.247 --> 01:58:44.484
another Baci Perugina again,
and the fior di latte,

01:58:44.484 --> 01:58:47.453
which is basically the
Italian version of vanilla.

01:58:48.521 --> 01:58:49.355
Ooh.

01:58:52.391 --> 01:58:53.993
Nice, yeah.

01:58:53.993 --> 01:58:56.996
Now on to the cold drink
options, starting down here,

01:58:56.996 --> 01:58:58.631
all the soda options
you get here in the US.

01:58:58.631 --> 01:59:01.400
Of course, we have way more than Italy.

01:59:01.400 --> 01:59:03.836
Starting with Dr Pepper.

01:59:03.836 --> 01:59:05.071
Oh, OK there.

01:59:06.506 --> 01:59:07.507
So fantastic.

01:59:07.507 --> 01:59:09.475
Diet Coke. No.

01:59:10.843 --> 01:59:11.677
Ugh.

01:59:11.677 --> 01:59:14.614
This completely unnatural-looking thing

01:59:14.614 --> 01:59:17.450
is Hi-C Orange Lavaburst.

01:59:17.450 --> 01:59:20.953
It's not carbonated,
but it's also not juice.

01:59:20.953 --> 01:59:23.589
I can't explain it. It's Hi-C.

01:59:24.724 --> 01:59:26.626
You can also get a sweet tea

01:59:26.626 --> 01:59:29.996
and an unsweetened iced tea at McDonald's.

01:59:29.996 --> 01:59:31.297
What I did feel like getting was this,

01:59:31.297 --> 01:59:33.733
the frozen Fanta blue raspberry.

01:59:35.334 --> 01:59:37.970
Oh, God, it's so sweet and so syrupy.

01:59:37.970 --> 01:59:40.039
Don't drink this, don't
give it to children,

01:59:40.039 --> 01:59:41.274
don't have it ever.

01:59:41.274 --> 01:59:42.942
They also have a Coke
version, frozen Coke.

01:59:42.942 --> 01:59:44.377
Also don't bother.

01:59:44.377 --> 01:59:45.878
Lemonade, though.

01:59:45.878 --> 01:59:47.713
So, we found out that lemonade in America

01:59:47.713 --> 01:59:49.649
is the least different
from lemonade in the UK.

01:59:49.649 --> 01:59:51.551
Again, this is not carbonated,

01:59:51.551 --> 01:59:53.419
it's not really juice,
it's something different.

01:59:53.419 --> 01:59:56.455
I don't know what
lemonade is like in Italy.

01:59:59.625 --> 02:00:01.427
Oh, man, it's so tart and so good.

02:00:01.427 --> 02:00:03.596
On to coffee drinks,

02:00:03.596 --> 02:00:05.531
or should I say cold coffee drinks,

02:00:05.531 --> 02:00:06.666
from here to here.

02:00:06.666 --> 02:00:08.134
I understand that's not a thing in Italy,

02:00:08.134 --> 02:00:09.902
which I think is hilarious.

02:00:09.902 --> 02:00:12.738
This giant glass right
here is iced coffee.

02:00:12.738 --> 02:00:14.907
You can also get it caramel flavored

02:00:14.907 --> 02:00:16.209
or French vanilla flavored.

02:00:16.209 --> 02:00:19.745
I went with black, the
ace of spades right here.

02:00:19.745 --> 02:00:20.580
Mm.

02:00:22.114 --> 02:00:24.417
Oh, man, they do something
with their coffee there.

02:00:24.417 --> 02:00:27.687
They do something where it
tastes like it's really roasted.

02:00:27.687 --> 02:00:29.188
I mean, I'm sure it's not.

02:00:29.188 --> 02:00:30.990
You can also get a iced latte.

02:00:30.990 --> 02:00:33.092
This over here is a frappé.

02:00:33.092 --> 02:00:35.795
You can get a mocha frappé
or a caramel frappé.

02:00:35.795 --> 02:00:38.297
Basically if you're an adult
and you want a milkshake,

02:00:38.297 --> 02:00:39.131
you get a frap.

02:00:39.131 --> 02:00:41.367
You can also get smoothies at McDonald's.

02:00:41.367 --> 02:00:44.737
We have a mango pineapple smoothie

02:00:44.737 --> 02:00:46.572
and a strawberry banana smoothie.

02:00:46.572 --> 02:00:49.342
In Italy, we have a few exclusive drinks.

02:00:49.342 --> 02:00:51.711
Let's start with the cold options.

02:00:51.711 --> 02:00:55.681
We have Lipton iced tea
both in lemon and peach.

02:00:55.681 --> 02:00:57.550
Then we have some fruit juices.

02:00:57.550 --> 02:00:59.085
We have pear,

02:00:59.085 --> 02:01:02.054
ace, which is very popular here in Italy.

02:01:02.054 --> 02:01:04.090
It should be very orange.

02:01:04.090 --> 02:01:06.592
It's a mix of orange, carrots, and lemon.

02:01:06.592 --> 02:01:08.294
Yeah, very orange.

02:01:08.294 --> 02:01:11.530
And it's named ace, which is A-C-E,

02:01:11.530 --> 02:01:14.767
after the three vitamins
that these fruits,

02:01:14.767 --> 02:01:17.670
or vegetables, I guess,
these carrots, contains.

02:01:17.670 --> 02:01:20.139
And then we got peach fruit juice.

02:01:20.139 --> 02:01:24.310
And here are our McDonald's
hot coffee drinks.

02:01:24.310 --> 02:01:26.379
"Coffee," right, Italy?

02:01:26.379 --> 02:01:27.913
All right, we get it.

02:01:27.913 --> 02:01:29.649
We went a little overboard
with our coffee drinks

02:01:29.649 --> 02:01:32.718
here in America, and McDonald's,
of course, is no different.

02:01:32.718 --> 02:01:35.921
You can get a caramel macchiato,

02:01:35.921 --> 02:01:38.491
a caramel cappuccino.

02:01:38.491 --> 02:01:42.261
Why are we doing so much
caramel stuff in America, right?

02:01:42.261 --> 02:01:44.697
Ah, caramel latte.

02:01:44.697 --> 02:01:47.066
You can also get it in vanilla.

02:01:47.066 --> 02:01:47.900
Don't.

02:01:47.900 --> 02:01:49.502
You can also get a mocha latte.

02:01:49.502 --> 02:01:52.872
We have a premium roast coffee.

02:01:52.872 --> 02:01:54.674
As I said before, I don't
know what they're doing

02:01:54.674 --> 02:01:56.409
at McDonald's, but

02:01:58.644 --> 02:02:00.012
I like the coffee.

02:02:00.012 --> 02:02:03.482
But you can also get,
finally, a black hot tea.

02:02:03.482 --> 02:02:06.352
What is this? The UK?

02:02:06.352 --> 02:02:07.386
Ugh.

02:02:07.386 --> 02:02:09.088
The hot drinks exclusive to Italy

02:02:09.088 --> 02:02:12.858
are obviously the king
of hot drinks, espresso.

02:02:12.858 --> 02:02:14.794
Then we've got a Moroccan coffee,

02:02:14.794 --> 02:02:17.229
which is not Moroccan in the sense of

02:02:17.229 --> 02:02:20.866
it's not Moroccan-style
coffee, but weirdly enough,

02:02:20.866 --> 02:02:22.768
and to be honest, I never
really understood this,

02:02:22.768 --> 02:02:25.671
it's named after a type
of Moroccan leather

02:02:25.671 --> 02:02:28.107
that looks this color.

02:02:28.107 --> 02:02:31.344
Honestly, it's like an
espresso with some milk.

02:02:31.344 --> 02:02:34.547
And then we got ginseng
coffee and barley coffee,

02:02:34.547 --> 02:02:36.982
which technically shouldn't
really be called coffee

02:02:36.982 --> 02:02:40.553
because it contains no
coffee, it has just barley,

02:02:40.553 --> 02:02:42.988
and this is like an alternative for people

02:02:42.988 --> 02:02:44.957
that cannot drink coffee

02:02:44.957 --> 02:02:47.860
and they still want to have something

02:02:47.860 --> 02:02:50.062
like a little espresso after lunch.

02:02:50.062 --> 02:02:51.864
Yeah, it smells very cereally.

02:02:54.900 --> 02:02:56.669
I don't know. I'm not a big fan.

02:02:56.669 --> 02:03:00.539
And then we got just a
standard latte macchiato.

02:03:00.539 --> 02:03:03.776
This is the closest thing
you will get to a latte

02:03:03.776 --> 02:03:05.678
that you will find here in Italy,

02:03:05.678 --> 02:03:09.915
so it's just a lot of
milk with a bit of coffee

02:03:09.915 --> 02:03:11.817
and some foam at the top.

02:03:14.019 --> 02:03:18.023
In Italy, a Big Mac will cost
you 6 euros and 10 cents.

02:03:18.023 --> 02:03:23.028
In dollars, that's about $6.76.

02:03:23.028 --> 02:03:26.599
A Big Mac in the US will cost you $6.29.

02:03:26.599 --> 02:03:31.003
That's a 3% price increase
from Italy to the US.

02:03:31.003 --> 02:03:33.272
What if you turn that into a combo meal?

02:03:33.272 --> 02:03:37.176
In Italy, a small Big Mac
meal with medium fries

02:03:37.176 --> 02:03:40.579
and a medium drink will
cost you 8 euros 90,

02:03:40.579 --> 02:03:43.616
and that's $9.86.

02:03:43.616 --> 02:03:45.818
Does a combo meal make
a difference in the US?

02:03:45.818 --> 02:03:47.920
A medium Big Mac combo meal over here

02:03:47.920 --> 02:03:50.222
will cost you $11.42.

02:03:50.222 --> 02:03:52.658
You can also save some
money if you buy in bulk.

02:03:52.658 --> 02:03:55.795
Here in Italy, you can
get a two-person Mac menu,

02:03:55.795 --> 02:03:59.999
which includes two Big Macs,
two large portions of fries,

02:03:59.999 --> 02:04:03.302
two large Coca-Colas, six nuggets,

02:04:03.302 --> 02:04:05.404
for 18 euros.

02:04:05.404 --> 02:04:07.973
In the US, we only do Big Mac combo meals,

02:04:07.973 --> 02:04:08.908
as mentioned before.

02:04:08.908 --> 02:04:11.444
So in order to get the
same order in Italy,

02:04:11.444 --> 02:04:14.113
you would have to order two Big Mac meals

02:04:14.113 --> 02:04:16.115
plus six nuggets on the side.

02:04:16.115 --> 02:04:20.052
It would cost around $36, which
in Italy is about 33 euros.

02:04:20.052 --> 02:04:23.022
Price-wise, I think they
are definitely better value

02:04:23.022 --> 02:04:24.623
than other fast-food chains.

02:04:24.623 --> 02:04:26.192
Well, not to believe Five Guys,

02:04:26.192 --> 02:04:30.362
I know that one has a reputation
for being quite expensive,

02:04:30.362 --> 02:04:32.498
but I think the burger
is, like, half the price.

02:04:32.498 --> 02:04:35.134
For the panzerotti, I think
that was more than 3 euros,

02:04:35.134 --> 02:04:37.236
3 euros something, which, honestly,

02:04:37.236 --> 02:04:41.507
for, like, three of those as a
side, it is a little bit sad.

02:04:41.507 --> 02:04:45.277
But again, I grew up in
the town of panzerotti,

02:04:45.277 --> 02:04:48.948
and I used to have, like,
a full one this size

02:04:48.948 --> 02:04:51.917
for, like, 2 euros. That was 15 years ago,

02:04:51.917 --> 02:04:54.153
so maybe now it would
translate into something

02:04:54.153 --> 02:04:56.522
like maybe 5 or 6.

02:04:56.522 --> 02:05:00.059
Once upon a time, McDonald's
was the cheaper option.

02:05:00.059 --> 02:05:03.062
It was a lot of food
for not a lot of money.

02:05:03.062 --> 02:05:05.931
As many people probably
pointed out on social media,

02:05:05.931 --> 02:05:10.503
this food is no longer
inexpensive. It's not expensive.

02:05:10.503 --> 02:05:12.037
Maybe because of the competition,

02:05:12.037 --> 02:05:13.439
maybe because of inflation,

02:05:13.439 --> 02:05:15.074
probably because of corporate greed,

02:05:15.074 --> 02:05:17.877
McDonald's and most fast food, I find,

02:05:17.877 --> 02:05:20.312
is not a good value anymore.

02:05:23.315 --> 02:05:24.517
Let's compare some items to see

02:05:24.517 --> 02:05:26.552
what the nutrition is of McDonald's food.

02:05:26.552 --> 02:05:28.320
A sandwich that exists in both countries

02:05:28.320 --> 02:05:31.924
and is theoretically
identical is the Big Mac.

02:05:31.924 --> 02:05:35.694
In the US, a Big Mac
contains 590 calories,

02:05:35.694 --> 02:05:39.498
34 grams of total fat, 46 grams of carbs,

02:05:39.498 --> 02:05:41.100
and 9 grams of sugar.

02:05:41.100 --> 02:05:42.968
How about an Italian Big Mac?

02:05:42.968 --> 02:05:47.273
One of those here contains 509 calories.

02:05:47.273 --> 02:05:51.243
Of these, there are 26 grams of total fat,

02:05:51.243 --> 02:05:55.648
42 grams of carbs, of
which 9 grams are sugars,

02:05:55.648 --> 02:05:59.685
and then there are 920
milligrams of sodium.

02:05:59.685 --> 02:06:01.120
What if we made it a combo meal?

02:06:01.120 --> 02:06:03.455
Starting with the fries,
a medium fry in the US

02:06:03.455 --> 02:06:07.326
contains 320 calories,
15 grams of total fat,

02:06:07.326 --> 02:06:09.695
43 grams of carbs, no sugar,

02:06:09.695 --> 02:06:11.664
and 260 milligrams of sodium.

02:06:11.664 --> 02:06:16.335
While a medium fries in
Italy contains 330 calories,

02:06:16.335 --> 02:06:20.873
16 grams of total fat, 41 grams of carbs,

02:06:20.873 --> 02:06:24.109
of which 0.4 grams are sugars,

02:06:24.109 --> 02:06:27.846
and 212 milligrams of sodium.

02:06:27.846 --> 02:06:30.349
And let's add the medium
Coke into the mix.

02:06:30.349 --> 02:06:33.319
It contains 210 calories, no fat,

02:06:33.319 --> 02:06:35.821
56 carbs, 56 of those are sugar,

02:06:35.821 --> 02:06:37.423
and 55 milligrams of sodium.

02:06:37.423 --> 02:06:38.891
That's funny there's salt in the soda.

02:06:38.891 --> 02:06:40.225
We'll do the same here.

02:06:40.225 --> 02:06:43.629
Here's what's inside a
medium Coke in Italy.

02:06:43.629 --> 02:06:46.699
It's 168 calories,

02:06:46.699 --> 02:06:49.034
zero grams of fat,

02:06:49.034 --> 02:06:53.038
42 grams of carbs, 42 grams of sugar,

02:06:53.038 --> 02:06:54.673
so it's all sugar,

02:06:54.673 --> 02:06:56.742
and zero grams of sodium.

02:06:56.742 --> 02:06:59.945
That leaves the total for
the Italian meal at this:

02:06:59.945 --> 02:07:02.247
1,007 calories,

02:07:02.247 --> 02:07:04.049
42 grams of fat,

02:07:04.049 --> 02:07:06.752
125 grams of carbs,

02:07:06.752 --> 02:07:09.555
51.4 grams of sugars,

02:07:09.555 --> 02:07:13.892
and 1,132 milligrams of sodium.

02:07:13.892 --> 02:07:17.229
While in the US, the total
ends up looking like this.

02:07:21.433 --> 02:07:23.736
Let's talk about ingredients now.

02:07:23.736 --> 02:07:26.805
McDonald's Italy shares a
lot of information, actually,

02:07:26.805 --> 02:07:28.841
about its ingredients.

02:07:28.841 --> 02:07:31.977
That's because the majority
of the items on the menu

02:07:31.977 --> 02:07:35.948
are made with 100% Italian products.

02:07:35.948 --> 02:07:38.384
The beef, like the one
that's used in the Big Mac,

02:07:38.384 --> 02:07:42.254
is sourced from over
15,000 different farms

02:07:42.254 --> 02:07:43.889
located in northern Italy

02:07:43.889 --> 02:07:48.627
around the regions of
Lombardy, where we are now,

02:07:48.627 --> 02:07:50.362
the capital of which is Milan,

02:07:50.362 --> 02:07:51.964
and Piedmont.

02:07:51.964 --> 02:07:53.666
There are apples from South Tyrol,

02:07:53.666 --> 02:07:55.267
which is where speck is made,

02:07:55.267 --> 02:07:56.969
just on the border with Austria.

02:07:56.969 --> 02:07:58.637
And just to give some recognition

02:07:58.637 --> 02:08:00.973
to the southern regions,
because I'm from there,

02:08:00.973 --> 02:08:04.043
so no bias at all, we've got some apricots

02:08:04.043 --> 02:08:07.746
from the Vesuvio National
Park, so in Campania,

02:08:07.746 --> 02:08:09.882
and Sicilian oranges.

02:08:09.882 --> 02:08:12.785
And when we talk about
DOP, this red label here,

02:08:12.785 --> 02:08:14.586
it's what you are looking for.

02:08:14.586 --> 02:08:18.724
It's a label that's used for
a lot of traditional products

02:08:18.724 --> 02:08:23.328
around the EU, and that means
that they have to be made

02:08:23.328 --> 02:08:25.898
following certain specific standards,

02:08:25.898 --> 02:08:29.401
most of the time in a very artisanal way.

02:08:29.401 --> 02:08:32.504
That also means that certain
products like Parmesan

02:08:32.504 --> 02:08:35.107
cannot be made outside of a specific area.

02:08:35.107 --> 02:08:37.309
That has to do with the climate.

02:08:37.309 --> 02:08:38.610
So, for example, for cheese,

02:08:38.610 --> 02:08:41.346
the main argument is that
it's a raw-milk cheese,

02:08:41.346 --> 02:08:44.917
and in raw-milk cheeses, you
do taste what the cows eat.

02:08:44.917 --> 02:08:47.453
So obviously, the grass
has a different taste

02:08:47.453 --> 02:08:49.621
depending on where you are in the world.

02:08:49.621 --> 02:08:52.524
But we do have some
American-sourced ingredients

02:08:52.524 --> 02:08:53.659
for McDonald's.

02:08:53.659 --> 02:08:56.962
The potatoes used for our
fries are grown in Washington

02:08:56.962 --> 02:08:59.131
at 100 Circles Farm,

02:08:59.131 --> 02:09:01.300
which is owned by Bill Gates, apparently.

02:09:01.300 --> 02:09:03.702
They grow the potatoes in circles so big

02:09:03.702 --> 02:09:05.738
you can see it from space.

02:09:05.738 --> 02:09:09.108
The potatoes are then cut into
fries at 70 miles per hour,

02:09:09.108 --> 02:09:12.211
which is faster than a cheetah.

02:09:12.211 --> 02:09:14.580
That's the unit of measurement?

02:09:14.580 --> 02:09:16.548
That not-so-secret ingredient
to McDonald's fries

02:09:16.548 --> 02:09:20.285
is beef flavoring, which they've
been doing since the 1950s.

02:09:20.285 --> 02:09:21.787
You want to see if there's
any differences in the US

02:09:21.787 --> 02:09:24.123
and Italy's Big Mac?

02:09:24.123 --> 02:09:26.358
These are all the ingredients
in a Big Mac in the US.

02:09:26.358 --> 02:09:29.795
Altogether, that's 68 ingredients
that make up a Big Mac.

02:09:29.795 --> 02:09:30.696
That's a lot.

02:09:30.696 --> 02:09:32.197
28 of those ingredients are in the bun,

02:09:32.197 --> 02:09:33.832
which is quite a lot for bread.

02:09:33.832 --> 02:09:36.235
The Big Mac sauce also
has a lot of ingredients,

02:09:36.235 --> 02:09:39.138
26 altogether, and it seems like we added

02:09:39.138 --> 02:09:42.174
a lot of relish to ours, which
bulks out the ingredients.

02:09:42.174 --> 02:09:45.344
In Italy, there are 54
ingredients in a Big Mac.

02:09:45.344 --> 02:09:46.311
Here they are.

02:09:48.380 --> 02:09:51.316
We only have 20 ingredients
in the bun, actually,

02:09:51.316 --> 02:09:55.320
because we don't fortify the
flour like you do in the US.

02:09:55.320 --> 02:09:58.423
Our Big Mac sauce has 15 ingredients,

02:09:58.423 --> 02:10:02.928
which is still nine less
than the US Big Mac, Joe.

02:10:02.928 --> 02:10:05.364
Most of the other ingredients are similar,

02:10:05.364 --> 02:10:07.399
but we don't have as many colorings

02:10:07.399 --> 02:10:10.169
or thickeners as you do in the US.

02:10:10.169 --> 02:10:13.105
Some of the ingredients
listed in our US Big Mac sauce

02:10:13.105 --> 02:10:15.974
caught our attention, so we
want to explain what they are.

02:10:15.974 --> 02:10:19.077
First up, propylene glycol alginate

02:10:19.077 --> 02:10:20.879
is derived from brown seaweed

02:10:20.879 --> 02:10:22.748
and is a thickener used in foods

02:10:22.748 --> 02:10:25.184
to give a smooth natural texture.

02:10:25.184 --> 02:10:27.352
Next up we got hydrolyzed corn,

02:10:27.352 --> 02:10:29.621
which is a plant protein
from corn or maize

02:10:29.621 --> 02:10:33.091
and is used as a flavoring
for its umami taste.

02:10:33.091 --> 02:10:36.361
Sodium citrate helps cheese to
melt without becoming greasy.

02:10:39.031 --> 02:10:41.533
I did grow up with McDonald's.

02:10:41.533 --> 02:10:45.170
I definitely celebrated a
couple birthdays over there.

02:10:45.170 --> 02:10:48.407
I had my share of Happy Meals

02:10:48.407 --> 02:10:51.510
with lots of little girly toys.

02:10:51.510 --> 02:10:53.312
It is definitely considered healthier

02:10:53.312 --> 02:10:55.280
than other fast-food chains

02:10:55.280 --> 02:10:58.417
because it has been around
for quite some time,

02:10:58.417 --> 02:10:59.952
but also, obviously,

02:10:59.952 --> 02:11:03.388
because it has Italianized
a lot over the years,

02:11:03.388 --> 02:11:05.324
incorporating things like Parmesan

02:11:05.324 --> 02:11:07.759
or like traditional cheeses and cold cuts.

02:11:07.759 --> 02:11:09.094
So just appealing a little bit more

02:11:09.094 --> 02:11:11.597
to the taste of Italians.

02:11:11.597 --> 02:11:16.401
I have been to stores
in the US and the UK,

02:11:16.401 --> 02:11:19.338
and Italian McDonald's seem, I don't know,

02:11:19.338 --> 02:11:20.839
a little bit fancier.

02:11:20.839 --> 02:11:23.175
It's everywhere and made burgers and fries

02:11:23.175 --> 02:11:26.645
and sodas to go the most
popular meal in the country,

02:11:26.645 --> 02:11:29.014
and then how many places followed suit?

02:11:29.014 --> 02:11:31.650
With Burger King and
Wendy's and all the like.

02:11:31.650 --> 02:11:33.552
And now we got
chicken-sandwich-version ones,

02:11:33.552 --> 02:11:34.386
we got fried chicken.

02:11:34.386 --> 02:11:38.590
McDonald's McDonald's-ified
the entire country

02:11:38.590 --> 02:11:39.858
and the world.

02:11:39.858 --> 02:11:43.595
McDonald's is like Nike or Christianity.

02:11:43.595 --> 02:11:45.430
It's everywhere!

